{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw","id":665862,"title":"How can I take Loyalist Abyssal seriously ? [NSFW]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-15T10:42:54-07:00","id":665862,"title":"How can I take Loyalist Abyssal seriously ? [NSFW]","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/YqcKUoF.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/TLCUh99.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/ZIUrdGa.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <hr /><b>Quiet Star:</b> Sooooo....this is the fearsome Abyssal that I keep hearing about, we don't have these edgy type in the First Age.<br /> <br /> <b>Houshou</b>: No.....nooo, this one is probably just some brain-dead zombie. The Abyssal must be......those two round-looking rock over there !<br /> <br /> <b>Quiet Star: </b>Stand aside girl, let's the elderly handle this....Hey Abyssal, I present an offer that you <i>can't </i>refuse....DO WHAT WE WANT OR WE'LL CRUSH YOUR TESTICLES !<br /> <br /> <b>Houshou: </b>WHAAAAT! How is that negotiation &gt;_&lt;'' And beside, Si-fu, this Abyssal is a Chain-boobs, not Chain-balls =_=''<br /> <br /> <b>Quiet Star: </b>Really, I thought she's a Skeleton-tits. Urgh, these edgy people all looks the same to us old people :/ <hr /></div> <br /> <br /> Not sure if it's because my distaste for &quot;edgy&quot; character like Alucard or something, but I just can't stop laughing whenever I see a loyalist Abyssal, dressing in their silly black costume pretending to be cool with their life-hating ideology and all that, doesn't help that their master are Deathlord, master of fashion-disaster and being overbearingly annoying. It kinda hard for me to take a faction seriously when their signature character include a chain-boobs and a skeleton-tits.....<br /> <br /> I would make me respect the loyalist more if chain-boobs can behead people by spraying milk all over the place and skeleton-tits can unbirth people by dragging people into her behind using skeleton hands and then CRUSH their skull with gigantic force ! Now that what I call ultimate horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 09-15-2015, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:18:25-07:00","id":665918,"title":"","content":"I'd say it can help to look at the contexts in which people have developed a lot of our familiar iconography of death and the gothic. For example, in real life, people build a cathedral out of human bones (including a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Sedlec-Ossuary.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">sweet chandelier</a>) when between war and plague you've got so many people dying that you don't have anywhere else to put them. That's also the context in which you personify death, giving it a tasteful shroud and picturing it as a harvester. Sometimes it helps for horror to have a face, and to even make a friend of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:24:57-07:00","id":665925,"title":"","content":"Just felt the need to say that Yusha Yoshihiko is great. Probably the funniest show I've seen in years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:26:31-07:00","id":665928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw#post665862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Jen's comic)</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/UZtLkcp.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/scale_medium/11120/111201126/4319830-steve-rogers-i-understood-that-reference.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw#post665862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if it's because my distaste for &quot;edgy&quot; character like Alucard or something, but I just can't stop laughing whenever I see a loyalist Abyssal, dressing in their silly black costume pretending to be cool with their life-hating ideology and all that, doesn't help that their master are Deathlord, master of fashion-disaster and being overbearingly annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're confusing Abyssals with the Abyssal fandom. XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:34:17-07:00","id":665937,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, now I know what Totentanz means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:39:00-07:00","id":665940,"title":"","content":"I tend to take them seriously when they kill of people and feed on death.<br /> <br /> And of the splats become very silly if you focus mainly on their iconography. Who would take Sidereals seriously with all that Woo Woo silly stars and destiny stuff they have going on, (I mean, who are you, Russell Grant or Mystic Meg?) while ignoring that they actually do what they say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:44:25-07:00","id":665943,"title":"","content":"I don't know. How WOULD you make a loyalist Abyssal that you can take seriously? What twists would you use to deconstruct and reconstruct the character concept? Whenever I hear something like this, whether it's for loyalist Abyssals in Exalted or Elves in fantasy I just take that as a challenge. <br /> <br /> I mean, just off the top of my head, it would be ridiculously easy to twist the story of Buddha into the story of an Abyssal. Simply have him die under that tree and gain the black exaltation rather than enlightenment and replace the freedom from reincarnation of Nirvana with the cessation of existence of Oblivion. Buddhism even has a term for people who could achieve Nirvana but choose to remain behind in order to help guide all of humanity to that state which in the terms of Exalted would be the role of the Abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:56:44-07:00","id":665948,"title":"","content":"Question are we talking loyal to the Deathlord or loyal to the objective of feeding the world to Oblivion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:04:04-07:00","id":665954,"title":"","content":"Well yea if you use the Exalted Kawai edition versions of the splats they are hard to take seriously.<br /> <br /> But lets keep some perspective, many people dont understand how you can take a game seriously when you sit around and pretend to be a sparkly magic man while rolling dice. To most playing this game at all is silly and impossible to take seriously","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7554-praise-the-sun","name":"Praise the Sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:04:29-07:00","id":665955,"title":"","content":"It helps if you ignore Lady Chainboobs as a character that exists at all! I mean you can hardly call her a character so much as a meme that propagates pffensoce stereotypes about the evil of female sexuality and the ease of objectifying a character such there there is literally nothing interesting written about them at all. <br /> <br /> It also didn't help with gonzo, impossible-to-take-serious necrotech stuff like the pregnant corpses that launch fetus bombs from their vaginas. Seriously, did WW hire 11-year-old boys to come up with that shit?<br /> <br /> In any case, I think Weeping Raiton is interesting as an independent loyalist whose devotion has left her brokenly insane, as is somewhat befitting a direct servant of the Neverborn. <br /> <br /> Fallen Tears Poet is an example of someone whose bad breakup kept them going beyond death <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> more seriously, he shows that not even death can stop human emotions and connections. I think he makes for a good character to relate to ghosts and bring their intense emotions some kind of peace through empathy. <br /> <br /> The surgeon guy always came across as a boring cliche necromancer who spawned a million imitations across games. <br /> <br /> Disciple was somewhat interesting with his duty to his lord conflicting with his human feelings for Harmonious Jade and memories about her. <br /> <br /> Really I think Abyssals suffered from being over-influenced by some of the flatter imagery of Vampire while simultaneously being presented for years with the shallow theme of &quot;kill shit,&quot; as if all Exalted don't do that. And &quot;no, really, kill it *harder*&quot; didn't make that any more interesting. <br /> <br /> I think making Deathlords less boring will go a long way to making loyalist Abyssals less one-note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:05:15-07:00","id":665956,"title":"","content":"That comic... it's like if David Cronenberg and David Lynch collaborated to make a comedy...<br /> <br /> ...Anyway, I think there's a right and a wrong way to depict Loyalist Abyssals. What you have described is definitely the &quot;wrong&quot; way - fixating on &quot;I want to kill everything&quot; as a motivation in and of itself, instead of trying to make a character who might wish to kill everything as a means to some other end. That's the kind of thinking that leads to extreme death-metal outfit stylings and cartoony personalities. Here are some of the &quot;right&quot; ways:<br /> <br /> 1. <i>Sadist</i> - Not recommended for players, but some kinds of people might want to kill the world because they <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qV3PhvCf_Jg\" target=\"_blank\">derive pleasure from murder and destruction</a>. They might actively hate the people around them, or be self-centered enough to believe that is the world does not give them joy, then it should not give joy to anyone else either.<br /> <i>* Suggested style </i>- Be a Hollywood Slasher. Dress up like a known urban legend or monster, or actively try to create the myth of one. Never be seen without some intimidating iconic garb that will prompt everyone to flee in terror - enjoy their fear.<br /> <br /> 2. <i>Nihilistic Saint</i> - Followers of the Bishop might be like this. Saints are people who <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cMZi217RUUY\" target=\"_blank\">genuinely believe that Creation is flawed and awfu</a>l, and they're not entirely wrong to think so. The act of killing is ultimately an act of mercy, as the destruction of the world and the end of the cycle of reincarnation will spare everyone endless lifetimes of torment and suffering.<br /> * <i>Suggested style - </i>Dress to impress. The garb of priests or other significant community figures (e.g. healers, civil leaders) will let you present yourself as a person of the people even while you're murdering them all. Take extra care to keep those clothes clean - gravedirt or blood spatter would ruin your image.<br /> <br /> 3. <i>Supreme Necromancer -</i> Necromancers see the power in death, and would use it to raise themselves up. These are the kinds of people who raise armies of undead and create shadowlands as fiefdoms for themselves because it seems like a good career move.<br /> * <i>Suggested style - </i>You want to be a king of the dead? Dress like one. Grave goods and bling, everywhere - a silver crown on a burial shroud, gold rings on skeletal fingers, and capes - you've got to have capes. Preferably black velvet.<br /> <br /> 4. <i>Lunatic</i> - A lunatic's reasons for destroying the world <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w8WH4uxmiF8\" target=\"_blank\">only make sense to them</a>. Maybe they're psychologically broken, or maybe they have some deeply flawed premises at the heart of their beliefs, or their logic has some holes in it. Whatever the reason, the outcome is the same - you've got somebody whose incoherence is almost as scary as their use of power.<br /> * <i>Suggested style -</i> Anything at all works, but the classic approach is to have an outfit as nonsensical as your ideology. Monster clown trappings and bizarre body modifications are popular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 09-15-2015, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:18:20-07:00","id":665960,"title":"","content":"So, 1. Be A Slasher 2. Be Messiah of Death 3. Be Xykon 4. Be The Joker. Seems about right.<br /> <br /> I would think of the phrase &quot;carpe diem&quot;, &quot;YOLO&quot; or &quot;seize the day&quot; for an loyalist Abyssals actions- the world is going to end, might as well enjoy what you can while you still can. They might join a tournament just for the sake of fighting in it while they still have time, they might conquer a nation just so they can waste all its resources on whatever decadent pleasure they can think of before it runs dry, not caring what damage it will cause in the long run, when you know death will come someday, why bother with long term goals? live in the moment, enjoy it before you die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:27:20-07:00","id":665966,"title":"","content":"Certainly, I can see the point about when all of the skulls and chains and crypts and poison and things are all just hung haphazardly off of a character as an easily digested visual shorthand for being scary or edgy; that's certainly cloddish. But when you have the means to tie it to a sophisticated depiction of or thesis on the macabre, the fascination for the dread and strange beauty in the universal dance, the great equalizer, then you should take it with gusto. After all, would you decry somebody wearing skull makeup for the D\u00eda de Muertos, or the swing of a jazz funeral as difficult to take seriously? I mean, maybe you would, but... you shouldn't. Although I do suppose that it might be difficult to sell certain modern people on the legitimacy of the macabre <i>before</i> we finally get around to some really good antibiotic-resistant microbe, or finally run out of oil/potable water/sustainable food-to-person ratio, or even when our infrastructure simply expands beyond any capacity to sustain it. Well, the ones who are left might appreciate that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:53:05-07:00","id":665999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=665960#post665960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, 1. Be A Slasher 2. Be Messiah of Death 3. Be Xykon 4. Be The Joker. Seems about right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not trying to specifically rag on you, but if this is all they got, I don't think they should be playable, and not much would be lost if they weren't.<br /> <br /> It's equally unpalatable if the whole reason for loyalist Abyssals to exist is for them to go renegade and seek redemption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:04:14-07:00","id":666012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=665955#post665955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helps if you ignore Lady Chainboobs as a character that exists at all!</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I significantly rewrote the Lady of Darkness in personality and motivations for my Exalted game, but I still kept her basic stripperific appearance. Instead of being a hyper-sexualized thing, though, it came off to the players as insanely scary, since she was basically able to shrug off sword-blows and gouts of fire while almost totally naked. I think having spears shatter on her skin while she breathed poison mist into soldiers' faces really killed the sexy for my players too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:09:26-07:00","id":666021,"title":"","content":"And now it would appear that looking into macabre imagery has given me yet another strong context in which those Abyssal Socialize Charms (with slightly modified wording for one or two of them) can work, because good God is there a lot of art depicting a young woman entwined lasciviously with a personification of death. An interesting combination of juxtaposition of imagery, drawing attention to how death comes to even the young and beautiful (especially if they're rock-climbing enthusiasts who follow a whim to climb some random place near to their home with no company or equipment), and taking a bit of the sting out of death by portraying it as a companion, with a bit of erotic subtext. {woof}","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:11:27-07:00","id":666023,"title":"","content":"On the subject of clothing, Creation (just like our world) is a big place so there are lots of thoughts on, references to, and themes based around death, so you don't need to have all the skulls and chains and such all the time. I think it was a bit of a failure on the part of the authors that so many Abyssals came across as such. I mean, in Creation the color most closely associated with death is purple, while black is associated with water, yet Abyssals used the color black far more than purple. That's due to the author's western sensibilities that say that black is the color of death.<br /> <br /> Still, it's not hard to come up with other things. In the last Abyssal game I played in, one of the characters wore a white kimono covered with a cherry blossom design She fought with a magical branch (mechanically a wrackstaff) and when she would kill something, it would instantly leech out the corpse's nutrients and momentarily be covered with cherry blossoms which could quickly fall off and and gently waft to the ground. Cherry blossoms are often associated with the idea of dying young, transience and wistfulness; it's the whole concept of mono no aware.<br /> <br /> My own character was based around the idea of &quot;rainbows&quot; (they're beautiful, short lived, ephemeral and appear only when there is rain and sunshine - not a bad metaphor for life and death ). So this character came from a culture in the East that viewed rainbows as ill omens and symbols of death. His clothing was a riot of different colors and he wore lots of different colored bodypaint as in the culture he came from, when someone died their corpse would be dressed up to resemble a rainbow and then hung from a tree.<br /> <br /> I hope in 3rd edition when the Abyssals book comes out, the writers expand beyond the traditional western-gothic death imagery and maybe grab stuff from other cultures and nations, as well as come up with some things that are unique to Creation. Abyssals and their &quot;all black all skulls all the time&quot; just never felt as cool as they otherwise might have been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-15-2015, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:15:43-07:00","id":666027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=665960#post665960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, 1. Be A Slasher 2. Be Messiah of Death 3. Be Xykon 4. Be The Joker. Seems about right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those were only the first four things I came up with when I asked myself the question - &quot;Why kill everyone?&quot; Certainly, I believe there are more options, and more ways of expressing the ideas I described than to fall back on cliches.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=665960#post665960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think of the phrase &quot;carpe diem&quot;, &quot;YOLO&quot; or &quot;seize the day&quot; for an loyalist Abyssals actions- the world is going to end, might as well enjoy what you can while you still can. They might join a tournament just for the sake of fighting in it while they still have time, they might conquer a nation just so they can waste all its resources on whatever decadent pleasure they can think of before it runs dry, not caring what damage it will cause in the long run, when you know death will come someday, why bother with long term goals? live in the moment, enjoy it before you die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a good follower for Lover Clad in the Raimant of Tears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:16:41-07:00","id":666028,"title":"","content":"That. Is. Awesome. <br /> <br /> Is the rainbow thing something you invented or something you found in an IRL culture?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:21:34-07:00","id":666031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the color most closely associated with death is purple</div> </div> </div> </div> The death of Endings, not of the Underworld. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the author's western sensibilities that say that black is the color of death</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh how I'm looking forward to John making a whole thing out of the Underworld including an intrusion of Western themes and imagery into the setting to emphaisze the unnatural wrongness of the Underworld and its adherents. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssals and their &quot;all black all skulls all the time&quot; just never felt as cool as they otherwise might have been.</div> </div> </div> </div> More colours to be sure, but most of your post has given me what I think is a good, simple way to articulate the difference between Endings and Underworld; the simple difference between funereal and macabre, between what we do to honour passing and to deal with the universal reality (and what was and shall be again the daily reality) of actually dying. (Compare to Liminals, who will probably wind up with transition and resurrection)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:25:56-07:00","id":666034,"title":"","content":"I had heard that in certain stories of Hindu mythology it's said that rainbows occur when important people die. I based the idea off of that and then made up some more stuff for this culture in East.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:55:07-07:00","id":666051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666031#post666031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh how I'm looking forward to John making a whole thing out of the Underworld including an intrusion of Western themes and imagery into the setting to emphaisze the unnatural wrongness of the Underworld and its adherents. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Underworld already has an intrusion of western themes and imagery, largely more than anything else. <br /> <br /> There are plenty of other real-life societies in different parts of the world (Native American mythology, the Ainu, Caribbean Vodoun, Hindu myths, etc) to draw on the idea of &quot;unnatural prolonged existence&quot; or the concept of unnatural beings who are not supposed to exist. I would be rather sad if those continued to be largely ignored in order to keep the Underworld so heavily Gothic-fantasy themed.<br /> <br /> To be honest that is one of the biggest problems and complaints I've seen people voice about the Underworld. It largely comes across as &quot;same-y&quot; and &quot;boring&quot; even though it should be even more diverse than Creation, with ghosts from societies that have been gone for thousands of years living side-by-side with ghosts who died yesterday. It should easily have ten times as many different societies and cultures that Creation does, and yet it definitely never felt that way at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-15-2015, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:03:06-07:00","id":666056,"title":"","content":"I've gotten a lot more mileage out of Deathknights by thinking of them as being part of a functioning social unit rather than a gang of serial killers who only seem to cooperate out of narrative contrivance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:08:43-07:00","id":666060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">there are plenty of other real-life societies (African, South-American, Asian, the Ainu, Indian, Native American, etc) to draw on the idea of &quot;unnatural prolonged existence&quot; or the concept of unnatural beings who are not supposed to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not different enough. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be rather sad if those were largely ignored in order to keep the Underworld so heavily Gothic-fantasy themed.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can see how it's fitting to be jaded about Gothic fantasy considering how much the Gothic is informed by being jaded, but it's still a rich genre with a lot of pedigree. I think it will benefit more from invigoration than dilution in search of a broad appeal. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">with <b>ghosts</b> from societies that have <b>been gone</b> for thousands of years <b><i>living</i></b> side-by-side with <b>ghosts</b> who <b>died</b> yesterday</div> </div> </div> </div> Hehehehe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:11:08-07:00","id":666061,"title":"","content":"What exactly about an entire world's dead side being Gothic themed is appealing to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:31:44-07:00","id":666071,"title":"","content":"Keeping in mind that I'm actually more focused on the term &quot;macabre&quot; rather than Gothic, it's a combination of wanting it to feel more like a dead side than another country, so it needs to be widely infused with reminders and examinations of death, and something to build upon for the whole thing of Abyssals as Death's Lawgivers rather than psychopomps or whatever (or murderers, for that matter; it's something I think can give the Abyssals a strong thesis, and a powerful complement to the Solars, in the face of a Time of Tumult which is likely to start producing a lot of death). I mean, people want to talk about the amazing alternative of associating white with death, as though I didn't link to a picture of a European church fixture made from bones. Oh you can't have skulls, that excludes some of those cultures that have a different kind of bone surrounding their precious head meat. I'm all for the sense of the Underworld containing a variety of memories of cultures that no longer live to emphasize the universality of loss and memory, but still all existing under a pall of their dramas having <i>finished</i>, and that they endure grasping at what they are at the end. Things like &quot;oh they've got actual cultures in there&quot; is how we get people going on about how all you really need to bring somebody back to life is to stick their ghost inside of a meat suit. Macabre themes because they're a powerful real world contemplation on why your ghost <i>would not be you</i>, while also diversifying the Abyssals and the Underworld beyond &quot;death is scary&quot; and &quot;death is murder&quot; (note to self: Abyssal character concept who contemplates how their immortality really translates to having to watch everything else die forever). Even then, hardly just European; you can also get so much from the ancient Egyptian, the Aztec, whatever aspects of the African have wound up finding new expression in the American, Chinese ideas about the residence of the lower soul, all that jazz. I want bones, but dear God do I want people to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Kostnice03.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">do interesting things with them</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:32:27-07:00","id":666072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666060#post666060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not different enough. I can see how it's fitting to be jaded about Gothic fantasy considering how much the Gothic is informed by being jaded, but it's still a rich genre with a lot of pedigree. I think it will benefit more from invigoration than dilution in search of a broad appeal. Hehehehe</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying that the entire Underworld should be based around Gothic-fantasy/western themes and imagery is like saying that all of Creation should be based around Ming Dynasty-fantasy.<br /> <br /> While the Ming Dynasty plays a large role in inspiring Creation, there are still plenty of other places that have been influenced by the Middle East, by Mezo-America, by Nordic fantasy, by Polynesia, etc. Which is <i>good</i>. Creation wouldn't be nearly so interesting if the setting didn't have that sort of diversity.<br /> <br /> Limiting it so that the entire Underworld was solely or almost solely inspired by Gothic fantasy would feel practically stifling. Gothic fantasy is cool and all and it should be a powerful source, but it should be far from the <i>only</i> source, and it shouldn't be so overwhelming of a source that it swallows up everything else. There's a million other equally interesting depictions of ghosts, spooks and the afterlife out there apart from western Gothic imaginings which should be able to serve equally well for inspiring an entire world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-15-2015, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T16:47:12-07:00","id":666174,"title":"","content":"I take Loyalists seriously by reading the first edition STC instead of the subsequent works on deathknights. To be less flippant, think of the soulsteel caste Alchemicals. Souls only become worthy of supporting that variety of Champion by living several lifetimes wherein they place their goals above their lives, and die in the process of fulfilling those goals, or making an attempt with everything that they have. For Abyssals, however, this continues past the point of death, which is kept at bay by their Exaltation, and gives them the means to continue pursuing said goal while they tend to their duties under the (hopefully non-omnicidal in this edition) deathlords. Abyssals are determined beyond the bounds of mortality to change the world with their vision, or to wreak vengeance on a foe that wronged them, or make discoveries of applied scholarship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T16:59:51-07:00","id":666178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Abyssals, however, this continues past the point of death, which is kept at bay by their Exaltation, and gives them the means to continue pursuing said goal while they tend to their duties under the (hopefully non-omnicidal in this edition) deathlords. Abyssals are determined beyond the bounds of mortality to change the world with their vision, or to wreak vengeance on a foe that wronged them, or make discoveries of applied scholarship.</div> </div> </div> </div> Does that not seem like something you could give to just about any Exalted? I mean, isn't it kind of what happened with Yurgen Kaneko? Old man goes out into the snows to die on his own terms, fights off horrible monster to that effect and finds himself rejuvanated to endure past all previously foreseen point of mortality? Even kind of has the end of old life thing, what with self-imposed exile from his own tribe. It's part of why I think Abyssals really need some evocative themes and categories and associations with actual death, as personified in the Deathlords, to give them some distinction and direction, because if &quot;Exalted of killing things even better&quot; is vague then I don't think &quot;Exalted of having not died&quot; does much better. I don't think John's idea of &quot;sacrifice name and destiny in order to become this blasphemous champion&quot; is strictly necessary, just neat enough that I want that as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T19:03:03-07:00","id":666303,"title":"","content":"I am not amused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T19:23:32-07:00","id":666311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=665999#post665999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not trying to specifically rag on you, but if this is all they got, I don't think they should be playable, and not much would be lost if they weren't.<br /> <br /> It's equally unpalatable if the whole reason for loyalist Abyssals to exist is for them to go renegade and seek redemption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important things to be aware of? First, Semicasual, who Raziere is paraphrasing and agreeing with, said these are &quot;some&quot; of the options, not all of them. Second, the guys you're responding to are fellow Exalted players and storytellers: they've got some ideas they like to use for loyalist Abyssals (and some of 'em are really popular playstyles!), but assuming their favorites are all that the developers intend to support is probably incorrect because, as you say, it's a rather limited palette.<br /> <br /> Here's an off the top of my head list of archetypes Abyssals take on in my stories.<br /> <br /> 1. The Slasher: I mostly use these as antagonists, because I'm a Storyteller, but every now and then you get that player who wants to be Belkar or Black Mage, and Abyssals are usually right up his alley. I'm rolling &quot;the Joker&quot; into this one, because let's be honest, there's not much difference. Xykon fits here too: methods differ, but when your goal is Evil for Evil's Sake or Evil for the Lulz, Abyssals are your guys.<br /> <br /> 2. The Messiah of Death: Nihilist buddhist wankery is one of the great joys of Exalted evil. Death as release from the cycle of agonies that is reincarnation can be a noble goal for a certain sort of player, who enjoys moody philosophizing. Sometimes they spend tons of time agonizing about the pain that the world forces them to inflict to free people from still greater suffering and whether it's worth it, sometimes they just want an excuse to murder their enemies. Either way, fun to play in much the same way an introspective Zenith usually is.<br /> <br /> 3. The Necromancer: Lot of genre territory here. Some players want to do the whole &quot;conquering army of the dead&quot; thing, some people want to do the &quot;obsessed with immortality and willing to bathe in the blood of virgins to get it&quot; thing, some people just want to do the traditional wizard &quot;I want to unlock the secrets of the universe&quot; thing with a deathly flavor.<br /> <br /> 4. The Speaker for the Dead: Abyssals as envoys and defenders of the dead can be loyalists and still fulfill a vaguely &quot;good guy&quot; sorta role. Again, there's a lot of different character concepts playable in this area-I've seen Deathknights who are all about forging the souls of slavers and rapists and drug traffickers and abusers of various kinds into soulsteel because &quot;just because Creation has no natural justice in the afterlife doesn't mean I can't deliver justice unto the wicked and grant the righteous a better life in my Kingdom&quot;, I've seen players who are all about trying to connect the living and the dead so that they get along better (Silver Prince and Bishop loyalists are big into Ancestor Cults and can be loyalists and True Believers without wanting to murder their ghost friends' families <i>right now, </i>because it's not like they're not gonna die soon anyway).<br /> <br /> 5. The Usurper: You can be loyal to your Deathlord and still think the Neverborn are asshats and screw those guys. You can be loyal to the Neverborn and still think your Deathlord is an asshat and screw that guy. This sort of player enjoys skullduggery and sneaky politics (and, in my experience, likes to wax poetic about Vampire games past) and wants to take over the Boss' job because they think they can do it better or they think they can have more fun doing it. Just because you're not a renegade doesn't mean you don't get to have the fun of plotting against your Dark Masters! That's the whole point of <i>having</i> Dark Masters in the first place!<br /> <br /> 6. The Obsessive: Deathknights have gothic imagery for a reason, and this archetype is one of those reasons. Sometimes it's fun to go with the over-the-top interpersonal drama and trappings that go with death. Whether you sold out Creation to save your child, or you study Necromancy in the hopes of one day bringing your lost love back to life, or you sacrifice screaming soul after screaming soul to the Mask of Winters because he holds your boyfriend prisoner, or you legitimately fell in love with the Lover one day and you want to go out kill the world and bring its heart to her on a silk pillow, the players who enjoy this sort of character really like playing up the whole &quot;what <i>won't</i> I do for X,&quot; where X is someone important to them, thingy. These players also often enjoy playing Lunars with a difficult Solar Mate, in my experience, and their stories are often tragic (unless the object of their obsession is another PC? For some reason those usually seem to work out better for the main characters). A subtype is the revenge fantasy, which is the same thing inverted: &quot;Am I willing to murder this orphanage to get to the guy who slew my father? LET'S FIND OUT!&quot;<br /> <br /> 7. Baby Death: It's not as common, but I've had players who like the Messiah thing and like the Usurper thing, but take it to a different place. They're the guys and gals who go &quot;Wait, why am I Death's Chosen? I wanna be DEATH.&quot; These are the players who, rather than trying to bring peace and an end to suffering, decide to personally embody Death. They do it for different reasons (sometimes it's because they chafe at being subservient to Deathlords or Neverborn less in touch with the Void than themselves, sometimes they do it because Death is the only enemy worth conquering, sometimes it's because trying to become death is somehow comforting in the face of its inevitability, and in least one case it was because &quot;Fuck Saturn, that's why!&quot;), but they try to embody the principles of Death itself. They anthropomorphize it and try to behave as Death does. Sometimes this ends in becoming a horrible Avatar of the Void whose breath causes stars to fall and blood to cool to ice, sometimes it ends in eating the corpse of a Neverborn (&quot;if they didn't want to get eaten, why'd they give me these fangs?&quot;), sometimes it winds up with taking a more &quot;Death is part of nature and the Void is not, therefore I shall kill this unhealthy Death and fix the natural cycle&quot; approach. The players who like this sort of thing also tend to enjoy playing Infernals who go in for Shintais, and some Sidereal players are drawn to it to for the poetry and the arguments about the nature of Abstract Principles like Death.<br /> <br /> 8. The Outcast: Death is unclean. We burn the dead or hide them away. We bribe them with false gifts of wooden toys and clay statues so they will not come to us asking for our assistance. We try to put them out of our minds. We dread someday becoming like them. Players who want to play Abyssals as outsiders often go for the Appearance 0 mummyfaced guys as opposed to the high-appearance vampire seductresses. They like to look at what it would feel like to be dead when you care about what the living think of you. They like to be ugly, and either tormented by their ugliness or perversely proud of it and fond of shoving it in the faces of the living to say &quot;just wait! Someday you will look just like me!&quot;. These guys like Abyssal medicine, usually, and they're fond of diseases. Sometimes they become champions of the downtrodden, of caste-system untouchables or criminals or the mentally ill or the Jackal tribes. Sometimes they become champions of the dead, like in Number 4. But what they're all about is railing at an unjust world that hates and fears them for being what they are. Sometimes they love the Deathlords or Abyssal allies who accept them, sometimes they resent them, but it's all about social status and bruised pride and bugs crawling out of rotten flesh with these guys. This is a playstyle that's a little harder to pull of with other Exalt types, because &quot;you hate me because I'm <i>gross</i>&quot; is usually more an individual thing than a splat-thing with those, and you don't get magic gross-powers for being a gold or silver colored Anathema. Formerly beautiful seducers and formerly diseased lepers seem about equally common in this group.<br /> <br /> 9. The Inevitable: Some Abyssal players in my experience like the idea that Death is inevitable, and as its champions so is their victory. These guys like Resistance charms. They like doing the thing where you just. Do. Not. Die. Sometimes they like playing Full Moons or Resistance focused Dawns. But Abyssals do it better, because you can beat an Abyssal to death and he claws his way out of the grave several days later and he's back. They're great as NPC antagonists (I absolutely love the Abyssal &quot;play dead&quot; charms!), but some PCs absolutely love being essentially unkillable because they've &quot;got an arrangement&quot; with Death. Some people love to play the tank, and the phrase &quot;But...I <i>killed </i>you!&quot; is music to their ears. Usually the character has some sort of personal goals to which they're very devoted, and this one tends to overlap pretty well with players who are into the Obsessive, because being the Determinator tends to appeal to the same sort of mindset.<br /> <br /> 10. Dead Sexy: There's nothing wrong with wanting to be a vampire ladies' man or a fell succubus of the night. Cliches get to be cliche for a reason, and that reason is usually mass appeal. Abyssals are a good way for the players who want to be dark and dangerous and brooding and sexy to find something in the game that appeals to them. Most of 'em in my experience have more interesting backstories (and often more dramatic tragedy-filled backstories) than our friendly local Lady of Boobs and Skulls, but there's no denying the mass appeal of this archetype. There's always that one player whose answer to the invading army is &quot;I can seduce their general,&quot; who dislikes the Immaculates more for the celibacy and holier-than-thou attitude than for the trying-to-kill-me, who enjoys telling people about what their character is or isn't wearing. I do not wish to denigrate people who want to play social-focused Abyssals who like to get kinky. You can get this sort of fun playing a Serenity or a social-focused Solar or a naughty Lunar, but Abyssals are all about the sexy danger in a way that the others rarely match...and half the fun is playing &quot;who is going to get the other one to betray their friends first&quot; when playing cat and mouse seduction games with seducers of other Exalt types.<br /> <br /> ...the hour grows late, and now I wanna play Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 09-15-2015, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T19:41:05-07:00","id":666324,"title":"","content":"Abyssals, if anything, are the opposite of the Soulsteel caste. Their moment of Exaltation literally requires them to prioritize their own continued existence above absolutely everything else.<br /> <br /> Subject to change in 3e, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T20:08:15-07:00","id":666352,"title":"","content":"I kind of hope it does change: it's a bit restrictive on character concepts.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to the OP, it sounds like the problem is just lack of variety. Black and skulls, again. So, I think the suggestions of a wide variety of cultural views of death that people have made are good.<br /> <br /> Though it depends a little on the STs idea of the trappings of death. Does a hunter bedecked in lionskins count? He's wearing literal dead creatures, but it's hardly a philosophical treatise on the nature of death.<br /> Whereas, say, a funerary priest, or a poet who writes tales of death, or someone whose skin is marked with a wasting disease... well, they're not wearing the trappings of death.<br /> <br /> What about a Jiang Shi? They generally just look Qing officials, but dead. Does dressing like a Qing official count?<br /> <br /> On the philosophy of life-hatred, again, it sounds like the issue is just lack of variety and subtlety.<br /> <br /> I hope (and am somewhat optimistic, though not entirely) in 3rd ed we'll get a lot more variety.<br /> Though, saying that, lots of variety isn't necessarily required: better discussion of the philosophy would also work. I mean, the Bishop's Shining Path is a proper philosophy, based on Buddhist ideas of the bliss of non-existence, but everyone else is just &quot;Grrr I hate life!&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But it also sounds like this is an issue with signature characters. Signature characters, even though they're just 5 random people who are not given much info, often inform the way people see the splat. The Abyssals on the front are pretty generic black-and-skulls. The Day caste is literally just a guy with white hair wearing black clothes. And this is an issue with the Abyssal art generally (and, weirdly, for such generic guys... none of them actually looks like the Grim Reaper!).<br /> There's a lot more variety that could be done: pharoanic death-masks, cloaks of human skin, death-Buddhists, people who actually look like undead monsters (Falling Tears Poet does, but you can't see it because he's masked) who can wear whatever because they still look like undead monsters. Tattoos or face paint to take the form of the undead. Etc. Rather than just black-and-skulls.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though something to say about the black-and-skulls: one of the issues is whether the design makes sense. Take chain-tits. That's not her actual name: we call her chain-tits because she looks so ridiculous. Why does she wear chains across her breasts? Isn't that terribly impractical, and uncomfortable? But no one complains about Falling Tears Poet because it makes sense: he looks like a zombie, so obviously he wears robes and a mask to cover it up.<br /> <br /> So half of the issue could just be solved with better character design rather than an entire rewrite.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T20:21:52-07:00","id":666359,"title":"","content":"I once made a loyalist abyssal that simply viewed the dead as better than the living. After all no mortal can compare to the knowledge, experience, and skill of an ancient ghost. Thus murdering people was doing them a favor, it was granting them the chance to cast off their mortal shell for a more pure form. He does not kill with hate or sadism but with piety and religious fervor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7554-praise-the-sun","name":"Praise the Sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T20:27:50-07:00","id":666375,"title":"","content":"The Maiden of the Mirthless Smile is nearly as bad. When I read her profile for the first time I could <b>feel</b> the edge in the deepest recesses of my soul.<br /> <br /> Honestly this is my problem with both Abyssals and Infernals, they are both either &quot;RAH I'M AN EVIL PIECE OF SHIT FEEEEEEEEEEAR ME&quot; or &quot;I SHALL DEFY MY MASTERS AND BECOME UNHOLY JUSTICE&quot; and...what else?<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh god I just checked and The Lady has a fucking &quot;catfights&quot; Speciality, is this shit serious lmfao<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 09-15-2015, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T20:41:03-07:00","id":666412,"title":"","content":"I don't think Cyan and Sulumor would actually be much different as Solars or Lunars because the situations that have put them at odds with the world have nothing to do with the Yozis. This is really more of an Abyssal problem.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-15-2015, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T20:47:41-07:00","id":666418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666352#post666352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of hope it does change: it's a bit restrictive on character concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it may happen. If they're making deals with the Deathlords instead of the Neverborn, and the Deathlords are no longer one-note DESTROY ALL LIFE.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T21:02:52-07:00","id":666428,"title":"","content":"Yeah, hopefully the Deathlords will have more varied motivations and plans (with some exceptions, they currently differ mainly in their methods and personalities), and so will recruit Deathknights for more varied reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T21:29:38-07:00","id":666446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666375#post666375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">]Honestly this is my problem with both Abyssals and Infernals, they are both either &quot;RAH I'M AN EVIL PIECE OF SHIT FEEEEEEEEEEAR ME&quot; or &quot;I SHALL DEFY MY MASTERS AND BECOME UNHOLY JUSTICE&quot; and...what else?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's waaaaay more common than it has any right to be, though there are exceptions here and there. Two Infernals mentioned in Masters of Jade* were cool individuals.<br /> <br /> One was simply trying to get his mother (and later the fragments of her soul) back from Guild slavers. They've manipulated him for a great while, but he's now biding his time, while privately nearing a possible soul substitute.<br /> <br /> The other wasn't really in focus, but was a Defiler who was intrigued by a dream-eaten former critic of the Guild, and sparked her back to something like herself. The new woman has since finagled her way into a position of the Guild Hierarch's trust, slowly building up a store of secrets until she can wreak her vengeance.<br /> <br /> * Every now and then, I'm reminded of just how cool a book that was. ^_^ I really need to reread it one of these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Breaking up the spacing a bit. 09-16-2015, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T00:03:16-07:00","id":666538,"title":"","content":"Isn't the reason that all DL feel vaguely similar is because how popular Falafel was, so the writer just make every later DLs like him ? Making them less one-noted seems like a bad idea, can you imagine all the uproar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666303#post666303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not amused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah......ah, your post is kinda scary somehow. I think I'll hide under the ground for now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=665955#post665955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also didn't help with gonzo, impossible-to-take-serious necrotech stuff like the pregnant corpses that launch fetus bombs from their vaginas. Seriously, did WW hire 11-year-old boys to come up with that shit?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is this........hentai anime....? Even Exalted can't be that bad &gt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=665955#post665955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The surgeon guy always came across as a boring cliche necromancer who spawned a million imitations across games.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeah, necro-tech focus mad scientist Daybreak is a little overdone these day, isn't it ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666174#post666174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take Loyalists seriously by reading the first edition STC instead of the subsequent works on deathknights.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that DLs was originally hundred of ghostly warlords in the Underworld instead of 13 evil Solars, but Abyssal was different back in 1st Edition too ?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 09-16-2015, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T02:03:33-07:00","id":666630,"title":"","content":"What I suggest is you imagine yourself as a regular, everyday person in Creation. Imagine your quaint village, your nice, happy family, and your quiet, happy job. Imagine your sexy wife/husband. Imagine your side guy/gal that you bang hard as hell when you get a spare moment. Come up with names and appearances for them, just like you were making a PC. Write some short stories. Do a doodle of them or two...<br /> <br /> <br /> Then imagine seeing a Dusk Caste walk over the hill and slaughter everyone in front of your eyes. Imagine the screams, the pain, and the anguish as you watch everything good in your life destroyed. Imagine what it would feel like to see that gothy, Dusk Caste plant four feet of steel in your spouse's skull. Think about what it feels like to be the <i>last person to die</i>.<br /> <br /> When a daiklave is run through your belly, I doubt your last thought would be &quot;Wow, that's an ugly outfit, girl, why you showing off 'dem boobies?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's easy to make light of death, pain, and suffering until you are staring it in the face. Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T03:33:09-07:00","id":666674,"title":"","content":"Errr, so I'm sure I'm not misreading anything; is that an argument of the &quot;it's okay to dress a woman character up in a ridiculous, sexualized outfit, because she's empowered&quot; bit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T03:44:17-07:00","id":666679,"title":"","content":"The argument is that it's fine for a female character to dress up in a ridiculous, sexualized outfit, because if she were killing you, then you wouldn't care about the outfit.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T04:01:48-07:00","id":666684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666538#post666538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making them less one-noted seems like a bad idea, can you imagine all the uproar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can never tell if you're being sarcastic on here but people are pretty excited about this. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666538#post666538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this........hentai anime....? Even Exalted can't be that bad &gt;_&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666538#post666538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that DLs was originally hundred of ghostly warlords in the Underworld instead of 13 evil Solars, but Abyssal was different back in 1st Edition too ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No they were always inside-out Solars. <br /> <br /> I think the difference is that Vampire was more culturally important to WW in 1e and part of the reason some of the splats were written as they were was to entice WoD players to buy into Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T04:30:33-07:00","id":666701,"title":"","content":"I think Totentanz's argument is that you can take a character seriously despite her ridiculous, sexualized outfit because she's capable of killing you.<br /> <br /> The outfit is still ridiculous and sexualized, though, and I don't see a good reason for dressing her like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7103-owill0w","user":"Owill0w","date":". 09-16-2015, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7103-owill0w","name":"Owill0w","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T07:32:29-07:00","id":666963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666538#post666538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that DLs was originally hundred of ghostly warlords in the Underworld instead of 13 evil Solars, but Abyssal was different back in 1st Edition too ?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>For about a year or two. Then the Skeletorizing happened. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4HAUzVJPM2g\" target=\"_blank\">MYAHAHAHAHA!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:02:06-07:00","id":666984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666538#post666538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the reason that all DL feel vaguely similar is because how popular Falafel was, so the writer just make every later DLs like him ? Making them less one-noted seems like a bad idea, can you imagine all the uproar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think he got that popular until his statting in 1E Alchemicals, which was near the end of that edition. The &quot;poster boy&quot; for DLs had always been the Mask of Winters, who was statted in the core and has always beenthe most visibly active Deathlord. And, yeah, probably the most &quot;Skeletor-like&quot;, being a devious schemer. FaFL is the straight-up, lead from the front &quot;Warlord-type&quot;. <br /> <br /> 2E switched a couple of things around, like making Eye and Seven Despairs more incompetent, while also making The Bishop more competent; but otherwise, it didn't change anyone *that* much, and they're not that alike: Bishop is the religious prophet, Silver Prince is the diplomatic leader, Eye is the mad scientist, Lover is the seductress, Princess is the ingenue, Dowager is the huntress/monster/witch, Walker is...really the most boring to me, and most in need of an overhaul.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah......ah, your post is kinda scary somehow. I think I'll hide under the ground for now. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm...not sure what he's unamused by, either!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Is this........hentai anime....? Even Exalted can't be that bad &gt;_&lt; </div> </div> </div>Context helps. Remember that, by this point, Exalted was still trailing influences from the OWoD, and many people *expected and wanted* to see that kind of extreme splatterpunk horror in the line. Only recently, as attitudes have shifted more away from that, have people begun complaining about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeeah, necro-tech focus mad scientist Daybreak is a little overdone these day, isn't it ? </div> </div> </div>True, there was a thread not long ago where we tried to come up with some new and different Daybreak concepts. Hopefully the official canon will, too!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I know that DLs was originally hundred of ghostly warlords in the Underworld instead of 13 evil Solars, but Abyssal was different back in 1st Edition too ?<br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div>No. And is THAT what folks are saying, now?! There have always been 13 DLs, who were the ghosts of Solars, that was always the plan, even before it was actually printed in Abyssals 1E. Where do these memes keep coming from?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:07:28-07:00","id":666995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Owill0w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666701#post666701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Totentanz's argument is that you can take a character seriously despite her ridiculous, sexualized outfit because she's capable of killing you.<br /> <br /> The outfit is still ridiculous and sexualized, though, and I don't see a good reason for dressing her like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when do people need a reason to express sexuality in ridiculous ways? Is it just the gender of the character in question, drawing out notions of prudishness and Victorian sensibilities? Would it help if there was some bara-Abyssal with literally nothing but eyeshadow and a kilt made of shrunken heads and belts all Lulu-from-FFX style as a counterbalance, or would that just make things worse?<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say, logic isn't necessarily a standard to judge costume design, especailly in people who, for one 'reason' or another, serve the end of existence, faithfully or begrudgingly. Maybe those skulls shoot lasers or something. Maybe she's making a mockery of her former life as a prostitute (see Scroll of Exalts) by dressing in over-the-top chain tops.Maybe she's got a wool or cotton allergy. Or maybe, while people are distracted by how that can't actually be something normal people wear, she's siren-screaming your flesh off its bones (Distraction Bonus?).<br /> <br /> (though I do admit the treatment of miscarriage and childbirth as subjects via the juxtaposition of the zombie tike launchers does come off as... garish. But that's a personal aesthetic taste; you know some Deathlord or Labyrinth-hekacthonitire probably has those things crawling about just to mess with ghosts and would-be heroes, I'm just not using them as a GM).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 09-16-2015, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:18:31-07:00","id":667000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666995#post666995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since when do people need a reason to express sexuality in ridiculous ways? Is it just the gender of the character in question, drawing out notions of prudishness and Victorian sensibilities? Would it help if there was some bara-Abyssal with literally nothing but eyeshadow and a kilt made of shrunken heads and belts all Lulu-from-FFX style as a counterbalance, or would that just make things worse?<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say, logic isn't necessarily a standard to judge costume design, especailly in people who, for one 'reason' or another, serve the end of existence, faithfully or begrudgingly. Maybe those skulls shoot lasers or something. Maybe she's making a mockery of her former life as a prostitute (see Scroll of Exalts) by dressing in over-the-top chain tops.Maybe she's got a wool or cotton allergy. Or maybe, while people are distracted by how that can't actually be something normal people wear, she's siren-screaming your flesh off its bones (Distraction Bonus?).</div> </div> </div> </div>you know for some reason that idea about a skull kilt kinda gave me the idea of giving someone either a kilt or a skirt made out of finger bones with skulls as a belt... i may just have to rework one of the characters in my comic to have that now... depending on how annoying it is to draw, thanks.<br /> <br /> also I agree (i assume) with what your saying there, to me a character can wear anything or nothing as long as it FITS with said characters &quot;Theme&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:22:49-07:00","id":667002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666995#post666995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since when do people need a reason to express sexuality in ridiculous ways? Is it just the gender of the character in question, drawing out notions of prudishness and Victorian sensibilities? Would it help if there was some bara-Abyssal with literally nothing but eyeshadow and a kilt made of shrunken heads and belts all Lulu-from-FFX style as a counterbalance, or would that just make things worse?</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's any prudishness factoring into the LoD's background and character design, it's the residual ideal that evil always wears less unless they're guys, in which case, PAULDRON TIME! GIANT, HUGE, SPIKED PAULDRONS! YOU'LL BE AT A LOSS FOR HOW THEY CAN TURN THEIR HEADS OR HAVE PERIPHERAL VISION!<br /> <br /> Which isn't really very sexual. At least, not overtly and in your face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Suffice it to say, logic isn't necessarily a standard to judge costume design, especailly in people who, for one 'reason' or another, serve the end of existence, faithfully or begrudgingly. Maybe those skulls shoot lasers or something. </div> </div> </div>And that requires her to be naked because...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe she's making a mockery of her former life as a prostitute (see Scroll of Exalts) by dressing in over-the-top chain tops. </div> </div> </div>You can't effectively mock something that's already down in the lowest status bracket. That's called punching down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe she's got a wool or cotton allergy. </div> </div> </div>Possible, but doesn't rule out other substances, and at the point where you would rule all of those out, it kind of feels contrived.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or maybe, while people are distracted by how that can't actually be something normal people wear, she's siren-screaming your flesh off its bones (Distraction Bonus?). </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://bikiniarmorbattledamage.tumblr.com/post/78944172315/female-armor-rhetoric-bingo\" target=\"_blank\">A two in one for rhetoric bingo!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:27:11-07:00","id":667007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666984#post666984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm...not sure what he's unamused by, either!</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be mistaken, but I think hippokrene's third-person pronoun of choice is &quot;she.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No. And is THAT what folks are saying, now?! There have always been 13 DLs, who were the ghosts of Solars, that was always the plan, even before it was actually printed in Abyssals 1E. Where do these memes keep coming from?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>To my understanding, it's not a meme. Waaaaaaaay back when, there was indeed a mention of it somewhere. Possibly in the same time and place that 400 Lunars were mentioned and Chosen of Endings used orange instead of violet. I wanna say... 1e ST guide...? Doesn't necessarily mean it wasn't written in error, mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 09-16-2015, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:33:51-07:00","id":667018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666995#post666995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just the gender of the character in question, drawing out notions of prudishness and Victorian sensibilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>oh come on<br /> <br /> no<br /> <br /> no that is not the issue at all","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 09-16-2015, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:48:07-07:00","id":667067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666538#post666538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this........hentai anime....? Even Exalted can't be that bad &gt;_&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, sadly, it can and has. See also: Lilun.<br /> Not that I'm opposed to body horror in the Underworld or Malfeas... but horror can be tasteful, without the sexual objectification for stupid shock value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:51:57-07:00","id":667070,"title":"","content":"Yeah, let's not confuse disinterest in juvenile fantasies with prudishness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:59:41-07:00","id":667077,"title":"","content":"I'm not really familiar with the topic of Bikini Witch, but are &quot;In-setting&quot; reasons a good excuse for the existence of sexualized female designs or silly gonzo stuffs ? Things like &quot;she don't wear cloth since she has Resistance charms&quot; or &quot;The Neverborn are evil, so it makes sense that they will create pregnant fetus bazooka&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:13:48-07:00","id":667095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666995#post666995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe she's making a mockery of her former life as a prostitute (see Scroll of Exalts) by dressing in over-the-top chain tops.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're using the Scroll of Exalts to justify design elements then you've hit a dead end because it rejects everything about her previously established characterisation in favour of saying she\u2019s a dumb prostitute trying to act smart, her name is Rose Petals Parted ffs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:15:11-07:00","id":667100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667077#post667077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really familiar with the topic of Bikini Witch, but are &quot;In-setting&quot; reasons a good excuse for the existence of sexualized female designs or silly gonzo stuffs ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not usually. The metatext of the writing usually shows right through, especially if it's a cliche that's being repeated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Things like &quot;she don't wear cloth since she has Resistance charms&quot; or &quot;The Neverborn are evil, so it makes sense that they will create pregnant fetus bazooka&quot;. </div> </div> </div>The former needs more to it. Basphomy in Verdegris isn't just constantly unclothed because her skin has been permanently changed to be stronger than most forms of armor, but also because Infernals are meant to appear extremely self-indulgent (more work is also probably necessary, but that's a start). The latter, however, is going into 40K territory, and 40K is self-mocking cliche. This is typically something you want to avoid. In general, the more cliche something is, the more the metatext behind it stands out, like Quiet in MGS5. She's photosynthetic? Well, if The End is anything to go by*, that's no reason for her to be half-naked all the time, so the actual reason that she is half naked all the time is pretty obviously not that she's photosynthetic.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*And basic autotrophic biology, but I kind of doubt that's going to enter into it.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:19:39-07:00","id":667107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667077#post667077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really familiar with the topic of Bikini Witch, but are &quot;In-setting&quot; reasons a good excuse for the existence of sexualized female designs ? Thing like &quot;she don't wear cloth since she has Resistance charms&quot; or &quot;The Neverborn are evil, so it makes sense that they will create pregnant fetus bazooka&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>no comment on the fetus bazooka (i just pretend it launches them out it's throat). having resistance charms is not really a in character reason to me. To me an acceptable in character reason for a female abyssal to be naked or more or less wear something akin to what lady of darkness wears would be if for example:<br /> Let's say that the character in question was a prostitute or something and then runs into a mortal serial killer. After &quot;conducting business&quot; the character has her chest slashed open by the serial killer.<br /> As her life ebbs away she gets offered the black exaltion, she accepts and deals out a good old fashion dose of karma on her killer. now her shtick is that she looks like a beautiful naked woman that more or less uses her looks to lure people out and when they get close (aka when they touch her) TADAH her old chest wound opens up and her ribs fly out like teeth brutally eviscerating the victim whilst she's laughing manically.<br /> After this she looks just like she did before she was touched (albeit covered in blood and gore) with a satisfied smile on her face. Not the best character i know but i did make it up on the fly, but that's too me a acceptable reason for a female character to wander around naked or pretty much naked...<br /> <br /> A bit more silly reason that works on any character would plain and simply be that said character is a nudist. Though if that's your reason well. It's your choice as the maker of said character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:26:08-07:00","id":667113,"title":"","content":"I like the Lover Clad in the Raiment of Tears, a Deathlord who is also a sexy necromancer queen that seduces those heroes who confront her in her castle of frozen blood with the unearthly delights of death, ensnaring them and slowly converting them into hollow eyed copies of herself. I think it's a great take on the sorcerer queen that Conan is pitted against on a lot of his covers. It also fits a modern vision of the sexy vampire, which can be fun to play.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a player looking at that and making a character that is pretty much &quot;Baby Lover Clad in the Raiment of Tears&quot;. It's cool, it's right in the middle of the Abyssal design space and I think it's a crying shame that people who are playing what amounts to &quot;Baby First and Forsaken Lion&quot; (the Dusk in superheavy plate, leading an army of the dead) and &quot;Baby Mask of Winters&quot; (Daybreak who focuses on animating bigger and bigger undead horrors) sneer at me because the example iconic Midnight was a prostitute named &quot;Rose Petals Parted&quot; before her death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:27:38-07:00","id":667115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667007#post667007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be mistaken, but I think hippokrene's third-person pronoun of choice is &quot;she.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> To my understanding, it's not a meme. Waaaaaaaay back when, there was indeed a mention of it somewhere. Possibly in the same time and place that 400 Lunars were mentioned and Chosen of Endings used orange instead of violet. I wanna say... 1e ST guide...? Doesn't necessarily mean it wasn't written in error, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e core: &quot;The Deathlords fight amongst themselves incessantly, constantly warring to advance themselves and their plans or for the sake of ego or simply for the love of strife. Though they command great forces, they have no common center. Each wishes to lash out at the world around her in her own personal fashion to recompense it for her death. The result is 100 little kingdoms of bone and steel and not a military juggernaut whose sole purpose is to crush the living and reunite all things across the Shroud.&quot; (p. 76)<br /> <br /> 1e Storyteller's Companion: &quot;Where there is the Blessed Isle in the living world, there is an island surrounded by a thousand petty citadels rising from a vast, still sea of death. The citadels are ruled by Deathlords and inhabited by the spirits of the departed.&quot; (pp. 42-43)<br /> <br /> There's no mention of how many Deathlords there are, or are supposed to be, across the 1e core, the Making of Exalted book, and the Storyteller's Companion. Could be the 1e team mentioned it online, but I can't find it in the early books. (However, the intent that the Deathlords were once Solar Exalted is present in the Making of Exalted.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:31:33-07:00","id":667116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666984#post666984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. And is THAT what folks are saying, now?! There have always been 13 DLs, who were the ghosts of Solars, that was always the plan, even before it was actually printed in Abyssals 1E. Where do these memes keep coming from?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That would be from page 76 of the First Edition corebook which talks about hundreds of deathlords and how their primary focus was in warring between one another rather than conquering Creation and the Storyteller's handbook which actually uses the word &quot;thousand&quot; when discussing Deathlords (that's more than thirteen) and that while they do attack the living they spend much more time battling one another.<br /> <br /> After Abyssals this concept was radically changed, primarily due to the fact that suddenly there are only 13 Deathlords most of whom are separated from one another by thousands of miles. Can anyone imagine that the Silver Prince spends most of his time and resources battling, trading and dealing with other Deathlords? It's hard to imagine that that's the case when his rivals are practically on the other side of the world. That entire idea, that the Deathlords were more interested in the Underworld, and that the Underworld was important to them, was basically dropped between the publication of the core book and Abyssals.<br /> <br /> They went from a setup where the Underworld was often locked into warfare between the Deathlords, who spent time attacking and conquering places, to a setting in which the Deathlords had already &quot;won,&quot; had full control over the Underworld, and most of their interest was focused entirely on Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:38:52-07:00","id":667119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667107#post667107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit more silly reason that works on any character would plain and simply be that said character is a nudist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying that the character comes from an environment that accepts social nudity (ideally one based on a real-life culture) is pretty much the best explanation for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:49:36-07:00","id":667124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666995#post666995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since when do people need a reason to express sexuality in ridiculous ways? Is it just the gender of the character in question, drawing out notions of prudishness and Victorian sensibilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that that is exactly the case - the issue with the Lady in Darkness and Bloodstained Robes is that she's a female character who dresses like that. I mean, we don't usually see similar complaints about characters like Panther or Cearr, or other male characters that wander around shirtless.<br /> <br /> I can't help but imagine that if the Lady in Darkness were the Man in Darkness, and other than being a man was the exact same character and he wore a long skirt-robe and was nude from the waist up in order to show off his hot bishie-body, nobody would be complaining about his sense of fashion, just like nobody complains about any of the other half-naked male characters that are so common in Exalted. <br /> <br /> I think the primary people have is that the Lady in Darkness is a female and that many feel that the gameline shouldn't be overly sexualizing female characters, or that the gameline is being juvenile when it sexualizes female characters, though I haven't seen too many complaints about the sexualization of male characters. <br /> <br /> What I find interesting is the fact that so many people dismiss her by calling her &quot;Chain-Tits&quot; instead of using her name. That seems rather telling that there's at least a bit of sexism going on in the way we (as a general society) view nudity in female characters vs nudity in male characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:54:40-07:00","id":667128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667119#post667119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying that the character comes from an environment that accepts social nudity (ideally one based on a real-life culture) is pretty much the best explanation for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>very true did not think of that. thank you for pointing it out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:01:04-07:00","id":667135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666538#post666538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that DLs was originally hundred of ghostly warlords in the Underworld instead of 13 evil Solars, but Abyssal was different back in 1st Edition too ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The old Storyteller's Companion doesn't really talk (or <i>know</i>) about the murder-the-world thing. Hell, it specifies that they're <i>not</i> doing that.<br /> <br /> Instead, it plays up their nature as beautiful vampires, emphasizing their passion, their joy, and the beauty they see in death and eternity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:05:42-07:00","id":667139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667002#post667002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://bikiniarmorbattledamage.tumblr.com/post/78944172315/female-armor-rhetoric-bingo\" target=\"_blank\">A two in one for rhetoric bingo!</a></div> </div> </div> </div>... and other accumulated points from Lioness, root, Jen, etc.<br /> <br /> Wow. these are all neat points. Especially the fact about using Scroll of Exalts. I'll have to make a deeper look into the character's depiction across the other books as well; I shouldn't over-simplify the character just on one interpretation and one costume choice (which was kinda the whole point of it). And I'l be sure to save that bingo card, both for the entertainment value of seeing how many of them I see in my previous posts, to avoid making cliche arguments in the future of this thread (should i continue to pursue this), and to figure out a more rational explanation of not only chain-tops with skulls, but also the skull-belt and fingerbone kilt Xanroth claims I've accidentally inspired (because kilts, people, need defending).<br /> <br /> Maybe I should focus more on a defense of gothic imagery, or move to a demonstration of how begrudging Loyalists, torn between supernatural duty and personal desires, make for great playing experiences?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 09-16-2015, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:05:57-07:00","id":667140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667115#post667115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1e core: &quot;The Deathlords fight amongst themselves incessantly, constantly warring to advance themselves and their plans or for the sake of ego or simply for the love of strife. Though they command great forces, they have no common center. Each wishes to lash out at the world around her in her own personal fashion to recompense it for her death. The result is 100 little kingdoms of bone and steel and not a military juggernaut whose sole purpose is to crush the living and reunite all things across the Shroud.&quot; (p. 76)<br /> <br /> 1e Storyteller's Companion: &quot;Where there is the Blessed Isle in the living world, there is an island surrounded by a thousand petty citadels rising from a vast, still sea of death. The citadels are ruled by Deathlords and inhabited by the spirits of the departed.&quot; (pp. 42-43)</div> </div> </div> </div>THAT'S how people are interpreting those passages?...Actually, I guess you *could* read it that way, now that I think about it. But ever hear of proxy wars? Or emperors, who, by definition, are rulers who rule more than one kingdom? That's what's being described there, a handful of DLs who are using the various kingdoms of the dead to war against each other. One person can rule many kingdoms and own many citadels, there being a hundred of one and a thousand of the other does not automatically mean that there can ONLY be one DL in control of each.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's no mention of how many Deathlords there are, or are supposed to be, across the 1e core, the Making of Exalted book, and the Storyteller's Companion. Could be the 1e team mentioned it online, but I can't find it in the early books. (However, the intent that the Deathlords were once Solar Exalted is present in the Making of Exalted.) </div> </div> </div>Given that the DLs were inspired by Wraith's Deathlords, who were even fewer (10-12, maybe? Maybe it was 13...), I think it's likely that the number was always intended to be around what was eventually printed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 09-16-2015, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:11:12-07:00","id":667164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667116#post667116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That entire idea, that the Deathlords were more interested in the Underworld, and that the Underworld was important to them, was basically dropped between the publication of the core book and Abyssals.<br /> <br /> They went from a setup where the Underworld was often locked into warfare between the Deathlords, who spent time attacking and conquering places, to a setting in which the Deathlords had already &quot;won,&quot; had full control over the Underworld, and most of their interest was focused entirely on Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it went from a Hot War to a Cold War situation, that's a clear change, I'll admit. Would the setting be improved by sticking to the original version? Hard to say, since it all depends on the execution. The devs have said that they were making the Underworld more exciting, but I don't recall them mentioning bringing back open warfare among the DLs as a way of doing it...<br /> <br /> Some other interesting changes: The STC's Dusk Caste anima power is them *singing*, which is so eerie it demoralizes anyone attacking them for a -2 penalty; there's some mention of Abyssal exaltation coming directly from a Deathlord, in such a way that it actually can *weaken* them, and that it might even occur without the DL intending to do it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:17:15-07:00","id":667175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667135#post667135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The old Storyteller's Companion doesn't really talk (or <i>know</i>) about the murder-the-world thing. Hell, it specifies that they're <i>not</i> doing that.<br /> <br /> Instead, it plays up their nature as beautiful vampires, emphasizing their passion, their joy, and the beauty they see in death and eternity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not even when it talks about how the Great Contagion was only a taste of things to come? Well, it doesn't have to go into it, as it's all right there inthe corebook, anyway. Read the lexicon definition of the Malfeans and Prince of Shadows' chapter fiction if you don't believe me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:18:38-07:00","id":667177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667124#post667124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I find interesting is the fact that so many people dismiss her by calling her &quot;Chain-Tits&quot; instead of using her name. That seems rather telling that there's at least a bit of sexism going on in the way we (as a general society) view nudity in female characters vs nudity in male characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a problem. I blame her Scroll of Exalts write-up on the fact that she was dismissed as &quot;chain tits&quot; by the fanbase years beforehand, it's interesting to contrast that with Gail Simone's rebooting of Red Sonja while keeping the iconic chainmail bikini. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:24:51-07:00","id":667182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667115#post667115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snip*</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the citations and correction. I can see how that jives with there having always been 13 Deathlords,<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I would most likely have concluded, &quot;there are hundreds of Deathlords,&quot; from seeing those two quotes in a vacuum, but that's neither here nor there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:25:24-07:00","id":667184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667107#post667107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> having resistance charms is not really a in character reason to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought over about what i said here and wish to correct myself. &quot;Having resistance charms is not really a in character reason for me to have said character nude (UNLESS IT REALLY FITS THEM)&quot; what i mean by this is if the core concept for your female dusk caste(for example) is to be the ferocious naked warrior that lets her foes cut her flesh to ribbons (alternativly having their weapons break on her skin) since that's not going to stop her, her clothes is the blood of the foe, then fine resistance charms is an acceptable in character reason in that case.<br /> If your diplomat whose core concept is that of a diplomat does the same thing then i'm going to say no.<br /> Your concept is that of a diplomat, unless the place you represent doesn't wear clothes then you will wear the damn clothes no matter how many spear will break of your bobbies!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:30:47-07:00","id":667188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667124#post667124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that that is exactly the case - the issue with the Lady in Darkness and Bloodstained Robes is that she's a female character who dresses like that. I mean, we don't usually see similar complaints about characters like Panther or Cearr, or other male characters that wander around shirtless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find Cearr hot, but I'm quite sure that female and us gay aren't the target demographic when he was created, unlike the Lady. Plus, I don't think just because a male character going around shirtless or have big muscles doesn't mean that he's being sexualized, I feel like it is more about poses, the activity that he has in the artwork, what part of the body does the camera focus in and their facial expressions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Though I kinda want to know what kind of sexualized male character do the lady want to appear in artworks, since I have always wondered whether woman tends to favor the bishie, the hunk or the bara.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:34:40-07:00","id":667192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667124#post667124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">though I haven't seen too many complaints about the sexualization of male characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because sexism against men isn't a thing and having &quot;sexy&quot; male bodies doesn't risk alienating men from getting into the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667124#post667124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we don't usually see similar complaints about characters like Panther or Cearr, or other male characters that wander around shirtless.</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't cultural baggage that says sexualized/shirtless men are inherently immoral or evil. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667124#post667124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I find interesting is the fact that so many people dismiss her by calling her &quot;Chain-Tits&quot; instead of using her name. That seems rather telling that there's at least a bit of sexism going on in the way we (as a general society) view nudity in female characters vs nudity in male characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably a fair thing to analyze. I know that when I have called her &quot;Lady Chainboobs&quot; it's to dismiss the existence of the &quot;character,&quot; if you can call it that, as nothing but a juvenile insertion to attract teenage boys with no actual thought put into it. She unfortunately adds nothing to the setting. I have problems with depictions of sulumor and Madame vert in art but they at least kind of have characterization written down somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 09-16-2015, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:44:22-07:00","id":667195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667188#post667188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find Cearr hot, but I'm quite sure that female and us gay aren't the target demographic when he was created, unlike the Lady. Plus, I don't think just because a male character going around shirtless or have big muscles doesn't mean that he's being sexualized, I feel like it is more about poses, the activity that he has in the artwork, what part of the body does the camera focus in and their facial expressions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Though I kinda want to know what kind of sexualized male character do the lady want to appear in artworks, since I have always wondered whether woman tends to favor the bishie, the hunk or the bara.</div> </div> </div> </div>to be honest it may have just been that the look that lady got was just how the artist interpreted his/her instructions on how lady was supposed to look. I mean if the instruction more or less can be shredded down to: Seductress, deceiver, former prostitute, jealous of anyone that get's more eye's on her than she is, chains and skulls. Well i guess that you would probably end up with lady of darkness. Her current design does more or less fill all of those categories...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:44:46-07:00","id":667196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667140#post667140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THAT'S how people are interpreting those passages?...Actually, I guess you *could* read it that way, now that I think about it. But ever hear of proxy wars? Or emperors, who, by definition, ae rulers who rule more than one kingdom? That's what's being described there, a handful of DLs who are using the various kingdoms of the dead to war against each other. One person can rule many kingdoms and own many citadels, there being a hundred of one and a thousand of the other does not automatically mean that there can ONLY be one DL in control of each.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, there's nothing in those early quotes to suggest a low number of Deathlords. Early Exalted players could have gone with hundreds of Deathlords, and there would have been nothing to say they were wrong at that point. Only after 1e Abyssals came out did that view become invalidated.<br /> <br /> We can see why people read them as indicating there were lots of Deathlords, when that was their first exposure to them and no specific numbers were given elsewhere. That we can also read it as supporting there being only 13 Deathlords is a result of later canon assuming primacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given that the DLs were inspired by Wraith's Deathlords, who were even fewer (10-12, maybe? Maybe it was 13...), I think it's likely that the number was always intended to be around what was eventually printed. </div> </div> </div>Wraith had eight Deathlords, one for each of the Legions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:46:47-07:00","id":667199,"title":"","content":"It's so frustrating to have to make the same arguments over and over and over again... still, it's the world we line in, and one must soldier on. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the issue with the Lady in Darkness and Bloodstained Robes is that she's a female character who dresses like that. I mean, we don't usually see similar complaints about characters like Panther or Cearr, or other male characters that wander around shirtless.</div> </div> </div> </div> The issue is that a disproportionately large number of female characters are depicted like that for the sake of titillation. There are people who like Panther and Cearr, but those characters are not drawn to titillate. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen too many complaints about the sexualization of male characters</div> </div> </div> </div> It's almost as if the sexualization of man, apart from being pretty damn uncommon and requiring a bit more than just not wearing a shirt, is something that doesn't exist within a wider context of sexualization of women being used to limit and marginalize their portrayals in fiction, and even some approaches to them as actual people. Like the difference between the occasional male football player doing a photo shoot and the president of FIFA suggesting that uniforms for women players should be made smaller and tighter. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I find interesting is the fact that so many people dismiss her by calling her &quot;Chain-Tits&quot; instead of using her name. That seems rather telling that there's at least a bit of sexism going on in the way we (as a general society) view nudity in female characters vs nudity in male characters.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's at least partially an indication of how so much of the artwork and written background has failed to sell people on the credibility of the character, but I'll certainly grant that there can be a tendency for some internalized misogyny to be expressed in criticism of problematic characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:53:40-07:00","id":667230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667164#post667164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it went from a Hot War to a Cold War situation, that's a clear change, I'll admit. Would the setting be improved by sticking to the original version? Hard to say, since it all depends on the execution. The devs have said that they were making the Underworld more exciting, but I don't recall them mentioning bringing back open warfare among the DLs as a way of doing it...</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the biggest problems the Underworld faced is that it never felt like it mattered. The Deathlords conquered it, they controlled it, they won.<br /> <br /> So if you were playing an anti-Deathlord character, the Underworld was enemy territory. If you went there, you were taking a huge risk because it was under the control of your enemies. So your best bet was to avoid it, and instead, to try and stop them from conquering Creation (since that was their main focus anyway).<br /> <br /> If you were playing a pro-Deathlord character, then the Underworld didn't matter. Your master already conquered it. He or she already controlled it. You had little reason to deal with the Underworld because it was already your territory. Instead, your major focus was on Creation because that place was the heart of your master's plans and not somewhere under his or her control.<br /> <br /> Essentially with the current setup, there aren't any strong reasons for characters who are working against the Deathlords or for the Deathlords to really go and muck around in the Underworld. You'll spend much more time dealing with Creation because that's where the Deathlord's focus is.<br /> <br /> If you have an Underworld in which the Deathlords are in the process of conquering it, or in which Underworld trade routes are incredibly important, then that creates more interesting opportunities for players to engage with. Your character can go join an independent kingdom and help them fight off the Deathlord. Or your can play two Deathlords off against one another. Or you can cut trade routes and cause all manner or havoc for that Deathlord.<br /> <br /> And likewise, if you're playing a character who is working with the Deathlord, then just turn those above examples around and your character suddenly has reasons to deal with the Underworld.<br /> <br /> I agree though that having open battles between the Deathlords however is largely impossible when there are only 13 Deathlords as opposed to the hundreds that were originally envision. The distances between the 13 Deathlords are far to extreme for any kind of military action to be common. Even the closest Deathlords, the Mask of Winters and the Walker in Darkness are separated by a pretty long distance, and for many like the First and Forsaken Lion, the Silver Prince or the Dowager, they're simply too far away from other Deathlords to make open conflict anything other than a very, very, very rare exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:55:36-07:00","id":667260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667188#post667188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find Cearr hot, but I'm quite sure that female and us gay aren't the target demographic when he was created, unlike the Lady. Plus, I don't think just because a male character going around shirtless or have big muscles doesn't mean that he's being sexualized, I feel like it is more about poses, the activity that he has in the artwork, what part of the body does the camera focus in and their facial expressions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Though I kinda want to know what kind of sexualized male character do the lady want to appear in artworks, since I have always wondered whether woman tends to favor the bishie, the hunk or the bara.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is an interesting question, maybe one deserving its own thread: What do those who are attracted to males find arousing and look for in art? This is something that's been an increasing concern in superhero comics as the creators have tried to cater to more diverse audiences, as well...<br /> <br /> Are the Hulk and Namor considered &quot;hot&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:05:07-07:00","id":667268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667196#post667196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, there's nothing in those early quotes to suggest a low number of Deathlords. Early Exalted players could have gone with hundreds of Deathlords, and there would have been nothing to say they were wrong at that point. Only after 1e Abyssals came out did that view become invalidated.<br /> <br /> We can see why people read them as indicating there were lots of Deathlords, when that was their first exposure to them and no specific numbers were given elsewhere. That we can also read it as supporting there being only 13 Deathlords is a result of later canon assuming primacy.<br /> <br /> Wraith had eight Deathlords, one for each of the Legions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a pretty good point. Perhaps it was my later knowledge of 13 DLs that biased me, or my prior knowledge of Wraith that did the same, but I never assumed high numbers for them. After all, those passages are still perfectly valid, in current canon (except for the citadels, which were never mentioned again). <br /> <br /> So, I would still argue that those who were familiar with the OWoD, and *knew that Exalted was meant and billed as its predecessor*, would naturally assume that these were the same or similar DLs from that game, who were even fewer, and were probably about the same amount.<br /> <br /> Either way, I'll concede that it can validly be read that way, sure. But that's still a far cry from the statement that &quot;it was supposed to be this way&quot;!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:07:05-07:00","id":667271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667230#post667230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the biggest problems the Underworld faced is that it never felt like it mattered. The Deathlords conquered it, they controlled it, they won.<br /> <br /> So if you were playing an anti-Deathlord character, the Underworld was enemy territory. If you went there, you were taking a huge risk because it was under the control of your enemies. So your best bet was to avoid it, and instead, to try and stop them from conquering Creation (since that was their main focus anyway).<br /> <br /> If you were playing a pro-Deathlord character, then the Underworld didn't matter. Your master already conquered it. He or she already controlled it. You had little reason to deal with the Underworld because it was already your territory. Instead, your major focus was on Creation because that place was the heart of your master's plans and not somewhere under his or her control.<br /> <br /> Essentially with the current setup, there aren't any strong reasons for characters who are working against the Deathlords or for the Deathlords to really go and muck around in the Underworld. You'll spend much more time dealing with Creation because that's where the Deathlord's focus is.<br /> <br /> If you have an Underworld in which the Deathlords are in the process of conquering it, or in which Underworld trade routes are incredibly important, then that creates more interesting opportunities for players to engage with. Your character can go join an independent kingdom and help them fight off the Deathlord. Or your can play two Deathlords off against one another. Or you can cut trade routes and cause all manner or havoc for that Deathlord.<br /> <br /> And likewise, if you're playing a character who is working with the Deathlord, then just turn those above examples around and your character suddenly has reasons to deal with the Underworld.<br /> <br /> I agree though that having open battles between the Deathlords however is largely impossible when there are only 13 Deathlords as opposed to the hundreds that were originally envision. The distances between the 13 Deathlords are far to extreme for any kind of military action to be common. Even the closest Deathlords, the Mask of Winters and the Walker in Darkness are separated by a pretty long distance, and for many like the First and Forsaken Lion, the Silver Prince or the Dowager, they're simply too far away from other Deathlords to make open conflict anything other than a very, very, very rare exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>actually, is the distance really that much of a problem for an army of ghosts? I mean they don't really need food right? Or have I missed some part where it says that all ghosts must eat their ghost apples every day or else they get the ghost scurvy and need to go to the hekatonkhire dentist (if i seem snarky with that part i apologize it was not my intention)?<br /> <br /> but yeah the the deathlords that makes most sense for them to have a bigger battle between each other would be the mask and the walker. One reason that could be used as to why the other deathlords aren't going all out conqueror on each others could be that the last great battle (the battle of Stygia where the lion went and made Stygia into his summerhouse.) roused the neverborn. when deathlord fought deathlord in an apocalyptic displays of power and they don't want to do that again. I think the walker and the mask may be too &quot;young&quot; to have been involved in that battle thus they don't know that the neverborn will &quot;spank&quot; any naughty deathlords that wakes them up from their anger nap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:09:07-07:00","id":667272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667230#post667230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially with the current setup, there aren't any strong reasons for characters who are working against the Deathlords or for the Deathlords to really go and muck around in the Underworld. You'll spend much more time dealing with Creation because that's where the Deathlord's focus is.<br /> <br /> If you have an Underworld in which the Deathlords are in the process of conquering it, or in which Underworld trade routes are incredibly important, then that creates more interesting opportunities for players to engage with. Your character can go join an independent kingdom and help them fight off the Deathlord. Or your can play two Deathlords off against one another. Or you can cut trade routes and cause all manner or havoc for that Deathlord.<br /> <br /> And likewise, if you're playing a character who is working with the Deathlord, then just turn those above examples around and your character suddenly has reasons to deal with the Underworld.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna belate for work so don't have time for examples, but...all ofthis is essentially what the Compass Underworld already DID. Seriously, browse through it, it's full of the idea and examples of kingdoms who are in the process of resisting the DLs, who as of this book at least, do NOT control or have conquered everything. So, all of the above is currently doable in canon. <br /> <br /> Really, it'sall there, folks. Just read the book!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:15:05-07:00","id":667275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667272#post667272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gonna belate for work so don't have time for examples, but...all ofthis is essentially what the Compass Underworld already DID. Seriously, browse through it, it's full of the idea and examples of kingdoms who are in the process of resisting the DLs, who as of this book at least, do NOT control or have conquered everything. So, all of the above is currently doable in canon.<br /> <br /> Really, it'sall there, folks. Just read the book!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except that isn't the case at all. The gameline makes it clear that those kingdoms are independent only due to the sufferage of the Deathlords and the fact that if one Deathlord started gobbling up too many of those independent kingdoms, the other Deathlords would step in to stop him. The Deathlords very much are directly in control of the Underworld, they have spies and followers everywhere, and the kingdoms that do exist there are not in any position to be able to stand up and challenge the Deathlords. <br /> <br /> I mean really, which kingdoms are currently at war with a Deathlord? Which kingdoms have successfully beaten back Deathlords?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:26:13-07:00","id":667281,"title":"","content":"Let's be real, an area the size of Creation being outright ruled by 13 hyper-powerful entities who can crush all opposition is like the Halta map borders problem on steroids. Its just too much even if those 13 entities are evil Solar ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:31:26-07:00","id":667295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667077#post667077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really familiar with the topic of Bikini Witch, but are &quot;In-setting&quot; reasons a good excuse for the existence of sexualized female designs or silly gonzo stuffs ? Things like &quot;she don't wear cloth since she has Resistance charms&quot; or &quot;The Neverborn are evil, so it makes sense that they will create pregnant fetus bazooka&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, those don't work. The <i><b>constant</b></i> oversexualization of females in Western fantasy art has no real excuse. Not to mention that <a href=\"http://marinka18.deviantart.com/art/Warriors-381539829\" target=\"_blank\">nudity and even sexuality without sexual objectification and grotesque bodily deformity</a> is actually quite possible, and it's easy to tell the difference. (This has been discussed a lot on the Monday Meeting threads, tho.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667124#post667124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that that is exactly the case - the issue with the Lady in Darkness and Bloodstained Robes is that she's a female character who dresses like that. I mean, we don't usually see similar complaints about characters like Panther or Cearr, or other male characters that wander around shirtless.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.shortpacked.com/2011/comic/book-13/05-the-death-of-snkrs/falseequivalence/\" target=\"_blank\">This is a false equivalence</a>. Those men are not sexually objectified, they are power fantasies for a male audience. They also do not exist in a context of constant discrimination and sexual violence against men.<br /> <br /> There have been attempts at actual male sexualization to try to highlight the problem -- see the Hawkeye Initiative, especially <a href=\"http://thehawkeyeinitiative.com/post/99168881876/jijikero-haha-ive-been-wanting-to-pair\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://thehawkeyeinitiative.com/post/50432219744/special-guest-edition-the-hawkeye-initiative-irl\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. The male equivalent of melon-sized boobs bursting out of skimpy bras, and bared inner thighs, is to have a melon-sized package barely contained in a thong that's too small.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-16-2015, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:33:20-07:00","id":667297,"title":"","content":"Looking back at the first post and recalling some things in illustrations, I feel a need to clarify that the values of the macabre are indeed undermined when they're presented in ways such as &quot;drape chains haphazardly around a naked torso&quot; (as opposed to something that might emphasize a sense of restraint or burden), and skulls used as little nipple adornments. Really, any kind of nipple covering is enough to undermine arguments that the bare-chested woman in question is being treated with an equivalence to men or should just be considered to have a values-neutral instance of being topless, because when you cover up just one part of the breast you're still doing the thing where the exposure of the breast is meant to titillate, with the hidden promise of some secret thing waiting to be uncovered. When you uncover everything but the nipples, you just reinforce the strange contemporary idea of women's breasts as a kind of secondary genitalia, making it both non-equivalent to a bare-chested man and inherently sexualized. One wants to talk about equivalences between and responses to nudity, but none of these characters are ever actually nude, because nudity is the point at which basically all capacity for titillation has been left behind, and it's just a human body. An actually nude Lady of Darkness would be preferable to me than one who has little fetish ornaments, because it would make several of those rhetoric points better. It's in a similar boat to how I've said that a Maiden of the Mirthless Smile wearing something like a ball gown would make the point better than one wearing a college Halloween costume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T12:42:46-07:00","id":667367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667260#post667260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting question, maybe one deserving its own thread: What do those who are attracted to males find arousing and look for in art? This is something that's been an increasing concern in superhero comics as the creators have tried to cater to more diverse audiences, as well...<br /> <br /> Are the Hulk and Namor considered &quot;hot&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://www.themarysue.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/12/falseequivalence-369x550.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Relevant to this discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T12:54:29-07:00","id":667372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667260#post667260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is an interesting question, maybe one deserving its own thread: What do those who are attracted to males find arousing and look for in art? This is something that's been an increasing concern in superhero comics as the creators have tried to cater to more diverse audiences, as well...<br /> <br /> Are the Hulk and Namor considered &quot;hot&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I've noticed over the years is that there isn't as much of a concensus as to what makes a guy Sexy as opposed to girls.<br /> <br /> For example, of the things listed in the comic posted by blackwingedheaven, the only thing listed by the lady in that comic that I point blank agree with is the lean body (I once spent one gaming session (I was in my 20's then) occasionally reminding people when things got stupid that I could have stayed home to watch 42 of what I consider the most perfect body types in the world compete in Olympic Men's Gymnastics rather than putting up with their BS.) The rest... well, kissable lips is open to interpretation, but I find bright pink lips on guys a turn-off. Eyes and cheeks are a bit more neutral, though the eyes in the example drawing are more cute than sexy to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T12:59:27-07:00","id":667374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667297#post667297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking back at the first post and recalling some things in illustrations, I feel a need to clarify that the values of the macabre are indeed undermined when they're presented in ways such as &quot;drape chains haphazardly around a naked torso&quot; (as opposed to something that might emphasize a sense of restraint or burden), and skulls used as little nipple adornments</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to make a post about this a few pages ago but got distracted. How the whole gothic thing is presented makes a huge, huge difference on whether or not it's a silly cartoon character or not. Part of what makes the dark gothic thing work is it's supposed to evoke feelings of sadness and loneliness, but like those feelings the the abyssal/death sort of motif has to be hidden and mysterious and dark. Abyssals shouldn't have bright white and purple bone armor that screams for your attention and to see how many skulls they can put all over it. For me an abyssal should be <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/c9/84/f9/c984f9a65fcbeb0390f1e51c4da203cf.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> guy sitting in <a href=\"http://orig09.deviantart.net/8c7e/f/2007/267/d/b/abandoned_gothic_cathedral_by_i_netgrafx.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> place. The creepiness doesn't come from the carnival of carved skulls everywhere, it comes from all the stuff you don't see. Why is he like that? Is he sad? Weary? Defeated? He could be thinking about all the people he's killed, and how it doesn't matter because they're all dead now, all the sadness he feels right now is something he's saved them from.<br /> <br /> The place too wherever it was it was clearly once a giant place of worship, but now it's dead and abandoned. There's just something about a place of grandeur and life and history and triumph that becomes so sad when it's cold, alone and empty. Or nearly empty. Even if it was filled with ghosts, that could be just as bad. I'm not entirely sure, but I think we all know that feeling of what it's like to be lonely in a crowded room. It's the kind of feeling that you can imagine somebody sitting in for a long time, and maybe actually believing that since everything will turn to dust anyway, that nothing really matters. Especially if everything that was theirs is lost and can never be brought back, except in an echo.<br /> <br /> That's actually one other, small, facet of it, is a kind of sad hope. An abyssal who's lost a lover might find some spark left inside her by sitting on a darkened balcony with his ghost. Knowing that this is the last vestige of her that he can't let go of. Like how some people who lose somebody in their real life keep watching videos, looking at pictures, holding on to any last scrap of them they can find, jealously guarding them. In the Abyssal's case, possible violently. For example a Deathlord might promise to keep his ghost safe and preserved for her, but she must go and kill the Solar exorcist who plans on destroying the Deathlord's shrines. Not a bad story for a loyalist Abyssal.<br /> <br /> The problem is that it's a fundamentally internal and personal experience, so you can't just show everything and fetishize it and expect it to work at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T13:16:06-07:00","id":667380,"title":"","content":"An Abyssal's Trappings of Death should be less this:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://images.popmatters.com/news_art/d/dvd-beetlejuicecompelteseries-500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" bor