pretty nice guy as far as abyssals go, he married his lunar mate after he found her, she helped him to almost reach redemption (and she got pregers to)... then comes his old abyssal mentor who captures them all and drags him before the deathlords he served. they chained and trapped his lunars soul AND exaltion into soulsteel together with the soul of his unborn child. they then made it so that the swords ALWAYS scream out in pain whenever they are swung, he can not use another weapon than them since they immediately switch place with any other weapon he grabs. they always appear at his side even if he where to throw them into oblivion and they will not allow him to die. the only way for him to end their suffering is to destroy creation.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T13:54:52-07:00","id":667407,"title":"","content":"Heh, original Cloud Strife's prettier than that Batman and no guys, as far as I can tell, really got &quot;uncomfortable&quot; per se. (well except the people in every group who get uncomfortable about everything that isn't 100% conventional). They just tend (at least in the US) to prefer something else, more MMA tough looking. Not many women seem to be too interested in imagining themselves as Gina Carano or Ronda Rousy or even Julia Vins for some reason, still (as in paying money for this stuff), or worry to much about how close the women in fantasy really look to the strongest real people.<br /> <br /> Women tend to go the romance novel route, traditionally, when they want to sexually &quot;objectify&quot; (I guess), from what I can see. I think that's popular because sensuality and intimacy seems pretty important to women when it comes to this stuff, and most of the more visual artforms don't often have much time / budget / writing to build that kind of stuff. Why no graphic romance novels in the West is a kind of interesting question - guess it comes from comics in the past being seen as &quot;kids stuff&quot;? (which they are even in Japan and Asia mostly, but a little less so perhaps). Or just no artist can sculpt a cartoon to be as perfectly an object of desire for the reader as the imagination can do itself.<br /> <br /> With physical types, women don't seem to agree too much other than men not being obese (ideally not overweight) and usually tall height, or at least &quot;not short&quot; height. From studies of this stuff, if I remember rightly, the height effect on male &quot;dating success&quot; tends to be harsher than I think any single effect for females, although in general women are more selective towards mates (i.e. more men remain unmated and out of relationships than women). But then there's a quite a bit of variance on muscularity and skeletal robusticity (usually comes down on &quot;not much more robust / muscular than average&quot; though) and hairiness and age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https: