55, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Except for the exaltation being stuck in the soulsteel part, which I dislike (soulsteel, in my opinion, should not be able to do that)...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> ...Great idea. This is a character and backstory I can get behind. A character, motivated not by psychotic-murder-glee, but an actual positive intimacy, to act temporarily in the interests of the Deathlords.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T14:29:08-07:00","id":667454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667407#post667407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With physical types, women don't seem to agree too much other than men not being obese (ideally not overweight) and usually tall height, or at least &quot;not short&quot; height. From studies of this stuff, if I remember rightly, the height effect on male &quot;dating success&quot; tends to be harsher than I think any single effect for females, although in general women are more selective towards mates (i.e. more men remain unmated and out of relationships than women). But then there's a quite a bit of variance on muscularity and skeletal robusticity (usually comes down on &quot;not much more robust / muscular than average&quot; though) and hairiness and age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like(ed - I'm happily married for over 20 years) to tell myself that height wouldn't matter - but at 5&quot; 1/2&quot;, the number of adult men who are shorter than I am is pretty low, so there never was an opportunity to test that (For what it's worth though, were the circumstances possible, I'd totally date Peter Dinklage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T14:31:08-07:00","id":667455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667451#post667451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Except for the exaltation being stuck in the soulsteel part, which I dislike (soulsteel, in my opinion, should not be able to do that)...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> ...Great idea. This is a character and backstory I can get behind. A character, motivated not by psychotic-murder-glee, but an actual positive intimacy, to act temporarily in the interests of the Deathlords.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">oh it's not the soulsteel that does it, it is just a small part of the whole thing.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> thank you kindly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T14:38:24-07:00","id":667461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667295#post667295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, those don't work. The <i><b>constant</b></i> oversexualization of females in Western fantasy art has no real excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I don't know that it needs an excuse.;<br /> <br /> Western fantasy artists tend to oversexualize females because it sells well, and the artists and producers are interested in making money. If they didn't make money by doing it, then most of them wouldn't be drawing women that way. One can look at similar issues in other artistic fields to find similar things - take a glance at &quot;Furry artwork&quot; and you'll see that the artists who draw sexy characters tend to be much more successful and profitable than the ones who don't. <br /> <br /> Of course, this argument goes back thousands of years. Plato discusses it in the Republic. Should artists write, draw and depict things that are positive and uplifting to society, or should they be free to depict whatever they want for any reason they want? <br /> <br /> In the end it's safe to say that when (or if) it ever becomes apparent to companies that oversexualized drawings of women hurt profits rather than help them, they'll stop doing it. But, even if that day never comes, I don't know that there's any reason to excuse or apologize for doing so. Ultimately you're discussing businesses who are striving to make profits, and it seems unreasonable to expect them to take unprofitable actions for the betterment of society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T14:50:23-07:00","id":667469,"title":"","content":"If it helps DnD fifth edition artists were given a rule: &quot;no bare midriff or cleavage without express permission from the developers to put it in for any piece of art.&quot; And subsequently I believe one of the only bare chested things in the first trio of books was the very male incubus. I'm not sure if since then they've done as much, I haven't been keeping track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T15:11:53-07:00","id":667480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667461#post667461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Western fantasy artists tend to oversexualize females because it sells well, and the artists and producers are interested in making money. If they didn't make money by doing it, then most of them wouldn't be drawing women that way. One can look at similar issues in other artistic fields to find similar things - take a glance at &quot;Furry artwork&quot; and you'll see that the artists who draw sexy characters tend to be much more successful and profitable than the ones who don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is always weird to me. &quot;Without demeaning depictions of women, we'll lose sales!&quot; All at once this communicates that (1) if women want to enjoy your product, they have to endure sexism, (2) men always enjoy this stuff, or at least don't mind, (3) creative people are pandering hacks, and (4) there is no such thing as tasteful sexuality.<br /> <br /> How about instead of glossing over all that, we try to have fantasy art that (1) doesn't tell anyone &quot;not for you&quot; and (2) doesn't brand the owner of the book as a creepy virgin. Let's also acknowledge that people who create clumsy, gratuitous, juvenile portrayals of sexuality are making a choice. Not one they should be drawn and quartered for, but a choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, this argument goes back thousands of years. Plato discusses it in the Republic. Should artists write, draw and depict things that are positive and uplifting to society, or should they be free to depict whatever they want for any reason they want? </div> </div> </div>And now we're conflating dislike of some art for censorship. The question is not whether the government should ban something; it's whether the artist (and the publisher, etc) should make it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the end it's safe to say that when (or if) it ever becomes apparent to companies that oversexualized drawings of women hurt profits rather than help them, they'll stop doing it. But, even if that day never comes, I don't know that there's any reason to excuse or apologize for doing so. Ultimately you're discussing businesses who are striving to make profits, and it seems unreasonable to expect them to take unprofitable actions for the betterment of society. </div> </div> </div>No one is sitting around with an abacus or a spreadsheet or anything doing the math and saying, &quot;Hey gang, some of you won't like this, but I calculated that we'd sell 3,000 more copies if we include silly fake looking boobs with chains and skulls and shit.&quot; There's a lot of cultural inertia or unconscious assumptions or whatever you want to call it that shapes the art we see. That's why it makes sense to be conscious of our choices and not just assume that things couldn't be different or must be the way they are for a solid reason.<br /> <br /> And the idea that tits and explosions sell isn't even that well founded. I can go on Netflix right now and find dozens of movies with plenty of violence, profanity, and gratuitous nudity that never were released to theaters. Half of them have Bruce Willis or some other recognizable star (actually I think he's in more than half). I can find vast swathes of drawings and fanfic packed with eye-rolling depictions of sex, and it's all <i>free</i> for anyone who can bother to consume it. I mean, I'd be nuts to say that no one has ever gotten rich by shoveling out bad art, just as I'd be naive to think that quality always leads to success. But pandering is far from a winning formula.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T15:13:07-07:00","id":667481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667461#post667461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end it's safe to say that when (or if) it ever becomes apparent to companies that oversexualized drawings of women hurt profits rather than help them, they'll stop doing it. But, even if that day never comes, I don't know that there's any reason to excuse or apologize for doing so. Ultimately you're discussing businesses who are striving to make profits, and it seems unreasonable to expect them to take unprofitable actions for the betterment of society.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's the middle square in female armor rhetoric bingo.<br /> <br /> Businesses promote the values they want their customers to have. Some do it consciously through advertising, or indirectly through content and practices. I don't think it's unreasonable for me to try to encourage businesses to promote my values when I buy their products - after all, all I'm telling them is how they can better cater to me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T15:20:14-07:00","id":667516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667481#post667481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's the middle square in female armor rhetoric bingo.<br /> <br /> Businesses promote the values they want their customers to have. Some do it consciously through advertising, or indirectly through content and practices. I don't think it's unreasonable for me to try to encourage businesses to promote my values when I buy their products - after all, all I'm telling them is how they can better cater to me!</div> </div> </div> </div>I vote with my dollars all the time. *pats large pile of Pathfinder books with their diverse artwork*<br /> <br /> I'm planning on buy Exalted Core when it comes out. Definitely going to pick up the Dragonblooded and Sidereal books too. The rest of the books will depend on whether my distaste of the artwork outweighs my completist tendencies. If Chainboob makes an appearance, I will not be picking up the Abyssal book. Though, I doubt Exalted is going to make the same mistakes. Society today is a lot less forgiving about sexist artwork than in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T15:27:38-07:00","id":667521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667516#post667516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rest of the books will depend on whether my distaste of the artwork outweighs my completist tendencies. If Chainboob makes an appearance, I will not be picking up the Abyssal book. Though, I doubt Exalted is going to make the same mistakes. Society today is a lot less forgiving about sexist artwork than in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Onyx Path isn't on the same aggressive schedule White Wolf was, so I don't think we'll see another Savant and Sorcerer incident brought about by strict deadlines and freelancer snafus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T15:50:57-07:00","id":667530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667461#post667461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Western fantasy artists tend to oversexualize females because it sells well, and the artists and producers are interested in making money. If they didn't make money by doing it, then most of them wouldn't be drawing women that way. One can look at similar issues in other artistic fields to find similar things - take a glance at &quot;Furry artwork&quot; and you'll see that the artists who draw sexy characters tend to be much more successful and profitable than the ones who don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this argument holds across media - people look at/buy sexy furry art when they want to look at something sexy. People look at and buy RPG art overwhelmingly in the context of &quot;the art is attached to a sourcebook I care about.&quot;<br /> <br /> As someone else pointed out, the D&amp;D 5E materials had hardly any sexualized art, and it has been doing rather well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:14:25-07:00","id":667540,"title":"","content":"Hmm, incidental point: between some aspects of this tangent, my observations of codpieces and some stuff from Dark Souls (specifically Executioner Smough), come up with Artifact armour designed to resemble (and Evoke powers emerging from) the Woman of Willendorf icon. How's <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Willendorf-Venus-1468.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a></i> for a breast plate?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 09-17-2015, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:33:24-07:00","id":667594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667007#post667007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be mistaken, but I think hippokrene's third-person pronoun of choice is &quot;she.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667260#post667260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting question, maybe one deserving its own thread: What do those who are attracted to males find arousing and look for in art? This is something that's been an increasing concern in superhero comics as the creators have tried to cater to more diverse audiences, as well...<br /> <br /> Are the Hulk and Namor considered &quot;hot&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>... is that an actual question?<br /> <br /> More women find Ed Norton's skinny Bruise Banner hot than find the Hulk hot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667407#post667407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Women tend to go the romance novel route, traditionally, when they want to sexually &quot;objectify&quot; (I guess), from what I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>The men in romance novels are sexy. They're also pirate captains, business entrepreneurs, or supernatural predators who consistently demonstrate their social and mental superiority over lesser men (and their love interest) and are often the actual protagonists of story.<br /> <br /> &quot;I was attacked by supernatural creatures and a sexy vampire man swooped in to save me, and then proceeded to destroy the evil threatening the city while I, a mere mortal, trailed along after him. We also had sex.&quot; &lt;- 80% of paranormal romance novels.<br /> <br /> Romance novels are gender essentialist, sexist dreck* but the male leads in them are not objectified. Often, more care is put into their personality, motivations, and making sure they're active agents in the story than that of the heroine.<br /> <br /> They are not the Lover Clad Something Something but Raksi.<br /> <br /> *And often homophobic, racist, and uncritically promote the idea that some humans are fundamentally superior to others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 09-16-2015, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T17:10:50-07:00","id":667620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Western fantasy artists tend to oversexualize females because it sells well, and the artists and producers are interested in making money.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is a myth. Like, it has been empirically determined to be a myth. Y'know Mad Men? You know how it would have been based off of real life 60s advertising tycoons, who would have been just as racist and sexist and everything else? You can find references to those real life 60s advertising tycoons recognising how sex does not actually improve the sales of a product; <i>they were frustrated by that fact!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T19:33:26-07:00","id":667730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667188#post667188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I kinda want to know what kind of sexualized male character do the lady want to appear in artworks, since I have always wondered whether woman tends to favor the bishie, the hunk or the bara.</div> </div> </div> </div>My facebook is split into two groups of fans:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Sherlock (<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Benedict </span></span><span style=\"color:#6A