\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667816#post667816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know dozens of women who find garrus, the bird reptile thing with half is face blown off, attractive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Exotic Attraction ? Acting akwardly in a cute way around your Shep while having all the hurted badboy aura does make me feel all weird inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 09-17-2015, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T22:54:09-07:00","id":667844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667829#post667829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erinyes said:<br /> &quot;I value <i><b>human life</b></i> and I do not accept any excuse for artwork that encourages men to view us as objects which exist only to give them sex whenever they demand. You might think my comparison examples are extreme but women are raped and murdered constantly because so many men all over the world believe that we are sex objects and every artist and publisher who chooses to produce this kind of art is <i><b>helping encourage that violence</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Human actions have consequences for the lives of other people. Adults should take responsibility for their behavior.&quot;<br /> <br /> As a man [with three daughters], I have a couple of issues with this. I grew up reading Playboy magazine, and seeing porn movies. In my life, I have never abused, assaulted, or deliberately mistreated any women, because I was raised to see sex as consenting fun, and people as people. I am also not a homophobe, racist, classist, or other form of bigot.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Josh Duggar.<br /> <br /> Yes, human actions have consequences, and we are all responsible for our behavior. That includes teaching your sons that women aren't objects, and teaching our daughters that they aren't possessions. The presence or absence of provocative drawings doesn't give anyone an excuse for negative behavior - that comes down to taking that personal responsibility for our actions. Blaming drawings in an RPG [or anywhere} is tantamount to blaming porn for Ted Bundy's actions, or the Koran for ISIS.<br /> <br /> Provocative representations of idealized characters aren't necessary, true, but they have been part of art as long as there has been art. As long as positive [i.e. strong and clothed female characters] examples balance the others, I don't see the harm, and blaming such illustrations for crimes like rape only trivializes the crimes, and gives an excuse to the people who perpetrate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree in general, the preponderance of sexualized females in RPG art does add to the general subconcious sexism in our society that undermines the efforts to teach our children that women are as valuable as men. It also does add to the &quot;boy's club&quot; aura that RPG's, including table-top RPG's, hasn't fully been able to shake, despite the continued growing numbers of female gamers. I grew up having to accept that gaming was aimed at boys/men, and I just had to deal with the sexist art. My daughter shouldn't have to do the same.<br /> <br /> What I've heard about the art for Ex3 has me hopeful that when I hand the book over to my daughter so she can make up her character, there will be few to no times when she looks up at me, points to a particular picture and says &quot;Really?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T23:18:57-07:00","id":667859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667480#post667480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is sitting around with an abacus or a spreadsheet or anything doing the math and saying, &quot;Hey gang, some of you won't like this, but I calculated that we'd sell 3,000 more copies if we include silly fake looking boobs with chains and skulls and shit.&quot; There's a lot of cultural inertia or unconscious assumptions or whatever you want to call it that shapes the art we see. That's why it makes sense to be conscious of our choices and not just assume that things couldn't be different or must be the way they are for a solid reason.<br /> <br /> And the idea that tits and explosions sell isn't even that well founded. I can go on Netflix right now and find dozens of movies with plenty of violence, profanity, and gratuitous nudity that never were released to theaters. Half of them have Bruce Willis or some other recognizable star (actually I think he's in more than half). I can find vast swathes of drawings and fanfic packed with eye-rolling depictions of sex, and it's all <i>free</i> for anyone who can bother to consume it. I mean, I'd be nuts to say that no one has ever gotten rich by shoveling out bad art, just as I'd be naive to think that quality always leads to success. But pandering is far from a winning formula.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about other companies, but nudity in White Wolf books was very carefully calculated. It's not like they accidentally had a bunch of nudity in their books or anything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> White Wolf's goal was to use graphic pictures (including nudity) and adult themes in books to attract gamers who were tired of, or uninterested in White Wolf's other competitors. And remember that for awhile, White Wolf was the second most successful RPG company on the market right after TSR. So the use of nudity in their books was carefully calculated to bring in profits, and importantly, it actually worked. It gave White Wolf books more of an adult vibe, and helped them to grab a core audience composed mainly of edgy older teens, young adult guys and women(!) - White Wolf had the largest number of female gamers of any other RPG company during the 90s, and many were attracted to the more realistic and adult representations and themes in White Wolf books.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say that they came <i>because</i> of the artwork, but it certainly did help to set certain moods, themes and expectations that were clearly popular with gamers (male and female) in the mid-90s.<br /> <br /> Now, of course, Exalted fans in 2015 are not the same ones who were buying Exalted products back during 2005, and they're definitely not the same people who were buying White Wolf games back in 1995. Times change, what was once good becomes bad, things that were good business decisions then might not be good today, etc<br /> <br /> But I don't think White Wolf/OPP should feel any need to offer any excuses or apologies for using nudity in their products. That was just a business decision and one that was actually pretty successful at the time. It's just not a policy that OPP should continue to use today, because hey, it's a different world and different audience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-17-2015, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T23:27:24-07:00","id":667862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667859#post667859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know about other companies, but nudity in White Wolf books was very carefully calculated. It's not like they accidentally had a bunch of nudity in their books or anything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> White Wolf's goal was to use graphic pictures (including nudity) and adult themes in books to attract gamers who were tired of, or uninterested in White Wolf's other competitors. And remember that for awhile, White Wolf was the second most successful RPG company on the market right after TSR. So the use of nudity in their books was carefully calculated to bring in profits, and importantly, it actually worked. It gave White Wolf books more of an adult vibe, and helped them to grab a core audience composed mainly of edgy older teens, young adults and women; White Wolf had the largest number of female gamers of any other RPG company during the 90s, and many were attracted to the more realistic and adult representations and themes in White Wolf books.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say that they came <i>because</i> of the artwork, but it certainly did help to set certain moods, themes and expectations that were clearly popular with female gamers in the mid-90s.<br /> <br /> Now, of course, Exalted fans in 2015 are not the same ones who were buying Exalted products back during 2005, and they're definitely not the same people who were buying White Wolf games back in 1995. Times change, what was once good becomes bad, things that were good business decisions then might not be good today, etc<br /> <br /> But I don't think White Wolf/OPP should feel any need to offer any excuses or apologies for using nudity in their products. That was just a business decision and one that was actually pretty successful at the time. It's just not a policy that OPP should continue to use today, because hey, it's a different world now.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about that is a case of &quot;beware what you hook&quot;. If you persist in skeevy and pointless nudity of characters that should probably have clothing given the context of their existence in the setting, and you fill the books with it, you'll have a hard time convincing people to take it seriously. It's like word count in that respect; spending word count the way it did had 2e warping everything into a drama about magitech and gave us an ineffectual group of whiny grimderp Lunars, to say nothing of the first chapter of the Infernals. Fostering the visual version of this is not actually good for Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T23:40:09-07:00","id":667869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667816#post667816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"http://venturebeat.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/03/garrus2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I know dozens of women who find garrus, the bird reptile thing with half is face blown off, attractive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's because he's totally awesome, obviously. I was very disappointed when I chose the wrong option (I was trying to play it cool! Always foolish when trying to woo a man) and had to settle for Thane instead.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we're really getting off the topic, and perhaps going down a road that's traditionally led to threads being closed.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, let's go back a bit.<br /> <br /> If you could redesign or rewrite the Lady of Darkness in Bloodstained Robes (let's call her by her proper name), how would you do it? Or would you just have a completely new Midnight sig?<br /> <br /> <br /> In general, would you like to see completely new sigs for the Abyssals (like we're having for the Solars), and if so, how do you want them to be different to the old ones?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-17-2015, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T23:46:22-07:00","id":667872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667869#post667869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because he's totally awesome, obviously. I was very disappointed when I chose the wrong option (I was trying to play it cool! Always foolish when trying to woo a man) and had to settle for Thane instead.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we're really getting off the topic, and perhaps going down a road that's traditionally led to threads being closed.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, let's go back a bit.<br /> <br /> If you could redesign or rewrite the Lady of Darkness in Bloodstained Robes (let's call her by her proper name), how would you do it? Or would you just have a completely new Midnight sig?<br /> <br /> <br /> In general, would you like to see completely new sigs for the Abyssals (like we're having for the Solars), and if so, how do you want them to be different to the old ones?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>it's pretty easy to make lady darkness more &quot;acceptable&quot; artwise by just giving her a dress under her robes. if they want to make it look &quot;scary&quot; and have it refer to her backstory they could make it out of the sewn together faces of the prostitutes that threw her in the river.<br /> <br /> <br /> hooooold the phone there, they're changing the sigs for the solars? well if that's the case then sure change the sigs for the abyssals too.<br /> <br /> I want it to be clear what each of their role is so to speak.<br /> <br /> the dusk caste: should look like a general of the dead. aka a damn unique silhouette that someone that's never seen exalted before should be able to just go &quot;Yeah, that's a warrior or a general&quot;.<br /> <br /> the others are a bit trickier, but they should still all have unique silhouettes.<br /> <br /> for the midnight: hmmm possibly a imposing very high collared robe.<br /> <br /> no idea for the other ones <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":4455,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","user":"Xanroth","date":". 09-17-2015, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T00:05:30-07:00","id":667937,"title":"","content":"Erinys: Don't forget roping the U.S. government into helping you take out the leadership of a third-world country so a dictator can move in and offer you low, low prices for banana-growing land!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T00:20:17-07:00","id":667943,"title":"","content":"Wiz: Moar bloodstained robes, less not being covered by bloodstained robes. Is the simplest and laziest way, and would silence 90% of comments.<br /> <br /> If they would keep some element of nudity, they could take it to a less &quot;Heavy Metal&quot; type place by giving her a more unusual, yet still intimidating physicality, like a more explicitly deathly form, or a powerful, strong, athletic physicality. That would be cool, but then with inconsistent art direction, could go down a cheesecakey route again.<br /> <br /> If new sigs, then <br /> <br /> a) cultural diversity would be nice (it is a bit strange for them all to be the stock evil European / East Asian looking people, with no blood drinking pseudo Dahomey or pseudo Aztec cultists or crazed Central Asian warlords and whatnot, done better)<br /> <br /> b) give some sense that they have interesting goals and are mostly independent agents, and having some interesting humanity, not just there to randomly get dropped on Solars and frustrate their plans (couldn't tell you what their goals are at the moment, while for most characters in Exalted you usually can remember). ideally their plans could have some nod to rw politics or economics, but don't let any of this that get in the way of anything or make them lose being iconic &quot;characters&quot; to become too much &quot;people&quot;.<br /> <br /> c) Deathlord - Exalt relationships should be sufficiently clear and important that they're memorable and iconic (really couldn't tell you off the top of my head who the Deathlords are for the existing characters, probably not a good thing) and not overbearing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T00:33:32-07:00","id":667947,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it is right in her name (and she has them on the cover).<br /> <br /> I think all the sigs work for Mask of Winters. I'm not 100% on that, but they do all work for the same Deathlord. \u200b<br /> <br /> But they are rather lacking in goals independent of Mask of Winters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T01:26:34-07:00","id":667989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667947#post667947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it is right in her name (and she has them on the cover).<br /> <br /> I think all the sigs work for Mask of Winters. I'm not 100% on that, but they do all work for the same Deathlord. \u200b<br /> <br /> But they are rather lacking in goals independent of Mask of Winters.</div> </div> </div> </div>aye they are all working for the Mask. I would really like it if the deathknights look at least in some way showed which deathlord it is they serve","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T01:26:55-07:00","id":667990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667859#post667859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know about other companies, but nudity in White Wolf books was very carefully calculated. It's not like they accidentally had a bunch of nudity in their books or anything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna assume you're accidentally glossing over the bits where I say nudity and sexuality can be tasteful. My point is <i><u><b>not</b></u></i>, &quot;Oh my God! Eve, cover your sinful, lust-inducing body!&quot;<br /> <br /> My point is that chainboobs is not an Exalted version of a sexy but dangerous vampire: she's tacky and puerile in a way that doesn't suit Exalted, Abyssals, White Wolf, or Onyx Path. She's a silly cartoon. I imagine other characters just walking up to her, shaking their heads, and giggling.<br /> <br /> The decision to create a more adult game is indisputable, but the execution at times was poor. No one was in a meeting defending chainboobs, specifically, as vital to sales (&quot;I know she's ridiculous, but her presence will draw in approximately 10,000 more customers while only alienating 1,200 current customers. This is dollars and cents, people!&quot; said no one ever.) Of course the overall strategy at White Wolf worked out great and gave all of us something awesome, but defending bad art makes as much sense as defending bad rules or bad writing. None of those were integral to the success of Exalted!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T02:57:55-07:00","id":668039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667943#post667943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wiz: Moar bloodstained robes, less not being covered by bloodstained robes. Is the simplest and laziest way, and would silence 90% of comments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of how one of the visuals I quite like in Hellsing is the symbolic representation of Seras Victoria's transition to full vampire by the colour change in her uniform as it also absorbs the blood she's drinking in order to make the change, which is part of the overall change in her look to be subtly more threatening. It might sound corny to some people, but I think the way it's framed manages to effectively sell it.<br /> <br /> Also the idea of Kratos having an unnatural pallor because he's been cursed with the ashes of the family he murdered.<br /> <br /> I'm getting at things that extend into a more symbolic than strictly physical take on them. The idea of the Lady, or anybody else, having clothes painted red or black as a kind of cursed mark thing rather than being hit with a lot of blood splatter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T03:07:55-07:00","id":668041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667803#post667803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, most of your initial examples are actually illegal.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why nobody is able to buy shoes that are sold by American companies but were made in China.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're basically trying to suggest that when someone makes a drawing of a sexy woman, that by doing so they're inciting men to go out and commit rape and murder and that making a sexy drawing of a woman is comparable to child slavery? That's uhhh....</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't presume to speak for Erinys, but I can articulate my own position that the still distressingly common incidence of gendered violence and marginalization demonstrate that there's a wider pattern in the world which means that artistic representations of women based around not taking them seriously and selling their image to men is not a value's neutral thing. It would not be a values neutral thing even without those extremes of violence, since being unharmed but perennially mistreated is still bad, and even just having constant visual reminders that make one feel uncomfortable about trying to pursue something they find fun is just plain unfair, but those extremes are part of a spectrum.<br /> <br /> I'll also support the point that being profitable should be unconstrained by morality or decency is also a terrible position, even if we did live in some kind of magical world in which the production of an RPG was the least bit profitable.<br /> <br /> Still, I would personally be more inclined to compare it to racial caricatures; to asking one to examine if their argument would hold up if applied to, say, Ebony White of the old Spirit comic books. &quot;Oh, I've heard assertions that depicting African Americans as servile cartoons sells well, so that should take precedence over all else, and it has no implications for the perception or treatment of a group of people anyway&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T03:25:17-07:00","id":668045,"title":"","content":"Hm.. i think that ilustration fits image of Lady darkness. She was cheap whore (sorry for those words but they fit) in mortal life. Exaltation did not change much she is not creature of refined passion, being insecure in her position she uses sex as main tool to feel safer (get in good graces of important/dangerous persons arend her). Sex is her main or most dangerous weapon but i do not see her as refined person she is still vulgar and her picture reinforces that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4588-ludek","name":"Ludek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T03:53:00-07:00","id":668055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667816#post667816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"http://venturebeat.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/03/garrus2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I know dozens of women who find garrus, the bird reptile thing with half is face blown off, attractive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My friends tell me he apparently has a really handsome voice. I imagine that helps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T06:57:25-07:00","id":668183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667803#post667803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, most of your initial examples are actually illegal. Anyone trying to do most of that stuff would be arrested and put in jail or forced to pay big fines. Making sexy drawings of women isn't against the law (at least not yet).</div> </div> </div> </div>So now you're moving the goalposts to say that everything legal is morally good, and nobody should ever attempt to have a personal moral conscience. I reject this utterly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667803#post667803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're basically trying to suggest that ... making a sexy drawing of a woman is comparable to child slavery?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that was pointing out that this belief that greed needs not be countered by morals, constantly leads to human rights abuses.<br /> <br /> As for encouraging violence against women? Yes, Western society is saturated with the message that women are less than people and that men have the right to take sex whenever they want. That doesn't mean Western men are rape robots without free will, that there aren't also attempts to teach a less sexist attitude, or that every person is shaped in identical ways by identical subcultures. It does mean that a culture that encourages sexual violence <i><b>has more sexual violence</b></i>. Culture always shapes attitudes and encourages behavior, <i><b>that's what it means to have a culture</b></i>. It is impossible for humans to think or act in a cultural vacuum, uninfluenced by the society and experiences that shaped them.<br /> <br /> (Yes, that means that growing up in Western culture, I have absorbed and internalised some subconscious prejudice against women, even though I am one, even though I'm consciously convinced that sexism is BS. That's harmful to me as well.)<br /> <br /> Publishers and artists should take responsibility for the messages they send.<br /> <br /> (I guess I erred in implying an equivalence in <i><b>degree</b></i> between encouraging violence and directly participating in violence. I was trying to illustrate that all actions, especially those that put greed above morality, have literally deadly consequences for other people.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-17-2015, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:21:43-07:00","id":668225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ludek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668045#post668045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm.. i think that ilustration fits image of Lady darkness. She was cheap whore (sorry for those words but they fit) in mortal life. Exaltation did not change much she is not creature of refined passion, being insecure in her position she uses sex as main tool to feel safer (get in good graces of important/dangerous persons arend her). Sex is her main or most dangerous weapon but i do not see her as refined person she is still vulgar and her picture reinforces that.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're generally assuming that this background goes the way of Lillun if the LoDiBR makes an appearance in EX3. Which is to say, put it out of your mind, because it's almost certain to never come back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:43:56-07:00","id":668240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ludek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668045#post668045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm.. i think that ilustration fits image of Lady darkness. She was cheap whore (sorry for those words but they fit) in mortal life. Exaltation did not change much she is not creature of refined passion, being insecure in her position she uses sex as main tool to feel safer (get in good graces of important/dangerous persons arend her). Sex is her main or most dangerous weapon but i do not see her as refined person she is still vulgar and her picture reinforces that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the illustration fits a &quot;character&quot; (and I use the term loosely) that has no real backstory to speak of beyond &quot;lol whore with STDs.&quot; <br /> <br /> It basically vilifies sex work by casting a prostitute as evil, diseased, filthy, and gold-digging; continues to vilify women being sexual beings by casting them as wicked and lazy seducers (but ofc its ok for men to be hypersexual, because men); and also does nothing but objectify the female body with that art. <br /> <br /> Got it. <br /> <br /> As an aside I just reread her entry in Scroll of Exalts and now I want to vomit. <br /> <br /> Anyone saying that I'm Victorian-prudish for being offended by these portrayals needs to wake up and check this entry out. This write up is chock full of repressive purity culture bullshit. All the references to how she's lazy and bad because of her sexuality, rather than being a good lil world-killing nihilist. <br /> <br /> She has specialties in Dodge (Against Those She Has Slept With) (lol domestic violence IS SO FUNNY Y'ALL) and Presence (Sounding Smart) (&quot;DUMB WHOREZ M I RITE LOLZ&quot;). Like, I can overlook MA (Catfights) but those other two? Really? *Really?!*<br /> <br /> Her current defining personality point is hating the Maiden of the Mirthless Smile *for being prettier than her*. <br /> <br /> ...jesus fuck. <br /> <br /> This reads like an entry in a slam book, where the author is a 13-year-old boy feebly sniping at the girl who rejected him.<br /> <br /> I would expect the kind of shit in that entry to come from Donald Trump's mouth or be printed in FATAL, not from a respected RPG studio that continually produced great products and at least ostensibly wants women to be consumers of its products. <br /> <br /> inb4 someone says &quot;oh it's supposed to be ironic&quot;: no, you're wrong, just no","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:19:32-07:00","id":668277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668183#post668183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now you're moving the goalposts to say that everything legal is morally good, and nobody should ever attempt to have a personal moral conscience. I reject this utterly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vibe I was getting is that the illegality of these things does something to stop it happening (it doesn't - a huge portion of the world's cacao has been harvested by child slave labor, so the industry as a whole does its damnedest to ignore that, et cetera.), as well as the notion that the wrongness of an action means folks will do something to stop it (did anyone throw out their chocolate just now?), and that people have illegalized a number of your examples (they haven't, or they did it on paper and haven't done a damn thing to enforce it, or did but did nothing to stop folks from taking their illegal activities to a place that didn't).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-17-2015, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:21:30-07:00","id":668279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668055#post668055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My friends tell me he apparently has a really handsome voice. I imagine that helps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Voice matters a lot, I distinctly recall being attracted to Beast Wars Megatron yesss.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:24:28-07:00","id":668283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=667869#post667869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, let's go back a bit.<br /> <br /> If you could redesign or rewrite the Lady of Darkness in Bloodstained Robes (let's call her by her proper name), how would you do it? Or would you just have a completely new Midnight sig?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know there's a new thread about new Abyssal sigs, but I actually had an idea about redesigning the Lady of Darkness in Bloodstained Robes. It's still sexy, but not quite as &quot;WTF.&quot; Note that all I'm going from is the fiction in 1st ed Abyssals and the art next to it.<br /> <br /> Take the Versacce dress Jennifer Lopez wore to the Grammys in 2000 (It made quite a stir back then and is really easy to look up on google), make it dark red-brown (fading to bright red at the hems where the blood is freshest) not sheer, and maybe sleeveless. Put some sort of death imagery over the broach holding it closed at her hips, and add those infamous chains across the chest - but this time holding the dress in place (instead of the costumer's tape that was actually keeping the dress from being indecent)<br /> <br /> The chains now have purpose and she's now actually wearing said bloodstained robes.<br /> <br /> (I actually did try to throw something together in Daz Studio, but I don't have the right parts to get the image in my head across, and my drawing skills suck.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:46:41-07:00","id":668298,"title":"","content":"You're on to something DeWaterRat. I don't know what 1E Abyssals said about her but I imagine a useful character could be had if we threw out every single word and image of her, and started over with a totally new character, using the name Lady of Darkness in Bloodstained Robes as an inspiration. And I guess her Caste... what Caste is she?<br /> <br /> To me &quot;bloodstained robes&quot; implies a Midnight who preaches while wearing robes stained with the blood of people killed in some kind of Oblivion-sacrament, since robes aren't easy to fight in. The blood is spilled to feed the dead (don't ghosts like to drink blood?), to kill the living (either for euthanasia, or to make them undead slaves or soulsteel raw material, or to reward loyal followers with undeath?), and as a sacramental symbolism -- blood ties the living and the dead together through descent from ancestors; through being both a component of living tissue and a corpse-element; through feeding the ghosts their favorite beverage (I'm assuming here that they drink it); by providing essence to thirsty Deathknights; and through the sacrament of sacrificing the living to further the aims of Oblivion (circular logic FTW!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668279#post668279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Voice matters a lot, I distinctly recall being attracted to Beast Wars Megatron yesss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Gargoyles Goliath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  punctuation 09-17-2015, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:49:44-07:00","id":668301,"title":"","content":"That's actually rather close to her portrayal in the chapter fiction of Exalted: the Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:14:01-07:00","id":668335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=666021#post666021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now it would appear that looking into macabre imagery has given me yet another strong context in which those Abyssal Socialize Charms (with slightly modified wording for one or two of them) can work, because good God is there a lot of art depicting a young woman entwined lasciviously with a personification of death. An interesting combination of juxtaposition of imagery, drawing attention to how death comes to even the young and beautiful (especially if they're rock-climbing enthusiasts who follow a whim to climb some random place near to their home with no company or equipment), and taking a bit of the sting out of death by portraying it as a companion, with a bit of erotic subtext. {woof}</div> </div> </div> </div>Sex and death was always closely related. On the one part, they are opposites: the one begets life, the other ends it. On the other hand, there's a similarity: the orgasm, often considered the height of sexual cycle, is also often the end of it (at least before proper recuperation has occurred, which I think has pretty necromantic connotation in this analogy). Conversely, the end of life could be seen as it's climax, the height and the release into a subsequent satiated rest. The orgasm is not called the &quot;little death&quot; for nothing.<br /> <br /> Of course, humans are typically super obsessed with sex and death, so bringing them together was probably unavoidable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:47:00-07:00","id":668374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668183#post668183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now you're moving the goalposts to say that everything legal is morally good, and nobody should ever attempt to have a personal moral conscience. I reject this utterly.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll notice that not once have I said anything about &quot;good&quot; nor about morality. <br /> <br /> Businesses exist to make profit. They don't exist to improve society or do &quot;good&quot; things. What is Walmart's goal? Is it to keep the environment safe? Is it to improve America's way of life? Is it to make sure that the people in a community are gainfully employed? <br /> <br /> Of course not. Like any business, Walmart's goal is to make as much profit as possible, and everything they do is calculated towards making money. And businesses will do anything they can to raise profits. The only things they won't do are those things which have been made illegal. If slavery were legal in the US, and if Walmart thought it would be more profitable to employ slaves, that's exactly what they would do. The reason they don't is because the US government has made that illegal. <br /> <br /> If Gerber (the company which produces baby food) discovered a way to double profits, but it would involve putting a tiny amount of poison into babyfood, and they knew with 100% certainty that it would never be traced back to them, and no one would ever blame them, it would be incredibly naive to believe that they <i>wouldn't</i> put that poison in baby food. <br /> <br /> Companies are completely amoral and do whatever they can (legally, but also illegally if they think they won't get caught) to make the highest amount of profit. Once in awhile you'll come across a company that has other goals (such as Chick-Fil-A, which refuses to do business on Sunday's due to the owner's religious beliefs) but that is very, very much an exception to the rule. <br /> <br /> Basically expecting companies to act in a moral manner of their own accord is hopelessly naive. That's why we have all kinds of laws to prevent businesses from abusing their workers or hurting the communities that they're based. <br /> <br /> At the moment, it's not illegal to draw pictures of sexy women in America, and if businesses believe that by including pictures of sexy women with their product will improve profits or help them lock down market shares, that's what they're going to do. If you feel that drawing sexy pictures of women is morally wrong, then you should maybe contact your senator and try to pass a law making it illegal. Because that's the only way that businesses will ever stop doing it.<br /> <br /> But that is at the core concept of &quot;freedom&quot; in western society. As long as something is legal, people will do it. Spitting in public might be gross and unsanitary, but unless it's illegal (and unless that law is enforced) people are going to spit in public. And ultimately I feel that it's better to have more individual freedom (like the ability to draw sexy women) than it is to make lots of things illegal because some people find it offensive or hurtful. <br /> <br /> For the record though, as an artist myself (who has drawn a fair share of sexy men and women in the course of my life) there's nothing morally wrong with drawing sexy women. I don't feel like a horrible person for doing so. In fact, I reject the idea that drawings directly lead to an increase amounts of rape or that those drawings lead to men hurting women or that I should feel or share the blame of any man that goes out and commits rape. <br /> <br /> That's because it's important to remember that it's not only guys drawing sexy women, it's also women drawing pictures of sexy women. Melissa Uran has drawn plenty of sexy or naked pictures of women in Exalted and other White Wolf products (and even posted some on the forums back in the day). Would you say that her drawings are encouraging rape? Should she stop drawing pictures of sexy women? When a man commits rape should she hold up her hand, take responsibility and apologize?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:02:56-07:00","id":668399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668283#post668283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The chains now have purpose and she's now actually wearing said bloodstained robes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're taking her name too literally. The &quot;bloodstained robes&quot; in her title is a reference to her own flesh. Her title says &quot;I'm actually a monster wearing human skin as a disguise.&quot; In that context, her near-nudity is a perverse dig at the people who would be attracted to her, since they're only seeing her &quot;costume&quot; and not the &quot;Lady of Darkness&quot; wearing it. &quot;My flesh is an illusion,&quot; and all that. The chains she wears are a metaphorical allusion to the &quot;chains of slavery&quot; that the living wear, and that she has chosen to continue wearing in order to be a boddhisatva of the dead. She has &quot;chained herself&quot; to life in order to bring Oblivion's grace to everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":53,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","user":"blackwingedheaven","date":". 09-17-2015, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:08:23-07:00","id":668401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackwingedheaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668399#post668399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're taking her name too literally. The &quot;bloodstained robes&quot; in her title is a reference to her own flesh. Her title says &quot;I'm actually a monster wearing human skin as a disguise.&quot; In that context, her near-nudity is a perverse dig at the people who would be attracted to her, since they're only seeing her &quot;costume&quot; and not the &quot;Lady of Darkness&quot; wearing it. &quot;My flesh is an illusion,&quot; and all that. The chains she wears are a metaphorical allusion to the &quot;chains of slavery&quot; that the living wear, and that she has chosen to continue wearing in order to be a boddhisatva of the dead. She has &quot;chained herself&quot; to life in order to bring Oblivion's grace to everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... except that as I said, I was going only based on the Exalted: The Abyssals fiction - where they specifically mention the ghosts of her cult sucking the blood off the hem of her gown. Nothing symbolic about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:15:49-07:00","id":668405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668374#post668374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record though, as an artist myself (who has drawn a fair share of sexy men and women in the course of my life) there's nothing morally wrong with drawing sexy women. I don't feel like a horrible person for doing so. In fact, I reject the idea that drawings directly lead to an increase amounts of rape or that those drawings lead to men hurting women or that I should feel or share the blame of any man that goes out and commits rape. <br /> <br /> That's because it's important to remember that it's not only guys drawing sexy women, it's also women drawing pictures of sexy women. Melissa Uran has drawn plenty of sexy or naked pictures of women in Exalted and other White Wolf products (and even posted some on the forums back in the day). Would you say that her drawings are encouraging rape? Should she stop drawing pictures of sexy women? When a man commits rape should she hold up her hand, take responsibility and apologize?</div> </div> </div> </div>wait what <br /> <br /> There are certainly ways to draw the nude human female body that are not inherently objectifying, demeaning, or sexist. I'm not sure you have gotten that point. <br /> <br /> By the same token, female artists can certainly create art which objectifies women and/or is sexist to the detriment of women. <br /> <br /> However if you're saying that negative, stereotypical, objectifying, and/or sexist depictions of women in media don't lead to people IRL treating women in similar ways based on what the media says is &quot;acceptable&quot; due to those depictions...you're simply wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:17:23-07:00","id":668407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668374#post668374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Businesses exist to make profit. They don't exist to improve society or do &quot;good&quot; things... And ultimately I feel that it's better to have more individual freedom (like the ability to draw sexy women) than it is to make lots of things illegal because some people find it offensive or hurtful.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are repeating yourself.<br /> <br /> The profit imperative of a business is moot - businesses are comprised of people, whose actions promote the values they want other people to share (inadvertently or otherwise). &quot;Profit before all else&quot; and &quot;Female objectification in art&quot; are values that the people in a business can choose or refuse to promote. If they are &quot;free&quot; to promote values we (the customers) don't like, then we should also be free to promote values we prefer (by complaining or boycotting goods).<br /> <br /> I don't believe anyone has argued at any time for legislation against sexy pictures in general, only against their use in this context for this purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668374#post668374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...it's also women drawing pictures of sexy women</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't presently on the Female Armor Rhetoric Bingo sheet, but I think it should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 09-17-2015, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:23:29-07:00","id":668436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackwingedheaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668399#post668399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're taking her name too literally. The &quot;bloodstained robes&quot; in her title is a reference to her own flesh. Her title says &quot;I'm actually a monster wearing human skin as a disguise.&quot; In that context, her near-nudity is a perverse dig at the people who would be attracted to her, since they're only seeing her &quot;costume&quot; and not the &quot;Lady of Darkness&quot; wearing it. &quot;My flesh is an illusion,&quot; and all that. The chains she wears are a metaphorical allusion to the &quot;chains of slavery&quot; that the living wear, and that she has chosen to continue wearing in order to be a boddhisatva of the dead. She has &quot;chained herself&quot; to life in order to bring Oblivion's grace to everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. That's actually pretty cool. I hadn't thought about it like that before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:26:22-07:00","id":668439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668405#post668405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait what<br /> <br /> There are certainly ways to draw the nude human female body that are not inherently objectifying, demeaning, or sexist. I'm not sure you have gotten that point.<br /> <br /> By the same token, female artists can certainly create art which objectifies women and/or is sexist to the detriment of women.<br /> <br /> However if you're saying that negative, stereotypical, objectifying, and/or sexist depictions of women in media don't lead to people IRL treating women in similar ways based on what the media says is &quot;acceptable&quot; due to those depictions...you're simply wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as playing violent video games does not lead to people being more violent, looking at certain objectifying or sexist depictions of women doesn't lead to people raping or murdering women. There is no causation, and if places like Japan are example (which has seen sexual attacks against woman slightly decline even as hardcore pornography and drawings of sexy women have increased a thousandfold) there isn't even a correlation.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* I mean, just look at America. <br /> <br /> Since the 90's the internet has become far more commonplace. Access to pornography and other demeaning images of women has become far, far easier than ever before. If there was a causation or correlation, then sexual attacks, murder and violence against women would have skyrocketed since the 90's and access to &quot;objectifying material&quot; become so much more commonplace. <br /> <br /> But that hasn't happened. In fact, the number of rapes in America has been declining since the 90s <a href=\"http://www.census.gov/compendia/statab/2012/tables/12s0314.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">from about 100,000 to around 80,000.</a><br /> <br /> That's even after women these days are more comfortable in reporting rape to the police which was not the case back in the 90s, so there are a higher percentage of rape victims going to the police today than there used to be.<br /> <br /> So if viewing demeaning or sexy pictures of women actually lead to increases in rape, then we should be seeing more rapes reported today, not less. That's not what's happening.<br /> <br /> So I reject the idea that sexy pictures of women lead to an increase in rapes of women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-17-2015, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:30:02-07:00","id":668442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668401#post668401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah... except that as I said, I was going only based on the Exalted: The Abyssals fiction - where they specifically mention the ghosts of her cult sucking the blood off the hem of her gown. Nothing symbolic about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's both in that particular case. Because if you look at the art that goes along with that fiction--and every other piece of art of her <i>ever</i>--her &quot;robes&quot; in that are just a mantle that doesn't really cover anything.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> At some point I should write an essay about the ways in which Abyssals engage with sexuality as a deconstruction of &quot;sex as the force that creates new life.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":53,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","user":"blackwingedheaven","date":". 09-17-2015, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:30:50-07:00","id":668446,"title":"","content":"If all you care about engaging with is the (admitted) extremes of rape and murder, while basically ignoring all the other issues that objectification and sexism can cause, there's not much point in continuing this conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:37:44-07:00","id":668452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668439#post668439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just as playing violent video games does not lead to people being more violent, looking at certain objectifying or sexist depictions of women doesn't lead to people raping or murdering women. There is no causation, and if places like Japan are example (which has seen sexual attacks against woman slightly decline even as hardcore pornography and drawings of sexy women have increased a thousandfold) there isn't even a correlation.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but it does contribute to men talking over women in conversations. It contributes to victim blaming and slut-shaming at rape trials. It contributes to double standards of dress codes at schools. It contributes to women's opinions being discounted even (and sometimes especially) when it is something that directly affects women on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> Objectifying art is not a direct cause of any of those things either, but it is an aggravating element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":424,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","user":"DaWaterRat","date":". 09-17-2015, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:44:05-07:00","id":668458,"title":"","content":"What if the LoDIBS wasn't Appearance Five and was instead Appearance Zero and looked like a withered crone with skin the color of an old bruise that clung tightly to her emaciated frame and shriveled, saggy breasts. Who still walked around mostly naked and used magic to seduce the virtuous into carnal debauchery with her with some charm or artifact that made her low appearance not matter but still allowed her victims to be horrified that they were rutting with this unnaturally seductive monster.<br /> <br /> Would that be an interesting take on the seductive temptress concept? Would that be as bad what we've got now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:45:44-07:00","id":668460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668446#post668446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all you care about engaging with is the (admitted) extremes of rape and murder, while basically ignoring all the other issues that objectification and sexism can cause, there's not much point in continuing this conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erinys said that sexy artwork leads men to commit rape and murder against women, and that artists who draw pictures of sexy women should have some sense of responsibility when someone goes out and rapes or kills a woman. I have simply been disagreeing with that statement. Sorry if you thought I was arguing about something different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:47:05-07:00","id":668462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668458#post668458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the LoDIBS wasn't Appearance Five and was instead Appearance Zero and looked like a withered crone with skin the color of an old bruise that clung tightly to her emaciated frame and shriveled, saggy breasts. Who still walked around mostly naked and used magic to seduce the virtuous into carnal debauchery with her with some charm or artifact that made her low appearance not matter but still allowed her victims to be horrified that they were rutting with this unnaturally seductive monster.<br /> <br /> Would that be an interesting take on the seductive temptress concept? Would that be as bad what we've got now?</div> </div> </div> </div>i think she's appearance 3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://