t</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Gargoyles Goliath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Goliath is basically a handsome beefy dude with fangs, though. He's kinda the male version of a green-skinned space babe :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:59:31-07:00","id":668479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668460#post668460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erinys said that sexy artwork leads men to commit rape and murder against women</div> </div> </div> </div>Corrections:<br /> Sexually objectifying, not sexy. The latter without the former is easy.<br /> Encourages, not leads to. Like most events in the universe, rape does not have a single simple cause, it has multiple factors that can contribute to its occurance.<br /> <br /> If you can't understand or admit that culture influences human behavior, or that people should take moral responsibility for their actions, then this conversation is quite hopeless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:01:16-07:00","id":668480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668458#post668458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would that be an interesting take on the seductive temptress concept? Would that be as bad what we've got now?</div> </div> </div> </div>I still wouldn't be happy with it for a signature character.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:02:50-07:00","id":668483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668470#post668470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goliath is basically a handsome beefy dude with fangs, though. He's kinda the male version of a green-skinned space babe :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant his voice, though. His voice sounds sexy to me. Mmmmmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:07:13-07:00","id":668491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668374#post668374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically expecting companies to act in a moral manner of their own accord is hopelessly naive. That's why we have all kinds of laws to prevent businesses from abusing their workers or hurting the communities that they're based.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's why we are here, doin' our thang. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668374#post668374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the moment, it's not illegal to draw pictures of sexy women in America, and if businesses believe that by including pictures of sexy women with their product will improve profits or help them lock down market shares, that's what they're going to do. If you feel that drawing sexy pictures of women is morally wrong, then you should maybe contact your senator and try to pass a law making it illegal. Because that's the only way that businesses will ever stop doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, as you say, make them believe that it <i>won't actually increase sales.</i> As, according to Isator previously, has been implied by statistics since the 60s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668374#post668374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that is at the core concept of &quot;freedom&quot; in western society. As long as something is legal, people will do it. Spitting in public might be gross and unsanitary, but unless it's illegal (and unless that law is enforced) people are going to spit in public. And ultimately I feel that it's better to have more individual freedom (like the ability to draw sexy women) than it is to make lots of things illegal because some people find it offensive or hurtful.<br /> <br /> For the record though, as an artist myself (who has drawn a fair share of sexy men and women in the course of my life) there's nothing morally wrong with drawing sexy women. I don't feel like a horrible person for doing so. In fact, I reject the idea that drawings directly lead to an increase amounts of rape or that those drawings lead to men hurting women or that I should feel or share the blame of any man that goes out and commits rape.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, man. Laws are ultimately expressions of the values of those who made the laws (and also local affairs; this isn't only about America). You have to start from the bottom. Trying to ban something that most people enjoys doesn't work that well. Before we can ever get any kind of law down, we must change the values those who are going to be affected by it.<br /> <br /> Because it's not about offence. It's about actual damage. There's undeniably more violence and oppression going on against women and members of ethnic minorities than against men and members of ethnic majorities. This is due to our culture, and culture is literally everything around us, from the abstract ideas of representation and thought processes to the physical realities of living conditions and economical situations. Representation in artwork is a part in all that. It's part of that &quot;background noise&quot; that was mentioned in a comic earlier in the thread, and I fully believe it has an effect. At least as much effect as any other factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668374#post668374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because it's important to remember that it's not only guys drawing sexy women, it's also women drawing pictures of sexy women. Melissa Uran has drawn plenty of sexy or naked pictures of women in Exalted and other White Wolf products (and even posted some on the forums back in the day). Would you say that her drawings are encouraging rape? Should she stop drawing pictures of sexy women? When a man commits rape should she hold up her hand, take responsibility and apologize?</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, sexy isn't a problem. <i>The same kind</i> of sexy, <i>all the time</i> and <i>in every context</i>, is.<br /> <br /> Secondly, women and men both can draw problematic images of women. There is such a thing as internalized misogyny (and here I again use the term not as an instance of expressed &quot;man I really hate those womenfolks&quot; but rather as that &quot;background noise&quot; from earlier). There is some difference between the cases, in my mind, but not much.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think there's much to be gained from looking at individual cases of rape and trying to find a cultural explanation, in much the same way as looking at individual cases of artwork and trying to get those revoked or changed is kind of missing the point. Sure, practical cases can be useful as examples and points of reference, but they aren't really the <i>problem</i>. The problem is the cultural structures behind them, that &quot;background noise&quot;. That is what discussions like these seek to change.<br /> <br /> So, bottom line, I'm not trying to blame you for drawing stereotypically sexy people. I'm just trying to point out that there are effects, and also alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:13:33-07:00","id":668497,"title":"","content":"Anubis, I'll go out on a limb and speak for others here.<br /> <br /> NO ONE has said that sex or nudity is wrong. That's your straw man.<br /> <br /> NO ONE has said that art causes rape. Again, straw man.<br /> <br /> At some point you ought to engage with what actual posters are saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:14:28-07:00","id":668498,"title":"","content":"I agree with most of your post Weimann, except:<br /> <br /> First, I would never support making this kind of artwork illegal. The bar for restricting freedom of speech needs to be very, <i><b>very</b></i> high to maintain a democratic society. This is why people need to be taught to exercise moral judgement, not just to robotically obey the law.<br /> <br /> Second, the effect of culture on human thoughts and behavior aren't just something I believe in out of faith. This is an abundantly demonstrated scientific fact. It's one of the most fundamental and well-demonstrated pieces of knowledge of social science... analogous to germ theory in medicine, and cell theory in biology.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I have never seen AnubisXY's art, specifically, so I can't comment on it at all. This side-conversation started because of Lady Chaintits, not anything Anubis drew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:19:27-07:00","id":668509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668479#post668479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corrections:<br /> Sexually objectifying, not sexy. The latter without the former is easy.<br /> Encourages, not leads to. Like most events in the universe, rape does not have a single simple cause, it has multiple factors that can contribute to its occurance.<br /> <br /> If you can't understand or admit that culture influences human behavior, or that people should take moral responsibility for their actions, then this conversation is quite hopeless.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there was a causation or correlation between objectifying images of women and mistreatment of women in real life, you would expect that women today would find themselves being mistreated terribly today much, much more often than they were in the past. After all, thanks to the internet, pornography and other types of objectifying images are far, far more common and easily accessible than any other time in the history of the world.<br /> <br /> And yet women (here in America) seem to be doing better today and have more equal treatment, run more businesses and hold more national offices than at any other time in American history. Violence against women has been declining, etc.<br /> <br /> I feel that any attempt to link an increase objectifying artwork with an actual real life increase of objectifying of or committing violence against women is shaky. After all, if there was a link, we would logically be seeing the mistreatment of women <i>increasing</i> since the 90's (and the growth of and ease of access to internet and thereby that sort of artwork) and yet the opposite has been true.<br /> <br /> While making objectifying pictures of women probably isn't a good thing (but then again most actions aren't inherently good), I also don't feel that it's a bad thing and that people who do it need to find excuses or issue apologies for doing so or take some sense of responsibility for people who commit rape or murder.<br /> <br /> Again, even as the number of, and ease of access to, pictures and videos objectifying women has increased, there has been a decrease in actual rape and violence against women since the 1990's, and an increase in the number of women who hold major positions in businesses, hospitals, government, etc. So I think any sense that those kind of pictures &quot;encourage&quot; rape or violence or mistreatment against women, and that the artists should be feeling a sense of responsibility when such actions occur, is shaky at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:22:41-07:00","id":668512,"title":"","content":"I've already mentioned the existence of other factors that influence how often sexual violence occurs and/or is reported. Many variables change over the same time period.<br /> <br /> It's not as if I claim that men are robots and misogynistic art is the sole cause of rape. You're arguing against a total straw man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:27:27-07:00","id":668516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668498#post668498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with most of your post Weimann, except:<br /> <br /> First, I would never support making this kind of artwork illegal. The bar for restricting freedom of speech needs to be very, <i><b>very</b></i> high to maintain a democratic society. This is why people need to be taught to exercise moral judgement, not just to robotically obey the law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't actually endorse any law against it either. The freedom of speech, particularly in art, must be maintained. I was more getting at the order of operations implied by AnubisXY. He seemed to imply that the only way to get people to stop doing stuff was to make it illegal, while I think the idea must gain a widespread cultural basis first. Look at the Prohibition, for example. But yeah, I don't think we disagree on this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668498#post668498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, the effect of culture on human thoughts and behavior aren't just something I believe in out of faith. This is an abundantly demonstrated scientific fact. It's one of the most fundamental and well-demonstrated pieces of knowledge of social science... analogous to germ theory in medicine, and cell theory in biology.</div> </div> </div> </div>My faith is, naturally, based on scientific sources as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was perhaps a bad word choice, since it make it sound like some sort of religious faith.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:36:14-07:00","id":668520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668509#post668509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there was a causation or correlation between objectifying images of women and mistreatment of women in real life, you would expect that women today would find themselves being mistreated terribly today much, much more often than they were in the past. After all, thanks to the internet, pornography and other types of objectifying images are far, far more common and easily accessible than any other time in the history of the world.<br /> <br /> And yet women (here in America) seem to be doing better today and have more equal treatment, run more businesses and hold more national offices than at any other time in American history. Violence against women has been declining, etc.<br /> <br /> I feel that any attempt to link an increase objectifying artwork with an actual real life increase of objectifying of or committing violence against women is shaky. After all, if there was a link, we would logically be seeing the mistreatment of women <i>increasing</i> since the 90's (and the growth of and ease of access to internet and thereby that sort of artwork) and yet the opposite has been true.<br /> <br /> While making objectifying pictures of women probably isn't a good thing (but then again most actions aren't inherently good), I also don't feel that it's a bad thing and that people who do it need to find excuses or issue apologies for doing so or take some sense of responsibility for people who commit rape or murder.<br /> <br /> Again, even as the number of, and ease of access to, pictures and videos objectifying women has increased, there has been a decrease in actual rape and violence against women since the 1990's, and an increase in the number of women who hold major positions in businesses, hospitals, government, etc. So I think any sense that those kind of pictures &quot;encourage&quot; rape or violence or mistreatment against women, and that the artists should be feeling a sense of responsibility when such actions occur, is shaky at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. <br /> <br /> Because you've never had some jerk at a convention make fun of you while you're behind the GM's screen. You've never had some guy try to cut in front of you while waiting in line for a game release thinking that because you're a tiny woman, he could get away with it. You've never had to yell at the male players in your gaming group (all of whom are very pro-equality) to shut up and let you talk because they weren't letting any of the women at the table in on the conversation. You've never heard your daughter complain about how the one boy in her science group over-rode everyone else's ideas on how to proceed with the experiment - and later prove that her idea was actually the right one. Because it's never happened to you, it's not happening.<br /> <br /> Right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:40:08-07:00","id":668533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668439#post668439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Access to pornography and other demeaning images of women</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me also point out that I don't think pornography is necessarily demeaning towards women. In fact, pornography houses some of those most progressive depiction of sex, being very comfortable with displaying female lust, same-sex and trans-gendered sexuality and many different non-standard variations and kinks. As a genre, pornography is as natural and meritorious as any other. The problem, again, comes down to stereotypes: all too often, porn gets made in order for a male viewer to get his rocks off at the lowest possible production price, which causes the majority of internet porn to be eight minutes of &quot;unexplained nude chick gets banged by unexplained nude dude&quot;. Without any other context given, the standard assumptions of our culture will cause the depiction of the woman to become problematic. But really, porn as a concept and field of potential is a really neat thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 09-17-2015, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:42:19-07:00","id":668535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668335#post668335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sex and death was always closely related. On the one part, they are opposites: the one begets life, the other ends it. On the other hand, there's a similarity: the orgasm, often considered the height of sexual cycle, is also often the end of it (at least before proper recuperation has occurred, which I think has pretty necromantic connotation in this analogy). Conversely, the end of life could be seen as it's climax, the height and the release into a subsequent satiated rest. The orgasm is not called the &quot;little death&quot; for nothing.<br /> <br /> Of course, humans are typically super obsessed with sex and death, so bringing them together was probably unavoidable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I should note that the idea of orgasm being the end of sex is a male perspective. A female perspective is completely different. They can have multiple orgasms before their partner or have no orgasm at all during sex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:45:10-07:00","id":668538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668512#post668512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've already mentioned the existence of other factors that influence how often sexual violence occurs and/or is reported. Many variables change over the same time period.<br /> <br /> It's not as if I claim that men are robots and misogynistic art is the sole cause of rape. You're arguing against a total straw man.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in other words, objectifying artwork is, at most, one among a million other variables and there is absolutely no correlation between an increase of objectifying pictures and an increase in actual, real-world discrimination of or violence against women (in fact, if anything, there is an inverse correlation.)<br /> <br /> In light of all that I'm just going to say that artists (especially artists for roleplaying book companies) shouldn't feel a sense of responsibility when someone goes out and rapes or discriminates against a woman. After all, like you just agreed, objectionable artwork is not a statistically important variable (a smoking gun). <br /> <br /> It's like demanding that, when someone goes out and robs a store or commits murder, the makers of violent video games offer apologies and feel a sense of responsibility for the crime someone committed. If there was a direct causation (or even just a very strong correlation) between playing violent video games and committing real-world crimes, I would understand and even agree that companies should be held responsible. But that's just not the case and I can't get behind demanding people offer apologies for something that they weren't responsible for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-17-2015, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:47:20-07:00","id":668546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668535#post668535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should note that the idea of orgasm being the end of sex is a male perspective. A female perspective is completely different. They can have multiple orgasms before their partner or have no orgasm at all during sex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true! There are those damn cultural structures again; thanks for calling me out.<br /> <br /> I think the idea of the difference between the male and female sexual experience, and how it translates to the death analogy, could make an interesting theme for a seduction-based Abyssal of either gender. If not a published character, than at least a PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:51:08-07:00","id":668553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668538#post668538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, like you just agreed, objectionable artwork it's not a statistically important variable</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, NO. I said it is not the ONLY variable, and your &quot;evidence&quot; against its effect lacks any scientific variable control. This is another completely absurd strawman.<br /> <br /> This conversation is clearly quite pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-17-2015, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:59:56-07:00","id":668559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668509#post668509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, let me go through this thread from post #63 on see if I correctly understand the course of this whole argument:<br /> First, you state that the Lady in Darkness and Bloodstained Robes' depiction is considered problematic <i>only because she is female</i> - that there really is no problem here, just an illusion of one created by a double-standard.<br /> <br /> Then, when told that the style of her depiction suggests sexuality in a way that the male characters' does not, you argue that the depiction is justified by business needs - i.e, presumed profit by using sex as a marketing tool.<br /> <br /> Then you argue that there is no correlation between sexualized art and the behavior of people in real life.<br /> <br /> Your latest argument seems to be that artists are not responsible for how their art influences other people.<br /> <br /> Between these points, you have ignored posts by me, Isator, and others refuting each argument, instead producing a new argument. I am not at all clear on what it actually is you believe or want - would you mind going back to square one and explaining what makes LiDaBR's &quot;chaintits&quot; look important enough to keep as is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 09-17-2015, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:00:41-07:00","id":668561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668553#post668553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, NO. I said it is not the ONLY variable. This is another completely absurd strawman.<br /> <br /> This conversation is clearly quite pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Clearly it is. I guess I'm done too so this will be my last post in the thread.<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say that if objectifying artwork is a minor variable (and clearly if the number of real world attacks against women has gone down even as that sort of artwork has become far, far more common and easier to access it <i>has</i> to be a minor variable), then artists who make those sorts of drawings shouldn't feel compelled to offer apologies when people commit real world attacks against women, just like makers of violent video games shouldn't feel responsible for when people go out and commit real world crimes.<br /> <br /> I just found it rather aggravating and worrisome (as an artist) when you suggested that artists who draw objectifying pictures of women should feel responsible for and accept blame for real-life attacks against women.<br /> <br /> I think this whole thing just gets down to fundamental disagreements on the concept of individual responsibility and how much someone is responsible for their own actions and how much society is responsible for that person's actions.<br /> <br /> I hope there aren't any long lasting bad feelings over this exchange as I do enjoy reading your posts Erinys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:01:49-07:00","id":668562,"title":"","content":"Edit: In fact, I'm just going to agree with Erinys here. This is clearly pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 09-17-2015, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:05:32-07:00","id":668566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668561#post668561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just found it rather aggravating and worrisome (as an artist) when you suggested that artists who draw objectifying pictures of women should feel responsible for and accept blame for real-life attacks against women.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who the fuck has actually said this? Where is this coming from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:07:51-07:00","id":668571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668566#post668566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who the fuck has actually said this? Where is this coming from?</div> </div> </div> </div>He said it himself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:10:27-07:00","id":668577,"title":"","content":"&lt;.&lt;<br /> &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Not really an argument I like to get involved in, but there's one thing I'd like to bring up:<br /> What's the difference between &quot;Videogames cause violence&quot; and &quot;Porn causes discrimination&quot;? Or are they both the same? I mean, both are basically the statement &quot;Media shapes our perception of reality, and by extension, our actions&quot;. So, both should come to the same conclusion - either both are true, or neither is.<br /> <br /> (Either way, violence and discrimination are huge problems that only amplify each other.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:15:53-07:00","id":668608,"title":"","content":"S.. so, moving on to a different aspect of the original question: how does one play, or handle, a loyalist Abyssal, and not throw out suspension of disbelief?<br /> The main answer from earlier posts seems to be to give a reason, beyond simple annihilation, as the impetus. Have the Deathlord hold somebody the Abyssal is attached to hostage to compel obedience. Make the end of the world a means to justify some other end, like freeing a loved one from confinement or ending suffering.<br /> <br /> This draws attention to an underlying question: has anyone actually played a loyalist Abyssal in-game? How long did that last before either the motivation to work alongside the Neverborn and/or the Deathlords changed, or the impetus for compulsion changed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:16:49-07:00","id":668609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668546#post668546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea of the difference between the male and female sexual experience, and how it translates to the death analogy, could make an interesting theme for a seduction-based Abyssal of either gender. If not a published character, than at least a PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about an Abyssal who sets out to vilify sex and especially reproduction, specifically because they believe life always causes suffering and that the only way to end suffering is to end all life? This would be another take on the pseudo-nihilist pseudo-Buddhist -- a person who opposes all actions that create new life.<br /> <br /> The depiction would have to be handled very delicately, though.<br /> <br /> They'd also have to explain how ghosts without descendants are going to get their grave goods to prevent their poverty (and thus suffering) in the Underworld. Hm. Unless they also want to flush the Underworld and all the ghosts into the Voidhole to <i><b>really</b></i> end suffering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:18:14-07:00","id":668612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668608#post668608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S.. so, moving on to a different aspect of the original question: how does one play, or handle, a loyalist Abyssal, and not throw out suspension of disbelief?<br /> The main answer from earlier posts seems to be to give a reason, beyond simple annihilation, as the impetus. Have the Deathlord hold somebody the Abyssal is attached to hostage to compel obedience. Make the end of the world a means to justify some other end, like freeing a loved one from confinement or ending suffering.<br /> <br /> This draws attention to an underlying question: has anyone actually played a loyalist Abyssal in-game? How long did that last before either the motivation to work alongside the Neverborn and/or the Deathlords changed, or the impetus for compulsion changed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A lot of Deathlords aren't really big on the idea of destroying Creation either. They just play along for cool death powers. So if you work for a Deathlord like that, you could have a common interest.<br /> <br /> You are from Lookshy and your Deathlord has an interest in throwing the Mask of Winters out of Thorns. Thus you easily work for a Deathlord that wants to see a strong Lookshy. After that goal is fulfilled, you might have a strong relationship with your Deathlord and might be able to influence him or he can influence you. Intimacies go both ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:23:22-07:00","id":668617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668609#post668609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about an Abyssal who sets out to vilify sex and especially reproduction, specifically because they believe life always causes suffering and that the only way to end suffering is to end all life? This would be another take on the pseudo-nihilist pseudo-Buddhist -- a person who opposes all actions that create new life.<br /> <br /> The depiction would have to be handled very delicately, though.<br /> <br /> They'd also have to explain how ghosts without descendants are going to get their grave goods to prevent their poverty (and thus suffering) in the Underworld. Hm. Unless they also want to flush the Underworld and all the ghosts into the Voidhole to <i><b>really</b></i> end suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, there is an Abyssal Monk that wants to break the wheel of reincarnation and end all suffering? That is a pretty awesome concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:23:37-07:00","id":668618,"title":"","content":"Slightly concerned a threadlock is imminent. <br /> <br /> Still to go on a slight rant, well, with the ideas that porn could cause the sort of social phenomena discussed, it *could* do those things. On the other hand, things might not work out like that.<br /> <br /> It's not like this stuff isn't plausible at all, but Anubis seems obviously right that there's not really much very good evidence for it (although he's restricting himself to discussing the rape and violence side of things).<br /> <br /> To me, it's just odd how confident people are in this. For an example, there was a study feted in the newspapers this week about the &quot;surprising&quot; or &quot;contentious&quot; correlation among between pornography use and support for women's rights... which obviously is not surprising at all for anyone with any anecdotal familiarity with what the main porn using male audience actually believe and are like vs the non-porn using audience (e.g. porn users tend to have relationships more than non-, tend to be less religious, tend to have better mood, tend to be more interested and engaged with the sex to who they're attracted generally). See - <a href=\"http://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/love-sex/watching-porn-does-not-cause-negative-attitudes-to-women-study-finds-10498204.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.independent.co.uk/life-st...-10498204.html</a><br /> <br /> Now this still isn't necessarily explaining the causal effect of porn and images on worldview, which is extremely difficult to really test (but does show that these effects seem not really powerful enough to outweigh differences in personality of porn vs non-porn using men, or other effects in their lives). <br /> <br /> Apparently this was considered baffling or counter intuitive for some reason. Possibly because of people have a lot of confidence in deeply held beliefs about causality like porn being about power* and hatred of women, and stuff like that, that probably don't come from any testing, and just are really axioms of their worldview and ideology that *has* to be true (or else it would demoralise the political movement they're part of).<br /> <br /> *IMO of course, porn is not about power or violence of any sort at all - it's just some form of sensory neurological &quot;cheesecake&quot; left over from a combination of evolution (particularly evolution not preparing us for the modern world) and random cultural sexual learning. The problems people will have from it, when they happen, are going to be more like drug and alcohol addiction (where most people are &quot;fine&quot; more or less, and you get some vulnerable people with addictions that really damage their lives, and the estrangement and alienation from other people that is characteristic of addiction), and the performer side health and exploitation issues. Not really so much to do with most of the &quot;oh, this causes people to think of women / men / sex in a certain sort of way which causes x&quot; problems some people think will come from it.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean I think what is essentially &quot;soft porn&quot; should be in RPG gamebooks which are supposed to have mass appeal necessarily, particularly with changes in the modern audience Anubis talks about. But I worry still that these campaigns to reduce &quot;soft porn&quot; style art in some venues and forms are not going to have the effect people think they will and leave the proponents disappointed with how they've used their time, while embittering some small minority of men (not many, most will just make more visits to their hentai or whatever website of choice, but a few guys will really want to believe that they've been victimised).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:28:45-07:00","id":668620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668608#post668608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S.. so, moving on to a different aspect of the original question: how does one play, or handle, a loyalist Abyssal, and not throw out suspension of disbelief?<br /> The main answer from earlier posts seems to be to give a reason, beyond simple annihilation, as the impetus. Have the Deathlord hold somebody the Abyssal is attached to hostage to compel obedience. Make the end of the world a means to justify some other end, like freeing a loved one from confinement or ending suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another option is for &quot;end the world&quot; to be a long, long-term goal of a Deathlord or other Liege who has a lot of more immediate goals. The Deathknights may be only distantly aware, or not aware at all, of the ultimate goal. They are signed on for the more immediate, local goals of Doing XYZ.<br /> <br /> To me, &quot;end the world&quot; only really works for the pseudo-nihilist pseudo-Buddha who wants to end suffering by ending existence, and the crazy guy who wants to destroy the world for revenge/fun. That seems rather constrictive to me, and is one of the reasons I don't find Abyssals interesting.<br /> <br /> I guess there's also &quot;I agreed when I was desperate and dying, didn't really understand or have time to think about what that meant, and now regret it. But there's other stuff we are doing that I don't object to. / But if I try to rebel there will be Scary Consequences / But I have nowhere else to go and nobody else to turn to. / But the end of the world is inevitable so why fight it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:29:34-07:00","id":668621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668609#post668609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd also have to explain how ghosts without descendants are going to get their grave goods to prevent their poverty (and thus suffering) in the Underworld. Hm. Unless they also want to flush the Underworld and all the ghosts into the Voidhole to <i><b>really</b></i> end suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div>A valid idea, though I had thought descendant-less ghosts would either<br /> 1. flock to regions rich in deathly Essence, like Sijan or Stygia, in order to get things,<br /> 2. be covered under some sort of communal ancestor cult thingie (similar to the Dwarven Paragons, but even that revolves around specific individuals)<br /> 3. steal items from others through either bloody-handed theft, Arcanoi (I can't believe I actually read the Arcanoi, but there are Charms that let you steal grave goods), or normal filching (never really understood why they didn't just let that happen; might have saved them some time)...<br /> 3.5 Have people worship their ancestors so that a bigger, stronger ghost (or Deathlord) just shakes them down for their lunch money in exchange for continued existence and not be soulsteel<br /> 4. forge other ghosts into plasm and soulsteel.<br /> 5. use Mutilation Arcanoi (again with the Arcanoi) to turn X-number excess peasant farmers into ghost cows and grave goods.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:30:50-07:00","id":668622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668620#post668620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option is for &quot;end the world&quot; to be a long, long-term goal of a Deathlord or other Liege who has a lot of more immediate goals. The Deathknights may be only distantly aware, or not aware at all, of the ultimate goal. They are signed on for the more immediate, local goals of Doing XYZ.<br /> <br /> To me, &quot;end the world&quot; only really works for the pseudo-nihilist pseudo-Buddha who wants to end suffering by ending existence, and the crazy guy who wants to destroy the world for revenge/fun. That seems rather constrictive to me, and is one of the reasons I don't find Abyssals interesting.<br /> <br /> I guess there's also &quot;I agreed when I was desperate and dying, didn't really understand or have time to think about what that meant, and now regret it. But there's other stuff we are doing that I don't object to. / But if I try to rebel there will be Scary Consequences / But I have nowhere else to go and nobody else to turn to.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>one of my custom deathlords doesn't actually know about the end of the world part, he was promised the greatest battle of his immortal existence. to him it was a obvious choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:31:55-07:00","id":668623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668577#post668577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;.&lt;<br /> &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Not really an argument I like to get involved in, but there's one thing I'd like to bring up:<br /> What's the difference between &quot;Videogames cause violence&quot; and &quot;Porn causes discrimination&quot;? Or are they both the same? I mean, both are basically the statement &quot;Media shapes our perception of reality, and by extension, our actions&quot;. So, both should come to the same conclusion - either both are true, or neither is.<br /> <br /> (Either way, violence and discrimination are huge problems that only amplify each other.)</div> </div> </div> </div>To comment on this briefly, I am of the opinion that video games causes violence to the same degree that novels, comic books or movies causes violence. That is to say, it's not actually the video games, but the culture of which video games are a part. So it becomes faults to isolate video games by themselves, but equally faulty do outright deny their influence. They don't have a causal link to individual acts of violence, but they do contribute to a culture that clearly does glorify violence, which in turn might make some people commit such acts. These won't necessarily be the same people who consume the video games.<br /> <br /> The same reasoning essentially goes for stereotypical pornography or sexy artwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:32:37-07:00","id":668624,"title":"","content":"Of course, if fewer Deathlords want to end the world, and none of them are on the verge of doing it, like, tomorrow, then that solves other problems with the setting, in addition to giving Abyssals more options!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668617#post668617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, there is an Abyssal Monk that wants to break the wheel of reincarnation and end all suffering? That is a pretty awesome concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't take credit for this concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-17-2015, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:36:08-07:00","id":668633,"title":"","content":"I have to admit I don't have much to add to the actual topic of conversation. I've never played an Abyssal (nor had any real interest in doing so) and I've only used them as &quot;boss fights&quot; for convention games, since someone else was running our regular Exalted game. The one Regular Antagonist Abyssal in that game kinda became the butt monkey and our &quot;pet&quot; Abyssal... I do remember sanctifying a vow that involved us letting him live as long as he provided useful information against Mask of Winters... and then that part of the campaign got dropped.<br /> <br /> But with 3rd ed coming along, and a possible re-write of Abyssal-Deathlord dynamics, loyalist, long-term opponents are of interest to me. I have two major Abyssal opponents already in mind, one may or may not be a loyalist, but the other certainly is. And I'd want her to seem realistic and not overly cartoon villain in her behavior. (I still haven't decided if she's Midnight or Moonshadow)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:58:27-07:00","id":668683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668618#post668618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slightly concerned a threadlock is imminent.<br /> <br /> Still to go on a slight rant, well, with the ideas that porn could cause the sort of social phenomena discussed, it *could* do those things. On the other hand, things might not work out like that.<br /> <br /> It's not like this stuff isn't plausible at all, but Anubis seems obviously right that there's not really much very good evidence for it (although he's restricting himself to discussing the rape and violence side of things).<br /> <br /> To me, it's just odd how confident people are in this. For an example, there was a study feted in the newspapers this week about the &quot;surprising&quot; or &quot;contentious&quot; correlation among between pornography use and support for women's rights... which obviously is not surprising at all for anyone with any anecdotal familiarity with what the main porn using male audience actually believe and are like vs the non-porn using audience (e.g. porn users tend to have relationships more than non-, tend to be less religious, tend to have better mood, tend to be more interested and engaged with the sex to who they're attracted generally). See - <a href=\"http://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/love-sex/watching-porn-does-not-cause-negative-attitudes-to-women-study-finds-10498204.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.independent.co.uk/life-st...-10498204.html</a><br /> <br /> Now this still isn't necessarily explaining the causal effect of porn and images on worldview, which is extremely difficult to really test (but does show that these effects seem not really powerful enough to outweigh differences in personality of porn vs non-porn using men, or other effects in their lives).<br /> <br /> Apparently this was considered baffling or counter intuitive for some reason. Possibly because of people have a lot of confidence in deeply held beliefs about causality like porn being about power* and hatred of women, and stuff like that, that probably don't come from any testing, and just are really axioms of their worldview and ideology that *has* to be true (or else it would demoralise the political movement they're part of).<br /> <br /> *IMO of course, porn is not about power or violence of any sort at all - it's just some form of sensory neurological &quot;cheesecake&quot; left over from a combination of evolution (particularly evolution not preparing us for the modern world) and random cultural sexual learning. The problems people will have from it, when they happen, are going to be more like drug and alcohol addiction (where most people are &quot;fine&quot; more or less, and you get some vulnerable people with addictions that really damage their lives, and the estrangement and alienation from other people that is characteristic of addiction), and the performer side health and exploitation issues. Not really so much to do with most of the &quot;oh, this causes people to think of women / men / sex in a certain sort of way which causes x&quot; problems some people think will come from it.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean I think what is essentially &quot;soft porn&quot; should be in RPG gamebooks which are supposed to have mass appeal necessarily, particularly with changes in the modern audience Anubis talks about. But I worry still that these campaigns to reduce &quot;soft porn&quot; style art in some venues and forms are not going to have the effect people think they will and leave the proponents disappointed with how they've used their time, while embittering some small minority of men (not many, most will just make more visits to their hentai or whatever website of choice, but a few guys will really want to believe that they've been victimised).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your points about porn, I really don't think it's damaging as a concept, even if the most visible type of internet porn is very stereotype and could use some variation.<br /> <br /> However, porn is clearly labelled &quot;porn&quot;. It's about sex, that's the prime subject and an understanding coming into it. In an RPG, there might different expectations coming in. now, if it's an RPG about relationships, then some sexuality is clearly appropriate. If it's supposed to be about (say) dragon slaying, then there's not much real space for sexuality. If the artwork still insists on bringing sexuality into dragon slaying, and particularly if there's a double standard between male and female characters (which there generally is), then it might be time start asking why.<br /> <br /> In Exalted, I feel a bit of nudity and sexuality is appropriate, but it should be in the right contexts.<br /> <br /> Edit: But yeah, we should probably let the thread get back on track now. If you have a counterpoint to me, maybe PM it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:51:42-07:00","id":668770,"title":"","content":"How I'd fix the Lady of Bloodstained Robes<br /> <br /> 1) Different Costume<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://41.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m94tiolnbU1rdq2opo1_1280.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/scale_small/0/6342/1570493-liliana1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd consider all of these suitably feminine and suggestive of death.<br /> <br /> 2) Don't Treat the Character as a Joke.<br /> <br /> I'd forgotten how bad the write up in the Scroll of Exalts was. I'd probably drop the her being a former prostitute and make her an actual noblewoman. Actually, I'd probably go for a Lady Bathory angle: she was a minor noblewoman who used her power to commit horrific acts against the peasantry. Eventually, she tripped up and killed the cousin of someone with authority. She &quot;died&quot; when an angry mob is riled up against her and her guards do nothing to stop them.<br /> <br /> Now she spends her time cultivating her new land, indulging in sadistic tendencies, converting adherents to some bizarre death-based occultism she's come up with, and seducing those she sees as her equal.<br /> <br /> The &quot;evil seductress&quot; is a boring trope. A female character who is evil and enjoys sex with a lot of different people while having a host of goals and interests other than &quot;seduction&quot; is fine. The problem comes when the character is primarily defined by the fact that she seduces others, or the only women who enjoy having lots of sex with lots of different people are the evil ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 09-17-2015, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T15:30:08-07:00","id":668888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668770#post668770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How I'd fix the Lady of Bloodstained Robes<br /> <br /> 1) Different Costume<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://41.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m94tiolnbU1rdq2opo1_1280.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/scale_small/0/6342/1570493-liliana1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd consider all of these suitably feminine and suggestive of death.<br /> <br /> 2) Don't Treat the Character as a Joke.<br /> <br /> I'd forgotten how bad the write up in the Scroll of Exalts was. I'd probably drop the her being a former prostitute and make her an actual noblewoman. Actually, I'd probably go for a Lady Bathory angle: she was a minor noblewoman who used her power to commit horrific acts against the peasantry. Eventually, she tripped up and killed the cousin of someone with authority. She &quot;died&quot; when an angry mob is riled up against her and her guards do nothing to stop them.<br /> <br /> Now she spends her time cultivating her new land, indulging in sadistic tendencies, converting adherents to some bizarre death-based occultism she's come up with, and seducing those she sees as her equal.<br /> <br /> The &quot;evil seductress&quot; is a boring trope. A female character who is evil and enjoys sex with a lot of different people while having a host of goals and interests other than &quot;seduction&quot; is fine. The problem comes when the character is primarily defined by the fact that she seduces others, or the only women who enjoy having lots of sex with lots of different people are the evil ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll agree with you there. Isn't Iron Siaka a sucker for a cute face too, though? Or is that just my misinterpretation?<br /> <br /> You could even make seduction not really be about sex. After all, we are often intrigued and seduced by that which is thrilling and challenging. Death is the final challenge, the ultimate mystery. You could spin the attraction angle to be based on fascination and mystery rather than lust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T15:35:51-07:00","id":668893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=665960#post665960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;YOLO&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno if someone noted this before but associating DKs and &quot;YOLO&quot; really made me ROFL","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:23:03-07:00","id":668955,"title":"","content":"I still like the idea of the Lady being motivated to undermine those who see themselves as righteous.<br /> <br /> To this effect, I would basically model her as the character in the song Take Me to Church.<br /> <br /> I particularly like that line about eating a fine looking high horse.<br /> <br /> As for seduction: sex doesn't sell, but the capacity for an erotic medium to be indirectly arousing (in several senses of the word) is still genuine. I could get something out of the idea of a Lady who converts people into dogs worshipping at the shrine of her lies and partaking of that deathless death through speech, ritual and body language*.<br /> <br /> There's room for sex, but in terms of her attitudes being conveyed when she forms personal relationships, rather than using personal relationships to convey the attitude.<br /> <br /> I also still like the idea of her as a former sex worker, just less crass. Not so much &quot;became riddled with venereal disease and was tossed in a sewer by jealous rivals&quot; and more a scenario that gave her perspective on why people seek sensuous oblivion and comfortable lies.<br /> <br /> * Also saucy puppet shows. Puppet shows in which the Scarlet Empress and a random urchin of Nexus disrobe their flesh and twine together to dance their way into the embrace of the grave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:26:01-07:00","id":668958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668770#post668770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd forgotten how bad the write up in the Scroll of Exalts was. I'd probably drop the her being a former prostitute and make her an actual noblewoman.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Admittedly, having a former prostitute be one of the signature Abyssals might not have been the best idea, but I've seen it played, in my rpg group, well (also, admittedly, with more of a geisha or courtesan origin than streetwalker).<br /> 2. How would one such as yourself go about designing a former-prostitute Abyssal? Is it possible to 'play' Lady of Darkness in Bloodstained Robes with just a costume change, or is a more through cleansing required before it becomes palatable as something 'playable'? (This is not meant as a critique; this is pure curiosity, and as a way to analyze thoguht processes beyond the 4-5 people I usually play with in terms of character generation. I intend no disrespect for you, or others)<br /> ...(Melancholic: I now feel like an elcor from Mass Effect; granted, text can sometimes be very hard to convey emotions with)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 09-17-2015, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:46:23-07:00","id":668970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668958#post668958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Admittedly, having a former prostitute be one of the signature Abyssals might not have been the best idea, but I've seen it played, in my rpg group, well (also, admittedly, with more of a geisha or courtesan origin than streetwalker).<br /> 2. How would one such as yourself go about designing a former-prostitute Abyssal? Is it possible to 'play' Lady of Darkness in Bloodstained Robes with just a costume change, or is a more through cleansing required before it becomes palatable as something 'playable'? (This is not meant as a critique; this is pure curiosity, and as a way to analyze thoguht processes beyond the 4-5 people I usually play with in terms of character generation. I intend no disrespect for you, or others)<br /> ...(Melancholic: I now feel like an elcor from Mass Effect; granted, text can sometimes be very hard to convey emotions with)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to turn that uselessly around on you, it's kind of up to you and your table. You're ultimately the arbiters of what you find palatable, and frankly, what you have in your own games is none of our damn business. In that sense, she's &quot;playable&quot; as is.<br /> <br /> That said, since you're asking, I think the biggest problem is her history and description, particularly if you go by the Scroll of Exalts entry. Bare breasts are salvageable, particularly since it's a non-visual medium and you determine the context they come up in. As someone said earlier, her walking naked yet unscratched though a battlefield is undeniably a powerful image (particularly if armour is a big deal in 3e), and one I personally think there should be room for in Exalted (on the male side as well). However, some of the attitudes expressed in Scroll of Exalts cannot really be saved, and they colour her personality way more than her appearance does. I'd start there, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T17:44:51-07:00","id":669038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668958#post668958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Admittedly, having a former prostitute be one of the signature Abyssals might not have been the best idea, but I've seen it played, in my rpg group, well (also, admittedly, with more of a geisha or courtesan origin than streetwalker).</div> </div> </div> </div>I want you to imagine the 30-year-old dude who flips burgers at McDonald's. Do you think that his dream job is shoveling out fast food for minimum wage? Or is it a shitty job with shitty work that he does because he has to pay the bills and he couldn\u2019t find better work?<br /> <br /> If he were suddenly given the powers of Exaltation, do you think he\u2019d use his newfound powers to make French fries? Or, would he burn the local McDonald\u2019s to the ground and go do all the awesome shit he\u2019s imagined himself doing for the last decade?<br /> <br /> Streetwalkers do not spend their time giving men $30 blowjobs behind the McDonald\u2019s because it\u2019s their dream job. Not only is it a shitty job, but the vast majority of people who do it become victims of sexual assault. If you have a streetwalker Exalt, and you immediately position her as a superpowered evil seductress, it\u2019s not just a failing of imagination, but of empathy. <br /> <br /> A courtesan background would be better, as it\u2019s more believable that she\u2019d enjoy her work and find pleasure in continuing it after death. Even a streetwalker would work if the writer didn\u2019t feel the need to call her a stupid, cheap disease-ridden whore who Exalts and still does little but constantly fuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T17:47:34-07:00","id":669039,"title":"","content":"The bare breasts can work fine if you tone down the warped anatomy by making her breasts normal-sized, and move those skulls somewhere more sensible.<br /> <br /> (NSFW-ish?)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/89/Kali_by_Raja_Ravi_Varma.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div> Just ignore two of her arms, and replace the red garland-thingy with a chain. Give her some boots and skin that ain't blue. Make those severed body parts proportionate to her body (maybe hands and eyes/ears instead of whole arms and heads?).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that qualifies as sexy <i><b>at all</b></i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-17-2015, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T17:55:33-07:00","id":669046,"title":"","content":"I don't care much for the statement that she lacks any kind of faith to the point of taking perfunctory part in Neverborn rituals and pretending to have Whispers myself. Bad enough that it gets rolled into the whole arbitrary rivalry with the Maiden, but what even is the point? There are characters having dubious morality and even personalities, and ones who appear set up to be denigrated at every turn. I mean <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">her walking naked yet unscratched though a battlefield is undeniably a powerful image</div> </div> </div> </div> Take that one comic in the Manual, where she just stands still and looks irritated when a bunch of projectiles are flying at her, but then recoils and has a pained expression from their impact; that doesn't make her look casually invulnerable, it makes her look foolish. Put that along with various other things, and you wind up with a character who was treated like a bizarre punching bag. What was the point?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T18:04:42-07:00","id":669049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=669046#post669046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the point?!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm comfortable calling it casual sexism done by people who were totally unable to critically reflect on what exactly they were doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T18:05:19-07:00","id":669051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=669046#post669046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take that one comic in the Manual, where she just stands still and looks irritated when a bunch of projectiles are flying at her, but then recoils and has a pained expression from their impact; that doesn't make her look casually invulnerable, it makes her look foolish. Put that along with various other things, and you wind up with a character who was treated like a bizarre punching bag. What was the point?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, naturally, you'd have to make her actually able to dodge and/or soak those hits, too. Otherwise it'd be silly, as you say.<br /> <br /> Or well, I think Abyssal Resistance is based on (narratively) taking damage and then regenerating it instantly, so maybe her getting hit and feeling pain would be okay. But then you have to show her grinning as her fatal wounds seal to no effect, to establish the grounds for her confidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T18:15:35-07:00","id":669056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=669038#post669038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want you to imagine the 30-year-old dude who flips burgers at McDonald's. Do you think that his dream job is shoveling out fast food for minimum wage? Or is it a shitty job with shitty work that he does because he has to pay the bills and he couldn\u2019t find better work?<br /> <br /> If he were suddenly given the powers of Exaltation, do you think he\u2019d use his newfound powers to make French fries? Or, would he burn the local McDonald\u2019s to the ground and go do all the awesome shit he\u2019s imagined himself doing for the last decade?<br /> <br /> Streetwalkers do not spend their time giving men $30 blowjobs behind the McDonald\u2019s because it\u2019s their dream job. Not only is it a shitty job, but the vast majority of people who do it become victims of sexual assault. If you have a streetwalker Exalt, and you immediately position her as a superpowered evil seductress, it\u2019s not just a failing of imagination, but of empathy.<br /> <br /> A courtesan background would be better, as it\u2019s more believable that she\u2019d enjoy her work and find pleasure in continuing it after death. Even a streetwalker would work if the writer didn\u2019t feel the need to call her a stupid, cheap disease-ridden whore who Exalts and still does little but constantly fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's how I felt. Being a streetwalker Exalt is like being a slave Exalt, or being a peasant Exalt. It's what you did in the past, but surely you'll leave that job and go and have heroic adventures, possibly using the skills you acquired (though for being a cheap prostitute, I think the main skills are probably sizing up potential customers, and negotiating territory, rather than seduction: in real life, while courtesans have risen to seduce Kings and become Queens, the main route to power for a streetwalker is to become an underworld don).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-18-2015, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T23:06:08-07:00","id":669288,"title":"","content":"Just to respond to DaWaterRat's response to my post a couple of pages back [sorry it took a while to answer]; you make some valid points about women and their representation in RPGs. Hell, I remember when it was really weird when a woman came into a comic shop in the first place, and the attitudes and images didn't help. I just object to the association of sexualized imagery = rape that was apparently being made elsewhere. At any rate, the topic has been dropped, and I don't want to start it up again. I just didn't want to appear to be a troll. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T00:13:31-07:00","id":669306,"title":"","content":"It's <i>not</i> &quot;sexy images = rape,&quot; nor has it ever been. Really, it's &quot;'sexy' images that depict women as sex objects influences attitudes of men and women, contributing to a subculture that unconsciously and sometimes very consciously treats women as sex objects, contributing to the sum total of sexual violence toward women.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-18-2015, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T00:42:11-07:00","id":669314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=669306#post669306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> [...] contributing to a subculture that unconsciously and sometimes very consciously treats women as sex objects, contributing to the sum total of sexual violence toward women.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say a -<i>Sub</i>-culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","user":"Kim","date":". 09-18-2015, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T01:55:50-07:00","id":669346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=669056#post669056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's how I felt. Being a streetwalker Exalt is like being a slave Exalt, or being a peasant Exalt. It's what you did in the past, but surely you'll leave that job and go and have heroic adventures, possibly using the skills you acquired (though for being a cheap prostitute, I think the main skills are probably sizing up potential customers, and negotiating territory, rather than seduction: in real life, while courtesans have risen to seduce Kings and become Queens, the main route to power for a streetwalker is to become an underworld don).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think both examples needs the same skill set , the courtizan just need to have a higher mastery on the said skills. Cheap prostitute need to be able to seduce ( usually diff 1), judge a character ( whether the costumer/prey can pay up or not, but most importantly to determine if he/she would kill her or not in the dark alley) (usually diff1-2). Lie or con her way for survival etc...<br /> <br /> A courtesans has almost the same pitfalls in her line of work but the people she needs to deal with has higher MDVs, and they are better at detecting lies etc...and she need to be better at seduction alot more since there is alot more competition and higher MDV or external penalty due to prey begin swamped with beauties from a young age for political reasons.<br /> <br /> Its like comparing Elite First Recon to a new recruit. One of them is just better at what they do.<br /> <br /> <br /> And you are correct one you have exalted, you have Exalted!!...Either riches and oportinities are thrown in your face, or you run for your life for the rest of your life.<br /> BTW it was totally the Wyld Hunt that destroyed the local McDonalds, they just tell that he did it for anathema propoganda!! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T04:27:27-07:00","id":669491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=669056#post669056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's how I felt. Being a streetwalker Exalt is like being a slave Exalt, or being a peasant Exalt. It's what you did in the past, but surely you'll leave that job and go and have heroic adventures, possibly using the skills you acquired</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's room for some granularity in this. I would find it quite appropriate for a given Solar to wind up as fairly humble, remaining to contribute to their community in ways that might incidentally increase its fortunes. Winding up as a kind of local John Henry character, or... I'm thinking of images of Goku from Dragon Ball using his immense strength to break and carry whole trees. I certainly like the image of a person who starts trying to get a better feel for the land in order to work together with the peasants to come up with superior ways to utilize it.<br /> <br /> Or you can have folk stories in which legendary sword fighters come from humble villages that they neither abandon for big cities nor turn into the centre of great conquests, especially in cultures that conflated the commonality of the village with recognition of it as a place of rich culture and tradition and lifestyles.<br /> <br /> A character who just keeps doing what they always were wouldn't really be a thing (although it's not really a thing with the Lady either), but I would be reluctant to approach from a perspective that seems to look on certain occupations or circumstances with contempt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the main route to power for a streetwalker is to become an underworld don).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mental note: supplement my idea for the Lady of Darkness as dread prophet with Lena Headey's character from Dredd.<br /> <br /> Oh wow, she sold mind-bending drugs as well, didn't she? And had some poor guy she was abusive towards in a manner that had a mild erotic subtext that managed to be more &quot;person being exploitative of victim whom they have power over&quot; more than &quot;evil woman is sexy&quot;. That comes together nicely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T04:33:36-07:00","id":669494,"title":"","content":"She gouged his eyes out too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThe very existence of flame-throwers proves that some time, somewhere, someone said to themselves, You know, I want to set those people over there on fire, but I'm just not close enough to get the job done.\u201d George Carlin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123-trax","name":"Trax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar123_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T04:40:24-07:00","id":669507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=669491#post669491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character who just keeps doing what they always were wouldn't really be a thing (although it's not really a thing with the Lady either), but I would be reluctant to approach from a perspective that seems to look on certain occupations or circumstances with contempt.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly my point was reductive: actually, you definitely can continue to be a peasant, in the sense of living in a poor village (and I deleted several other examples, like being an infantryman), but you're no longer a peasant in the sense that you are forced to work the land. Maybe you defend your village from monsters, or build stuff to help their lives, or whatever.<br /> And there's perhaps some interesting concepts you could do with a Solar slave who continues to be a slave: perhaps they could lead the Mamluks to power, or be the power behind the throne.<br /> Similarly, a prostitute who exalts could continue to live in the seedy bad parts of the city, but she'd no longer need to go and turn tricks to make a bit of cash. She could become perhaps, a champion of the poor, a powerful madame, or even a sex-worker union leader. Or maybe turn from &quot;streetwalker&quot; to &quot;courtesan&quot; and seduce a king/queen. Or (as this is Exalted), a god.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... I'm trying to say this is in the same way, because I hate restricting character concepts (in terms of mortal background). I'm not saying that if a player said &quot;I want to play a Solar streetwalker who is still a streetwalker&quot; I'd say no (well... actually, for some of my players I would, but for a different reason) per-se. Maybe you can do something interesting with it. I don't really see what, but maybe a player could come up with something.<br /> <br /> I'm saying that I don't see the point of the Lady in Bloodstained Robes. What does she do? Badly evangelise, and screw her team-mates. How does this show what Abyssals are about (which is the point of signature characters)? She has no plans, and not really much in the way of competence or effective skill.<br /> Honestly, my impression is that the artist drew her, and then they made up the background later purely to explain why she looked like that, &quot;oh, uh, why she's bare-breasted, because, uh, she was a prostitute? Like, a really scummy one? Sure, that'll do.&quot;<br /> Honestly, if they'd said &quot;she's from Africa-land where they don't wear much, and also she's got this really interesting religion she's spreading, but it comes into conflict with her boss for X, Y and Z reason,&quot; I'd have accepted it fine.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-18-2015, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:07:49-07:00","id":670056,"title":"","content":"I wonder, when one talks about a courtesan seducing somebody, are they thinking of all of that roleplay stuff that might be a preamble to put their client at ease prior to the actual sex? Kind of like in that episode of Firefly where Inara is hired for a rich man's virgin son, and she has the tea ceremony and pleasant conversation with him beforehand? I mean, other than that... it's a service that one gets commissioned for, you don't really get seduced for it. Incidentally, I've noticed that most historical accounts of some unlikely person winding up rising from lowly position to become the consort of a powerful ruler (Theodora to Justinian, Roxelana to Suleiman, Catherine to Peter the Great), or managing to stand out amidst a harem to usurp the position of most highly regarded wife (Zinat Mahal Begum to Bahadur Shah Zafar), those accounts tend to universally feature women who forged relationships through wit and shrewdness, attractive personalities and no small talent for government, rather than being &quot;seductive&quot;; a few of them actually wound up becoming co-rulers or successors. It's an interesting point on what it might take to actually stand out and form a lasting connection with somebody who possesses the wealth and power to get sex basically whenever they want, rather than being lured into it somehow. &quot;Oh, you'd better watch out king, I might manage to manipulate you by being a pretty face and a good lay.&quot; &quot;Person, there are entire industries based around getting that to me on-demand; how's about you try to hold an interesting conversation for a few hours, and I'll decide if association with you is anything I want to jeopardize my dominion for.&quot; &quot;Drat, foiled again! Why is Amazon taking so long to deliver my copy of <i>How to Make Friends and Influence People</i>?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:51:38-07:00","id":670129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=669507#post669507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying that I don't see the point of the Lady in Bloodstained Robes. What does she do? Badly evangelise, and screw her team-mates. How does this show what Abyssals are about (which is the point of signature characters)? She has no plans, and not really much in the way of competence or effective skill.<br /> Honestly, my impression is that the artist drew her, and then they made up the background later purely to explain why she looked like that, &quot;oh, uh, why she's bare-breasted, because, uh, she was a prostitute? Like, a really scummy one? Sure, that'll do.&quot;<br /> Honestly, if they'd said &quot;she's from Africa-land where they don't wear much, and also she's got this really interesting religion she's spreading, but it comes into conflict with her boss for X, Y and Z reason,&quot; I'd have accepted it fine.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of the thing. I mean, people can rag on how badly the Abyssal sigs were portrayed, but in terms of productive discussion (well, I suppose inciting laughter is productive, but we'll go with productive in 'how do I use these characters?'), I'd say that you're going to want to start changing the character. Now, of course, if you change the character too much, they just become a different character, so you want to stick to their basic traits. So what traits does the Lady have?<br /> <br /> 1. She's an ex-prostitute<br /> 2. She sleeps with various members of her circle<br /> 3. She's jealous of Maiden of the Mirthless Smile for being prettier than her<br /> 4. She's not very devout, and her cult is mostly her own creation that sounds profound, even though she doesn't hear the Whispers.<br /> 5. She did <i>something</i> to attract the Mask of Winters' attention in order to get an Abyssal Exaltation.<br /> <br /> So, let's break this down. First off, we know the Lady was a prostitute originally. From the descriptions, she wasn't even a very upscale prostitute. These are the ones that get into the job because it's that or starve. She didn't have repeat clients that looked to her for skill. She was in the gutters, saw that her sexuality and body were her only tool, and proceeded to use them as much as she could.<br /> <br /> This ties into 2-3. Even after Exalting, the Lady isn't going to change much. Her life has taught her that sexuality is a weapon, and the one in her arsenal she's most familiar with. Using sex as a means to have leverage over her Circlemates is a common thing, because it demonstrates she has power, either through the simple method of leading them via their urges, or through having enough social Charms that she can persuade them anyway. It's a symbol, as much to herself as to the others, that she's not the disposable item she was before, and that what she handed out for a pittance before is now what people would die (literally, occasionally) to possess now. <br /> <br /> Similarly, her rivalry with the Circle's Dusk is because she's also grown to see prettier women as a threat. There's only so many customers to go around, so being the first choice was the difference between food on the table and starving. Similarly, the Maiden got the Mask's attention by basically walking up and being so crazy he stopped her heart and <i>then</i> Exalted her. The Lady's aware that the Mask is the whole reason she has power and status now, so him having another favorite for any reason is unacceptable, and a <i>pretty</i> favorite further undermines her own pro points. It's not petty jealousy so much as the survival instinct of making sure that you're the one to catch the customer's eye and thus be able to eat.<br /> <br /> Number 4 is pretty self-explanatory, even if it's a little contradictory. The Lady was never legitimately considered a person of influence in life, but persuading people by playing on the little hooks and quirks and insecurities was her bread and butter to convince them they <i>wanted</i> what she specifically could provide. Her cult benefits her in the sense of being in a position of authority over the rabble, rather than one of the scavengers begging the madame for scraps. But the Lady doesn't believe in the Oblivion-flavored tripe she's hocking. If she did, she wouldn't care about the fact her worshippers bring offerings and adoration she never had before. The status of being a Priestess of Oblivion is more important to her than the doctrine, and this is reflected in that she's not so close to Oblivion's nihlism to hear the whispers of her patrons slipping through the cracks in Creation. She'd have to be listening for them to do so.<br /> <br /> Number 5 is pretty much the big thing. The Lady of Bloodstained Robes did <i>something</i> to get the Mask's attention. He doesn't go around handing out shards to complete wastes of space, so something about her was so cruel and clever that he thought to recruit her into his service. What that was can vary from game to game, but it's the defining thing. She was <i>personally picked</i> to be an Abyssal. So obviously there's something that deserves it.<br /> <br /> Again, this basically boils down to having two choices. Either you ignore the character exists because they're bad and you don't want to use them, or you make them something you want to use.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:56:26-07:00","id":670134,"title":"","content":"I think Isator, it's just a matter of players viewing the archetype of courtesan through the viewpoint of a player character in an RPG.<br /> <br /> What I mean is, for real life courtesans, their goal was generally to make enough money not to need to resort to prostitution, to find a sponsor who had money, and to eventually find a husband or paramour who was willing to support them for life. Their skills, and their refinement of their skills where essentially an ends, in and of themselves. Simply by improving their ability to play instruments or their ability at conversation (or even skills at sex though that wasn't really all that necessary), they would naturally find their goals coming true. Further, they traditionally didn't need to go seek people out, but rather people would seek <i>them</i> out.<br /> <br /> But players tend to have much larger goals (overthrow the evil king, destabilize the Realm, set up a major kingdom, etc). For these players, when they play a courtesan, they tend to have a much different goal in mind than just making a living. For them, their courtesan &quot;tool set&quot; is the means to an end - they're going to want to hook up with important individuals so they can destabilize the king, or get important information that their allies can use. Further, in many games, the Storyteller isn't going to have the player sit around idly while sending various clients to his or her character. Instead, the player is going to find him or herself in a position where they need to be more active.<br /> <br /> This means quite a few players aren't really looking to play a standard courtesan but rather a Mata Hari-type seductress (and many Storytellers expect that a player who makes a courtesan is looking to play this sort of character and design their games accordingly). They tend to unconsciously add that concept to their idea of courtesan or simply conflate the two together for the beginning. So for many people, when they say they want to play a courtesan or when they think about courtesans, they are in part thinking about spies who use seduction - someone who uses those courtesan skills as a means towards an end.<br /> <br /> Because of that, a lot of players tend to view the entire system of courtesans through the &quot;player perspective&quot; and imagine that seduction is a very important tool that courtesans need, even though that isn't really the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:03:09-07:00","id":670213,"title":"","content":"Darn it, did I forget to add that part about people who wound up as the second most powerful folks in the Byzantine, Ottoman and Russian empires through their development of profound relationships out of what might have started off as basic physical attractions? Shoot, I was so happy with those examples, and for them to go to waste like that... such a pity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:19:09-07:00","id":670226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OpMegs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=670129#post670129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this basically boils down to having two choices. Either you ignore the character exists because they're bad and you don't want to use them, or you make them something you want to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd ditch the whole notion of &quot;well I basically channel the Anti-Life Equation and can scream so hard peoples' skin falls off, but my defining character trait is hating Becky because she's prettier than me.&quot;<br /> <br /> That kind of junior high drek ruins it; even if it's a perfectly normal human feeling to be insecure about your appearance and jealous of someone else for theirs, and while i think it's totally acceptable for Exalted to have those feelings, it's pretty weak sauce when that is the <i>primary</i> conflict point between Abyssals. It's not even on a level of &quot;she wants to kill everything, while I want to ride the world down an infinite sinkhole while riding on a mattress made of people of every possible gender.&quot; It's just so <i>banal. </i>It makes for a good personality facet, but not the most front-and-center thing about her.<br /> <br /> 1-2 and 4-5 aren't terrible, though #2 is just kind of...ehhhh....to me, it's pretty boring, and if the character was a PC, it's a thing that can be problematic. The rest is generally ok as a basis. I even like the &quot;priestly&quot; caste being irreverent!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 09-18-2015, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:33:44-07:00","id":670231,"title":"","content":"I look at it all laid out and... the character is all about sex and basically nothing else. She's one-dimensional. A cardboard cutout, not a person. Add that it's a woman, drawn the way she's drawn, whose life revolves around sex and apparently only sex, and I don't see how the character is worth keeping in canon.<br /> <br /> If an Abyssal is trying to destroy kingdoms or alliances or cities through sex, they're probably better off doing it as Isator Levie described, by focusing on the talky stuff that goes along with being a high-society courtesan.<br /> <br /> If they're using just sex itself as a weapon, they could instead use it as a vehicle for bizarre brainwashing charms, or they should be inventing new venereal diseases or maybe parasites and introducing them into living populations as weapons or experiments. Twist the very force that creates new life into a vehicle for death, cause children to be born already diseased or sickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-18-2015, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T17:33:40-07:00","id":670341,"title":"","content":"On the other hand...the very image that she apparently projects plays right into the type of society and male stereotyping that we have been decrying in this thread. Isn't it possible that, as an Abyssal, she would appear exactly the way that oh-so-many men expect, and take advantage of their &quot;Oh, look; a whore. How dangerous can she possibly be?&quot; mentality?<br /> That's how I would play her. My wife has a very powerful character [in a different game system] who was once a courtesan, and she uses her knowledge of male psychology to her advantage in business, combat, and leadership. Just because the image is overtly sexual doesn't mean it's useless, or that the character in question couldn't be used. But it's what works for you in your game that matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T18:13:30-07:00","id":670358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=670341#post670341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand...the very image that she apparently projects plays right into the type of society and male stereotyping that we have been decrying in this thread. Isn't it possible that, as an Abyssal, she would appear exactly the way that oh-so-many men expect, and take advantage of their &quot;Oh, look; a whore. How dangerous can she possibly be?&quot; mentality?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the value in an ironic/subversive interpretation like that outweighs the very real risk of someone reading it straight and thinking it's an acceptable norm. <br /> <br /> Also it's pretty clear that, while that could be a good way to portray her, that was in no way the authorial intent. And that is an equally big issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T18:13:39-07:00","id":670359,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that's more about using sexuality as a cover for the Abyssal's actual weapon(s), whatever those may be.<br /> But I guess my disease/parasite, HAX brainwashing charms, and talky manipulation suggestions fall under the same rubric.<br /> <br /> Either way, something has to be added to the carboard cutout to make it an actually interesting character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T18:19:05-07:00","id":670363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an Abyssal is trying to destroy kingdoms or alliances or cities through sex, they're probably better off doing it as Isator Levie described, by focusing on the talky stuff that goes along with being a high-society courtesan.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I think there's two sides to that. When it's a courtesan who's looking to work their way up to consort, I see the personality stuff as taking precedent. If you're somebody like Nur Bai of Delhi, who was said to have the lanes around her house backed up each night with elephants carrying gifts to her, and drove many men to ruin, I'd see it as a form of brand management; you offer a quality service, but also cultivate the image of prestige that reflects well on those who give so much to you. Either case has more to it than seduction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T19:32:55-07:00","id":670426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=670226#post670226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd ditch the whole notion of &quot;well I basically channel the Anti-Life Equation and can scream so hard peoples' skin falls off, but my defining character trait is hating Becky because she's prettier than me.&quot;<br /> <br /> That kind of junior high drek ruins it; even if it's a perfectly normal human feeling to be insecure about your appearance and jealous of someone else for theirs, and while i think it's totally acceptable for Exalted to have those feelings, it's pretty weak sauce when that is the <i>primary</i> conflict point between Abyssals. It's not even on a level of &quot;she wants to kill everything, while I want to ride the world down an infinite sinkhole while riding on a mattress made of people of every possible gender.&quot; It's just so <i>banal. </i>It makes for a good personality facet, but not the most front-and-center thing about her.<br /> <br /> 1-2 and 4-5 aren't terrible, though #2 is just kind of...ehhhh....to me, it's pretty boring, and if the character was a PC, it's a thing that can be problematic. The rest is generally ok as a basis. I even like the &quot;priestly&quot; caste being irreverent!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. This is basically boiling down the big things and adding a touch more depth to them than presented while not changing them too overtly. It gives a bit more flesh to the reasons, but doesn't change what they are, which, like you said, is kind of questionable as is.<br /> <br /> If I was going less &quot;taking the canon and smoothing a few rough edges&quot;, I'd honestly go for the social camouflage route, where she's deliberately playing the vain, self-absorbed harlot-made-good to hide the fact that she's smarter. By this token, the &quot;I hate the Maiden because she's prettier than me&quot; is presented as &quot;because pretty = a weapon and I need as many as I can get&quot; but is actually because &quot;The Maiden can't be bargained with, and while I can loop her around a little, when it comes down to it, she just wants to see the world burn, while I <i>enjoy</i> the living world, but can't actually <i>say so</i> because my boss works for a bunch of people where the Maiden is Employee of the Year for getting on board with the mission statement.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, using it as a way of hiding her real self is pretty much a recursive &quot;okay, she acts like this but she's actually nothing like this&quot; explanation, and still kinda dealing with the flotsam of her rather poorly done 2E portrayal.<br /> <br /> If I was going to go whole hog and just lay into changes, I'd keep her origin as is, and basically have her die more because [inciting event] caused her to realize that her life was killing her slowly, and she'd rather slit the throats and pick the pockets of a few of the assholes on the way out and risk nasty death rather than continue sucking down the abuse. Keep the Abyssal Priestess who's not devout aspect because she likes the power, and essentially have her be the Devil May Care type that does it mostly because in the end, she's looked at Death and found there are things worse than it. Better to live and die on her terms than survive on someone else's. Essentially thumbing her nose at the concept of Inevitable Death Bearing down would probably tickle the Mask's sense of humor, given he's the Deathlord least interested in causing Oblivion, and her social schemer/backstabbiness would probably remind him of himself. It'd also fit the more apprentice/master relationship the Deathlords are likely to have in 3E.<br /> <br /> Amusingly, in this version, she'd probably be the boss's favorite compared to the Maiden who's the boss's bosses' favorite. <br /> <br /> That said, I still cannot say anything to justify chaintits. If you're deep enough into a Resistance Tree that your skin is armor enough, you might as well go whole hog John Carter of Mars level accessories and nothing else like Basphomy from the Infernal preview. So the lesson learned here today is <i>just say no to chaintits</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T21:54:11-07:00","id":670478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=670341#post670341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand...the very image that she apparently projects plays right into the type of society and male stereotyping that we have been decrying in this thread. Isn't it possible that, as an Abyssal, she would appear exactly the way that oh-so-many men expect, and take advantage of their &quot;Oh, look; a whore. How dangerous can she possibly be?&quot; mentality?</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem is that this mentality is more likely to be found among modern readers than people in Creation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T22:07:28-07:00","id":670483,"title":"","content":"I'm reasonably sure most mortal denizens of Creation don't expect sex workers to literally scream their faces off.<br /> <br /> Well, maybe in Sijan...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T22:33:37-07:00","id":670490,"title":"","content":"I'm reasonably sure that most denizens of Creation (mortal or otherwise) wouldn't see someone dressed like The Lady of Darkness and think &quot;sex worker&quot;.<br /> The point stands, it's a modern reader who'll be inclined to underestimate her as pointless fanservice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T00:31:31-07:00","id":670533,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I guess I'm just trying to think as a GM, &quot;How would I make her useful/interesting&quot; vs. &quot;How did the writers/artists portray this character&quot;, and they aren't the same thing. But I'm leery of sexuality being eliminated from any future material for fear of giving offense or feeding in to stereotypes. No, the &quot;Chain-boobs&quot; art isn't necessary, but in the same way that Creation doesn't have the negative stereotypes about women and clothing, they shouldn't have our negative views on sexuality, either. Hopefully the new editors/artists will be able to allow material for an adult audience [not &quot;erotica/porn&quot;, but mature subjects and stories] without being gratuitous. Having survived the great &quot;D&amp;D is Satanism&quot; panic of the 80's, I don't want to see fear of objectifying people remove anything even remotely upsetting from the world of RPGs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T04:23:56-07:00","id":670763,"title":"","content":"I think one might find that there's a key difference between notions of &quot;tabletop gaming promotes satanism/video gaming promotes violence&quot; and &quot;tabletop/video gaming exist amidst a hotbed of misogynistic exclusivity&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T04:35:17-07:00","id":670784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=670533#post670533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I guess I'm just trying to think as a GM, &quot;How would I make her useful/interesting&quot; vs. &quot;How did the writers/artists portray this character&quot;, and they aren't the same thing. But I'm leery of sexuality being eliminated from any future material for fear of giving offense or feeding in to stereotypes. No, the &quot;Chain-boobs&quot; art isn't necessary, but in the same way that Creation doesn't have the negative stereotypes about women and clothing, they shouldn't have our negative views on sexuality, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation may not, as a whole (though certainly some places probably do; Creation has more land than Earth, and a myriad of different cultures, each with its own mores).<br /> <br /> However even if Creation generally does not, the real world does. <br /> <br /> The real world is a context in which the game exists, and the people who wrote the game should be mindful of this. <br /> <br /> There is a huge difference between saying &quot;all imagery which could possibly be interpreted as erotic should be eliminated&quot; and &quot;blatant sexualized/fanservice media that effectively play into real world notions about the badness of women's sexuality have no place in the books.&quot; People need to stop conflating the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T09:30:48-07:00","id":671028,"title":"","content":"No, no, I get the difference. I'm just concerned that trying to eliminate the one thing [fan-service art] will lead to the other [sanitizing of the products]. The &quot;D&amp;D is Satan&quot; thing spread out to cause an atmosphere of &quot;kids play the games, so we should only cater to kids&quot; for a while after the peak of the hysteria [something that is thankfully long over now], and so it's easy for things to get out of hand.The White Wolf WoD line was, in many ways, the beginning of the end of that era. It went too far on more than one occasion, but it got the hobby on a road to recognizing that the audience includes a lot of adults, and that sex, violence, religion, and other sensitive topics shouldn't be taboo in RPGs. Putting a Muslim terrorist, who uses their version of their religion as a weapon, in an action RPG doesn't mean you think all Muslims are terrorists [they aren't]; putting a female character who uses sex as a weapon in an RPG doesn't/shouldn't mean you see all women in a negative light. The problem is a lack of balance, in ALL forms of media.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T10:01:09-07:00","id":671039,"title":"","content":"I don't think Onyx Path or the Ex3 team is in any danger publishing sanitized &quot;but think of the children!&quot; books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T10:52:04-07:00","id":671114,"title":"","content":"Also, is parading around topless even a good idea for a seductress or a prostitute?<br /> I've generally been under the belief that nudity very quickly loses its allure when it's present constantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T11:05:15-07:00","id":671143,"title":"","content":"I'd depend that on the body in question and if one is in the mood to see naked people. It's a lot more complex then the novelty of being nude wearing off, though that probably plays some role.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T11:11:13-07:00","id":671149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671028#post671028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, no, I get the difference. I'm just concerned that trying to eliminate the one thing [fan-service art] will lead to the other [sanitizing of the products]. The &quot;D&amp;D is Satan&quot; thing spread out to cause an atmosphere of &quot;kids play the games, so we should only cater to kids&quot; for a while after the peak of the hysteria [something that is thankfully long over now], and so it's easy for things to get out of hand.The White Wolf WoD line was, in many ways, the beginning of the end of that era. It went too far on more than one occasion, but it got the hobby on a road to recognizing that the audience includes a lot of adults, and that sex, violence, religion, and other sensitive topics shouldn't be taboo in RPGs. Putting a Muslim terrorist, who uses their version of their religion as a weapon, in an action RPG doesn't mean you think all Muslims are terrorists [they aren't]; putting a female character who uses sex as a weapon in an RPG doesn't/shouldn't mean you see all women in a negative light. The problem is a lack of balance, in ALL forms of media.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a question of convincing game designers, writers, and artists to care about treating all of these topics and people with <i><b>respect</b></i> -- something they should be doing anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T12:38:04-07:00","id":671205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671114#post671114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is parading around topless even a good idea for a seductress or a prostitute?<br /> I've generally been under the belief that nudity very quickly loses its allure when it's present constantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely. There's a reason most alluring magazine covers and stuff are lingerie. <i>Almost </i>everything being revealed seems to be a more potent attractor than everything being revealed, according to market trends and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T13:31:17-07:00","id":671239,"title":"","content":"If presented all the time, it would lose its effectiveness. How common is nudity in Creation?<br /> On the other hand, if a group of adventurers found a lone female in next to no clothing, would it have the effect of surprising them long enough to give her the upper hand?<br /> And do the Abyssal Lords represent concepts of their associated sin, or are they Exalted people with powers? Because if the former is the truth, then she might show herself as the idealized concept of a courtesan, not worrying about logic or propriety.<br /> But YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T13:47:36-07:00","id":671269,"title":"","content":"It also depends on the culture! If you show your breasts in a southeastern jungle where all the women go topless all the time, nobody will care or feel aroused, because their culture won't consider breasts erotic. (Though you can maybe make yourself look younger than you really are if your breasts are firm from a lifetime of wearing tailored cup bras, and the jungle women your age are all saggy from never wearing them.)<br /> <br /> Conversely, some cultures consider a woman's hair, or ankles, or other body parts erotic.<br /> <br /> Presumably this also varies somewhat for how men are viewed. At least I would assume so, but I know of no real world examples.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I liked Wonderandawe's post in Hero Quest where Svante looked at porn for the first time and wondered why anyone would pay money for nude pictures (presumably hand-drawn, block-printed, or maybe lithographed) because naked gods roam the streets of Yu-Shan.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-19-2015, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T14:03:19-07:00","id":671288,"title":"","content":"Exactly - from the perspective of the fictionalized world of Creation, the appearance of the character may be normal, boring, shocking, or amusing, depending on the culture involved. I guess that what this proves is that the pictures were drawn, and are being interpreted, by people from a Western culture in the real world, and every interpretation we make is filtered through that. Officially, I don't think it's necessary to have nudity in the books, unless it involves both genders in a non-discriminatory way. The background of the Abyssal Lord in question doesn't seem to be pushing as many buttons - maybe she just needs a makeover? There must be a good PR firm in the Abyss! :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T14:04:33-07:00","id":671289,"title":"","content":"In the BBC documentary Human Planet, there was this tribe where the men were basically naked and the woman were topless and wore grass skirts. Yet, they had the men climb up into the new tree house first so the men couldn't look up the woman's skirts as they climbed. <br /> <br /> ((In Hero, the God and Goddess of nudity are this middle aged overweight couple. Because they believe nudity should not be limited just to beautiful people. Nor restricted by gender.))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":".  Auto correct fail 09-19-2015, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T15:29:22-07:00","id":671361,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to say that everybody is going to be like Mad Max, who sees a nude person in a cage and immediately thinks &quot;obvious trap&quot;, but it's the ideal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T15:43:48-07:00","id":671370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">is parading around topless even a good idea for a seductress or a prostitute?</div> </div> </div> </div> For somebody working in a brothel? I'd say it can be; a display for the clientele and cultivating a sense of comfort and openness. For somebody attempting seduction, I would say it works when it's a bit aggressive or unexpected, something that renders somebody sheepish and only partially evasive (like that kind of evasion that keeps trying not to look despite kind of wanting to), like calling somebody to your residence and being undressed when they arrive, or bringing them before you while you're in the middle of something you very pointedly don't desist from. That all depends on how you sell it, a combination of posturing and being casual enough to keep drawing their attention in that way that has them catch themselves and turn away when they're reminded. It's still based on harnessing the taboo, and it would need to be targeted at the kind of person who <i>could</i> be so embarressed (I wouldn't say it would work on somebody jaded and familiar). It can also be a gamble even with a suitable target; being teased can easily transition to being guarded. This is all rooted in more context than &quot;bunch of assassins enter her room and she's just kind of standing around with her weird get up&quot; (seriously, you could do a fair bit to redeem that comic by just having another person having been in the room with her).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:15:26-07:00","id":671507,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion that the Lady in Bloodstained Robes' skimpy attire has less (soley) to do with being seductive and more to do with her being an utterly shameless attention whore.<br /> Irrespective, she probably relies more upon her Charms than her looks to ensnare and manipulate those around her.<br /> <br /> Though to get back on topic, is she the only loyalist abyssal that people have trouble taking seriously?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6615,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6615-swazzle","user":"Swazzle","date":".  Poorly worded sentence 09-20-2015, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6615-swazzle","name":"Swazzle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:29:10-07:00","id":671523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671114#post671114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is parading around topless even a good idea for a seductress or a prostitute?<br /> I've generally been under the belief that nudity very quickly loses its allure when it's present constantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, if the science of prolonged exposure has anything to say about it. The question, though, is how long anyone actually spends in a room, looking at Lady of Darkness, in any given outfit<br /> {including nigh-there chain<i>shirt</i><br /> ------{I'm tired of using the phrase 'chaintits', though I understand chainshirt is a bit of a stretch here}<br /> }<br /> in sufficient lighting, with, over the course of, say, three months. My guess is, at best, 2 hours tops, in a mirror-comunnicae(Necromancy spell) for a team boardmeeting, +/- three to four hours monthly low-light condiitions (do any of them 'leave the lights on' during encounters?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 09-19-2015, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:52:11-07:00","id":671540,"title":"","content":"On that note, is anyone else annoyed that one of the Lady of Darkness' biggest established character traits (hates Maiden of the Mirthless Smile) is <i>told</i> to us, not shown to us?<br /> <br /> I get that some of us aren't on-board with the trait in the first place, because it's annoying that such a shallow trait is one of her <i>only</i> traits, but I'm just as bugged by the fact that we never seem to <i>see </i>it. Have Lady and Maiden ever even been in the same room? The only place I can recall seeing the two together is on the cover of Manual: Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T18:09:08-07:00","id":671564,"title":"","content":"Barring chapter fictions, I don't think RPGs are exactly the best medium for showing their own (non-player) characters. Still, to answer your question, they interact in the Abyssal chapter comic for Scroll of Exalts; the Lady cattily points out that the Maiden reeks after her foray into the sewers, and the Maiden shoots back by saying that she brought her quarry back alive for the Lady to finish so that she wouldn't feel completely useless. It's a bit of a shame, I could easily see the exact same dialogue as being the playful banter of slightly caustic friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T18:18:00-07:00","id":671569,"title":"","content":"If I were to play a Loyalist Abyssal, I'd probably go more subtle.<br /> <br /> You ever sat in a room by yourself after a busy day? Everyone was running around, it was loud and demanding, and you could never get anything done? Then you get home, crack a beer/soft drink/coffee, and just...sit. Enjoying the peace, the silence.<br /> <br /> Then someone gets home, or a car backfires, or the phone rings, and the peace is shattered. And even if the silence returns, it's been broken.<br /> <br /> Obvious parallels are obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T18:41:12-07:00","id":671589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671564#post671564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barring chapter fictions, I don't think RPGs are exactly the best medium for showing their own (non-player) characters. Still, to answer your question, they interact in the Abyssal chapter comic for Scroll of Exalts; the Lady cattily points out that the Maiden reeks after her foray into the sewers, and the Maiden shoots back by saying that she brought her quarry back alive for the Lady to finish so that she wouldn't feel completely useless. It's a bit of a shame, I could easily see the exact same dialogue as being the playful banter of slightly caustic friends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops, I missed that one.<br /> <br /> And yes, one more reason Exalted needed to go back to the chapter fictions for the third edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T19:18:12-07:00","id":671599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Swazzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671507#post671507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though to get back on topic, is she the only loyalist abyssal that people have trouble taking seriously?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Maiden can fuck people up with her big ass Sword. Disciple can actually land a hit on Harmonious Jade. Seven-Degreed Physician knows how to make Rhino Tanks and maintains the frigging Juggernaut.<br /> <br /> Even if there are silly aspects to their character, they're characters you wouldn't take the piss out of it you were stuck in a room with. Including the Lady. Midnight Charms have some serious shit going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T19:50:20-07:00","id":671620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Swazzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671507#post671507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though to get back on topic, is she the only loyalist abyssal that people have trouble taking seriously?</div> </div> </div> </div>MotMS's fingerbone corset/bra kinda ruin it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671599#post671599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maiden can fuck people up with her big ass Sword. Disciple can actually land a hit on Harmonious Jade. Seven-Degreed Physician knows how to make Rhino Tanks and maintains the frigging Juggernaut.<br /> <br /> Even if there are silly aspects to their character, they're characters you wouldn't take the piss out of it you were stuck in a room with. Including the Lady. Midnight Charms have some serious shit going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah all this is well and good from an IC perspective, the &quot;are they goofy or stereotypical or offensive&quot; is more of an OOC thing/issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 09-19-2015, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T19:51:18-07:00","id":671621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671540#post671540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have Lady and Maiden ever even been in the same room? The only place I can recall seeing the two together is on the cover of Manual: Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take this as a sign of how signature characters have been mishandled in Exalted.<br /> <br /> We don't <b>need</b> a signature character to show us what the deal is with a Dusk Caste because that's pretty fucking obvious but an iconic Dusk Caste who functions as part of a group with the Midnight, Daybreak, Moonshadow and Day brings something to the table that shrugging your shoulders and going &quot;you've seen a slasher movie haven't you?&quot; doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-19-2015, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T20:02:46-07:00","id":671624,"title":"","content":"I remember goth Legolas, who seemed okay. The ambiguously gendered poet one with the long veil and hammer, who I thought was neat. And the signature Dusk one, who I think of as a more blood thirsty Harley Quinn.<br /> <br /> As someone who doesn't get into sig characters (I had to look up the one we've been talking about), I find the rest of the Abyssal sigs fine.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T01:48:31-07:00","id":671727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if there are silly aspects to their character, they're characters you wouldn't take the piss out of it you were stuck in a room with.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are ways to make something like this work with a character, like Jayne Cobb and his cunning hat, but to simply trot it out as a sweeping response to criticism is right down there with &quot;maybe she doesn't like the feel of wool or cotton or stuff&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T02:02:59-07:00","id":671730,"title":"","content":"Something else I think this thread has emphasized is how it would be useful to present Abyssals in terms that don't wind up falling into neat categories, not least because trying to think of terms to answer Jen's question is difficult when he's complaining about three different things that are only semi-related. Same with Infernals; to be able to associate or not associate with their patrons in terms complex enough to not be drawn in simplistic battle lines as though there's some kind of bipartisan political dispute going on down there. Then you can answer the multifaceted question of &quot;how do you take seriously an Abyssal who is personally loyal to a Deathlord/willingly takes part in their network/shares some of the belief systems regarding the nature of death and Solars/adopts some of the classical motifs of the Underworld&quot; by just making a strong presentation of those things that would feel organically compelling to different individuals without being necessarily associated with one another or being observed in terms of big categories. Much like the Realm, both in terms of Dynasts liking it for reasons that aren't evil but also aren't sanitized for the comfort of the modern player, and how the way the whole thing is breaking down is multifaceted in a manner that doesn't fall into straightforward categories; I don't think I've ever seen somebody talk about Loyalist Dynasts, even if that would be a case in which it would actually be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T02:49:38-07:00","id":671742,"title":"","content":"Well I suppose the issue is that an Imperialist with a caste-based religion is a lot more complex and nuanced than a champion of &quot;let's kill everything&quot; in black armour, so allows multiple interpretations and sympathetic traits.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the Abyssals need to be linked by a more complex philosophy/milieu, to give them multiple motivations. Now, this was sort of attempted before &quot;he wants to kill everyone to stop their suffering&quot;, but it never felt very believable.<br /> The only ones I felt worked well were the Bodhisattva's nationalism+eternal life, and the Bishop's claim to be leading Creation to nirvana/heaven, where oblivion is bliss. \u200bThe issue is that because of the way Deathknights were recruited, it was a little difficult to play, say, a Deathknight who wants to defend Skullstone from Coral pirates and save people from being forced to reincarnate, because he absolutely had to be all about ending the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T03:53:07-07:00","id":671797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671599#post671599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if there are silly aspects to their character, they're characters you wouldn't take the piss out of it you were stuck in a room with. Including the Lady.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure.<br /> Back on the previous forums I remember a thread asking about how people had used signature characters in their games and I really disliked how much open sneering there was. I'm pretty sure people did call The Lady of Darkness a whore to her face and hid behind a perfect defence and insurmountable DV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T04:02:40-07:00","id":671800,"title":"","content":"Do people use signature characters much?<br /> <br /> I used Harmonious Jade once when the PCs were in Nexus (the Guild hired her to steal from the PCs to try to get them to back off), but that's it.<br /> I've never really seen people use the signature characters, with the one exception of the Dragonblood sigs (who hold important positions in the Realm, so are sort of inevitable).<br /> <br /> Mostly, to me, the sigs are there to show people what kind of characters they can expect to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-20-2015, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T04:52:15-07:00","id":671818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people use signature characters much?</div> </div> </div> </div>(raises hand)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T05:36:28-07:00","id":671829,"title":"","content":"This isn't an accusation. I'm just wandering what you (or others) use them for specifically.<br /> <br /> By sig characters I mean the ones on the front of the book. I've used a few of the characters from the Caste books as well.<br /> I have used Ophilis Ses a bit, because I think he's an interesting antagonist... though the PCs didn't really come into conflict with him. Actually one of the PCs made a wedding ring for his boyfriend (Azure Path) to propose to him with.<br /> We've also used Lyta and Havesh (though Havesh was in disguise). I used that Haltan Dawn briefly, though she'd become a Warrior-Queen. One of the players quit and his PC married her while the other PCs left the Hundred Kingdoms.<br /> <br /> Though, in retrospect, I decided I'd used too many Solars from the books. It detracted from the idea that Solars are very rare, and most are hidden and inexperienced.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T06:30:20-07:00","id":671857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I suppose the issue is that an Imperialist with a caste-based religion is a lot more complex and nuanced than a champion of &quot;let's kill everything&quot; in black armour, so allows multiple interpretations and sympathetic traits. Essentially, the Abyssals need to be linked by a more complex philosophy/milieu, to give them multiple motivations.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes that's certainly the precise thing that I said. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;he wants to kill everyone to stop their suffering&quot;, but it never felt very believable</div> </div> </div> </div> I can see Abyssals and the Underworld including a thing of life being suffering when compared to the experience of Oblivion or even just the power and luxury that can be afforded to ghosts. To actually kill people for this is something I see as crude. Honestly, I could do without revising Abyssals in terms of some overall purpose regardless of what it might be, some dubious and convoluted argument in favour of active destruction; I'm more interested in matters of perspective and experience, closer to the Solars. To whit: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">he absolutely had to be all about ending the world</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually would like Abyssals to still be a thesis on doom for the world, just without any need for mass murderers or Earth-shattering kabooms or anything so simplistic and ornery. To have it feel like something that might organically emerge from the powers or attitudes of them in terms that are subtle enough to warrent immediate response or indicative of a cartoonishly villainous character. To not be generic doomsday villains but heralds of the grave. And also just a bit of obtuseness and projection on the part of the Deathlords (between several things that John has said, I like this image of the Deathlords as figures who had their lives taken and so despise the living, and erroneously assume that if somebody loses their life and surrenders their name and destiny in order to become a herald of the grave, they must hate the living as well, combined with a bit of self-loathing and appropriation in the idea of &quot;of <i>course</i> Solars would bring about the end of the world&quot;). Things that can feel like distinguishing aspects of the Abyssal without feeling like manacles for character concepts or actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T07:08:20-07:00","id":671873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671800#post671800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people use signature characters much?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, for me their sole utility is in providing some archetypes for new players to understand the varied backgrounds that Solars can come from.<br /> <br /> I have more character ideas than I would be able to play through a thousand years of games; many of them can easily slot into an NPC role as-needed, though I agree that &quot;your Circle of Solars meets this random Solar this week, and that random Solar next week,&quot; detracts from the notion that there are 150 Solars and tens or hundreds of millions of people in Creation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I specifically mean Solar sigs. I've gotten use out of DB, Lunar, and Sid, probably because I think they're all more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 09-20-2015, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T09:06:44-07:00","id":672059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671800#post671800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people use signature characters much?</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly have. I've used quite a few of the NPC's in the gameline over the years. All of the Dragon Blooded signature characters (Mnemon, Tepet Arada, the Roseblack, etc) have all played huge roles in my campaigns. Signature characters from other splat books might crop up depending on where the PC's are and the needs of a particular story.<br /> <br /> I'm not shy about including pre-generated NPCs in the games, especially if the players find some of them to be kind of cool. My players would read the Aspect or Caste books, and then I'd include some of those NPC's in my games, simply because the players already have a good understand of many things about those NPCs (that characters history, desires, goals, regrets, etc) so that character comes off as more rounded and memorable in our games than if I had introduced an entirely new character (which I certainly do, but sometimes it's nice to drop one of those pre-made characters as a cameo or such). <br /> <br /> Ultimately I view the signature characters as no different from any other NPC - they just happen to have a bit more spotlight in the artwork than the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T10:33:43-07:00","id":672192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671800#post671800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people use signature characters much?</div> </div> </div> </div>For when newbie players need good pre-gen characters, sure.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T10:38:52-07:00","id":672205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671797#post671797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so sure.<br /> Back on the previous forums I remember a thread asking about how people had used signature characters in their games and I really disliked how much open sneering there was. I'm pretty sure people did call The Lady of Darkness a whore to her face and<i> <b>hid behind a perfect defence and insurmountable DV.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, I'd say their actions are speaking a hell of a lot louder than their words.<br /> <br /> Talk is Cheap. PD's cost motes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T12:09:56-07:00","id":672266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=672192#post672192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For when newbie players need good pre-gen characters, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd require the sig characters to be good for pregen purposes :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T12:12:49-07:00","id":672270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=672205#post672205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, I'd say their actions are speaking a hell of a lot louder than their words.<br /> <br /> Talk is Cheap. PD's cost motes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why? That's what they'd use against an actual credible opponent. They don't need to blindfold themselves or completely forgo the use of essence to demonstrate their superiority and attempting to do so would probably make the NPC in question look far worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-20-2015, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:27:29-07:00","id":672334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, I'd say their actions are speaking a hell of a lot louder than their words.</div> </div> </div> </div> So a person using their powers to defend against the consequences of their trash talk lacks credibility, but a person using their powers to be taken seriously as a danger despite looking ridiculous is the most impressive figure in the world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:51:25-07:00","id":672346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671800#post671800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people use signature characters much?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the time.<br /> <br /> Arianna, from the 2E Signature circle, was kind of an experiment for me, in that I wanted to make her a rounded character rather than a stereotype. The end result had her wind up lovers with one of the PCs, resulting in lots of interpersonal shenanigans that are a lot of fun, given said Zenith is more of a free-love type, while Arianna's self-worth issues from growing up mean she's moderately threatened every time her lover flirts with another woman.<br /> <br /> They ran into a <i>lot</i> of the DB signatures, and Mnemon has pretty much been a recurring NPC companion to the party (though due to the fact this is a Shard setting with no Realm, she's a bit less Cersei Lannister and a bit more 'socially awkward genius sorceress'). Due to the circumstances of the shard, the DB House Founders are still around, and they've met Cynis, V'neef, and Ledaal while staying with the Blood Red Jade (this Shard's version of Her Redness)<br /> <br /> A few Alchemical sigs showed up in Gem when they broke through, dethroned the Despot, and started turning it into essentially Autochthonia's first Creation-based colony.<br /> <br /> Gyrfalcon from Infernals hasn't actually had his Exaltation yet, but has been a recurring means of transportation for the PCs. When he does Exalt, that'll be fun. Sulumor traded in her hellnun gear for something more practical, and helped our PCs dethrone the corrupt Censor of the South via wish-granting, alongside Basphomy, the iconic not-Slayer that showed up in the Infernal preview.<br /> <br /> There's been some mention of the Lunar elders, but the only ones the PCs have run into have been Anja Silverclaws and Ma Ha Suchi, who the PCs do not know is Ma Ha Suchi, because he was shapeshifted at the time and pretending to be someone else.<br /> <br /> Also, two of the PCs are from Lookshy noble houses, so they're on speaking terms both with Karal Linwei and Karal Fire Orchid.<br /> <br /> So yeah, sig characters are always fun to use for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T18:29:12-07:00","id":672638,"title":"","content":"The reason I asked, was that I wondered how important it is for the characters on the front of the books to have well-rounded backgrounds, rather than just look inspiring.<br /> <br /> It came out of a conversa\u200btion I had with one of my players a while ago: I said I didn't like the characters on the front of the Core because they're too stereotypical and their backgrounds are rather dull and clich\u00e9d. There were more interesting (and, frankly, likeable) Solars in the Caste books they could have used instead. It also encourages people to make very stereotypical characters.<br /> He argued that's good: their purpose isn't actually to be an interesting character, it's to give new players (whether that be new players of the game, or new players of that splat) an immediate idea of what Solars are and what each caste represents. You look at Dace, and you know that a Dawn is some kind of fighter. You look at Harmonious Jade sneaking and jumping around in the comics, and you know that Nights are good at Athletics and Stealth.<br /> <br /> This is why I was asking about the sig characters themselves (as in the ones on the front of the books), rather than canon NPCs generally. Do people actually use them in their games, or not. Do they need to have good and interesting backgrounds, or just look inspiring.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T19:06:04-07:00","id":672719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do people actually use them in their games, or not. Do they need to have good and interesting backgrounds, or just look inspiring </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Well...I don't use most of them, but that is <i>because </i>I don't find most of them interesting. if they were (and &quot;interesting&quot; here is a combination of visual design, background, personality, deeds) I would use them more often. That said, I consider the primary function of signature characters to be as illustrations of somewhat typical character types possible, or reflecting something about that character type in the setting (you could have a sorcerer in massive armor, for instance, which is unusual in many other fantasy settings).<br /> <br /> From what is known about the new Sigs so far, I'd say they are likely to succeed at being interesting, both as characters in general and in visual designs, as well as serving their purpose as Signatures illustrating things about the characters in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T19:24:02-07:00","id":672741,"title":"","content":"I found their backgrounds more interesting than their looks really, which didn't excite me (I liked Volfer, though his sword is a little ludicrous). But their backgrounds had some depth to them (more than just &quot;I'm a commander&quot;, &quot;I'm a diplomat&quot;, &quot;I'm a librarian&quot;. HJ and Panther had decent backgrounds though.<br /> But they do look like that caste: Shin clearly looks like a Twilight, the girl whose name I forgot looks like a Night, Volfer is clearly a Dawn, etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T20:21:53-07:00","id":672801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=672270#post672270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why? That's what they'd use against an actual credible opponent. They don't need to blindfold themselves or completely forgo the use of essence to demonstrate their superiority and attempting to do so would probably make the NPC in question look far worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but if they didn't acknowledge her as a credible adversary on some level, they wouldn't activate that scenelong to keep themselves from getting their faces screamed off.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't quite call it respect of course, but its at least <i>acknowledgment </i>of the peril of their current situation. Though, I'll admit there are other ways to interpret it..<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/JamesArmsLength.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T20:32:44-07:00","id":672828,"title":"","content":"I don't think I've ever read the setting sections of the core book. I do read the write-ups for signature characters I like though, and that tends to be what informs me about the setting.<br /> <br /> The signature characters, like most NPCs, teach me about the world they live in and the cultures and orginizations that define them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T21:51:50-07:00","id":672883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=671800#post671800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people use signature characters much?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see the Maiden of the Mirthless Smile feature constantly, but that's pretty much it. Oh! Manosque Cyan got a huge facelift in a high-power game I'm in and is basically De Facto Queen of Infernals What Care About Creation (they have a more or less de jure king, who is the first Infernal, but he basically only cares about Malfeas any more). Never seen sigs as good guys, ever.<br /> <br /> Honestly, you can't really take loyalist abyssals very seriously so long as you adhere to the following assumptions (as laid out in the books):<br /> <br /> 1. Abyssal endgame is blowing up the space station after blowing up the escape pods, followed by the sun<br /> 2. They all know this<br /> 3. They're all on board<br /> <br /> Just changing 2 and 3 just gets us the Loyal Infernal Problem (where a loyalist is just someone who hasn't been screwed over enough yet), so, I figure it's on us to make a better endgame. There are people in the real world who are pretty stoked about the idea of the world ending, but there are a lot of assumptions that go along with it (like &quot;get a better world in its place&quot; and &quot;everyone I don't like will finally get theirs&quot;). SO.<br /> <br /> Idea 1. Broken Windows, Cosmic-Tier<br /> <br /> People will cling to a corrupt system to have any sort of system at all. Start tearing it down and you'll be amazed at what solutions they'll come up with!<br /> Oblivion exists as written. Creation is a shithole. Abyssals and Deathlords are privy to some First Age secrets and the existence of their kin Exalted Solars and Infernals, who are both possessed of the ability to create worlds. Rather like a surge in interest in coastal engineering when the storms start getting more intense, serious threats to the stability (and continued existence) of Creation are liable to start the Powers That Be looking into that much more seriously. Heck, a sufficient amount of access fae shenanigans (and the connections between faerie and Guild) means that even mortals could make it happen. A meschlum-esque Road Into Forever sounds <i>crazy</i> when the world isn't under threat or when the worst threat anyone faces is just another conqueror.<br /> <br /> They're deathknights. Making things better by providing the best opposition is what they do, right?<br /> <br /> Idea 2. I'm a Final Fantasy villain. Good thing it means I get such nice hair.<br /> <br /> Oblivion's whispers drive ghosts mad. That's pretty much a given. People have been trying to interpret the ramblings of nephwracks for ages without much success. However, none of them were necromantic geniuses who had the benefit of actually being alive, capable of holding the raw data-stuff of Oblivion in their minds (ghosts are excessively self-referential, and will get stuck in recursions, becoming trapped in an endless programming loop; &quot;going mad&quot; is just a side effect). Abyssals, when they try, actually get real patterns and programming instructions (that manifest themselves as superpowers or the ability to turn into a swarm of bats or kung fu, but what are you going to do). Oblivion isn't so much alive as it is the precursor to something that intends to 'be.' A human would probably classify it as a primordial but it is to a Primordial what a Primordial is to a human.<br /> <br /> If allowed to escape/manifest/ascend/be born it will consume the remnants of its former kin. It will consume universes (the infinite worlds of the Yozi) and herald a new era of darkness - but one in which it's liable to be pretty damn sweet to be its avatar. The influence that it has on the world defies description; cults pop up seemingly out of nowhere. It has prophets and actual, real prophecy due to living 'outside' the normal flow of being. It is the closest thing that the Exalted universe has or will have to a proper God. (Too bad that having been suckled on the suffering of living universes and born by eating them, it's probably evil.)<br /> <br /> (Obligatory HE IS ALREADY HERE)<br /> <br /> Meanwhile they also need to help the Infernals hellscape enough of Creation that the entrance to Malfeas is &quot;wide&quot; enough for a newborn void-god to get in and eat the Yozis, too. (The Yozis, meanthile, support the Abyssals because they think some prominent Abyssal successes will let them offer the gods a devil's bargain - put us back in charge and we'll stop the destruction of everything; refuse and you and everything you care about will get oblivion'd.)<br /> <br /> Idea 3. Sometimes you gotta tell the world &quot;get out of the way,&quot; this time it was a little more literal<br /> <br /> Similar to 2, except that inside the black hole is an infinite universe compressed into a single point through denial of the concept of &quot;distance.&quot; (Like a protoshinmaic vortex, but times a billion.) The Abyssals' powers are derived not from death but from <i>entropy</i>; dust, death, decay, degradation (and free cosmic power to the first one that figures it out). It could unpack into a brand new universe, except that Creation is quite literally, quite physically and metaphysically &quot;in the way.&quot; Like a dam, they need to crack it enough to get it to bust, but the old thing is remarkably well-built! Through their Fetters, the Neverborn are some of the most effective tethers that it has, whether they know it or not. They want to join with the new universe, but what they really need to do is get flung off into the Wyld somewhere so they'll stop keeping Creation intact so well!<br /> <br /> What happens when the point is allowed to expand? Well, they might call that a &quot;big bang?&quot; At which point the Abyssals emerge from their perfect defenses and step out to become gods of their new world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 09-21-2015, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T04:55:50-07:00","id":675118,"title":"","content":"I find that the signature characters make a good reference point for a game that began in vanilla Creation and you want to give a potential new player an idea of what's changed globally.<br /> <br /> Edit: I once tried to join a long-running game where the ST told me all about the players and major NPCs and I figured I had enough to go on. So I made a member of a character who had some relation to the Guild only to be told that the PCs had casually destroyed the Guild while they were in Nexus. I ended up with a sense of continuity lockout and ultimately didn't join the game, but I think I learned how to keep my own games more accessible from that experience.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-23-2015, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:24:19-07:00","id":675668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=672883#post672883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, you can't really take loyalist abyssals very seriously so long as you adhere to the following assumptions (as laid out in the books):<br /> <br /> 1. Abyssal endgame is blowing up the space station after blowing up the escape pods, followed by the sun<br /> 2. They all know this<br /> 3. They're all on board<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Can't there just be Abyssals who look at the world and see it as a horse with a busted leg?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:32:46-07:00","id":675676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=675668#post675668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't there just be Abyssals who look at the world and see it as a horse with a busted leg?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would need an entirely new portrayal of Abyssals... which we seem to be getting, luckily.<br /> As-is in 2ed, any Loyalist Abyssal literally wants to end the world. Any Abyssal who just wants to fix it (outside of &quot;Old Yeller Style&quot;) wouldn't be a loyalist.<br /> <br /> That being said, from what I've heard, in 3ed, Deathlords are more self-absorbed and distracted than 2ed's, and more focussed on <i>conquering</i> the world first. Abyssals are probably more effective, but still more focussed on &quot;Conquering and ruling the Underworld and Creation&quot; - any potential world-destruction either happens afterwards, and/or as an &quot;unintentional&quot; side effect of having powerful death-monsters rule the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:14:53-07:00","id":675693,"title":"","content":"Amakawa, &quot;Old Yeller Style&quot; is pretty much the only way to deal with a Horse that broke their leg. Their legs, don't break the way ours does, they shatter, rendering the horse crippled and in <i>constant agony </i>for the remainder of their lives. So much pain that the pain itself will probably kill them, albeit much slower. So, the only way to spare them that pain, that suffering, is to end their lives as cleanly and gently as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:29:35-07:00","id":675701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=675676#post675676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would need an entirely new portrayal of Abyssals... which we seem to be getting, luckily.<br /> As-is in 2ed, any Loyalist Abyssal literally wants to end the world. Any Abyssal who just wants to fix it (outside of &quot;Old Yeller Style&quot;) wouldn't be a loyalist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, I think you missed the point of the post you were replying to. You (almost) have to euthanize a horse with a broken limb due to a combination of cost (which is...less applicable in this metaphor) and the fact that the horse goes into shock pretty much immediately, which makes treatment difficult at best (hence the metaphor drawn above), and frequently pointless, because surgery, again, makes the horse go into shock. Horses are fragile.<br /> <br /> (Relevant sidenote: humans are absurdly resistant to injury-induced shock and the like. Other mammals, particularly herbivores, not so much. Well, other than cattle.)<br /> <br /> Ed: Uh, ninja'd, but I guess I had additional input, so I'll leave this here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":58,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","user":"Lokisenna","date":". 09-23-2015, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T05:53:57-07:00","id":676330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=668888#post668888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll agree with you there. Isn't Iron Siaka a sucker for a cute face too, though? Or is that just my misinterpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>She's a lesbian, though, so that's okay.<br /> <br /> No, really.<br /> <br /> Note the talk about sexuality, even in this thread, and think of all the female characters in Exalted. There are those who have sex because they enjoy it, and those who use it as a weapon (Raksi as the former, Rafara as the latter, The Empress and The Lover being noted for both), and those who are in committed relationships with men they love... and there are absolutely no instances of a female character that sees men the way Siaka sees women. As you said, she 'is a sucker for a pretty face'. She is not having sex 'because she enjoys it', she finds girls attractive, woos them, and enjoys her time with them. For most other characters, though, that connection is absent; they seem to either value the male genitalia in abstract, their own pleasure, or be in a committed relationship built on entirely non-sexual impulses, but you don't see someone intent on 'that guy is a hunk, I want to have him and break the bed with him.' Not a single one.<br /> <br /> That kind of creeps me out, to be honest. And I'm someone who doesn't mind the Lady's outfit in the slightest.<br /> <br /> In fact, you also won't see this attitude in Exalted's men, either; they are oddly, eerily sexless, compared to the female characters.<br /> <br /> (The sad part? Exalted is just about the BEST RPG I've read on that topic. This complaint may well apply to most media, and certainly most RPGs.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 09-24-2015, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T06:12:21-07:00","id":676339,"title":"","content":"@TV Head and Lokisenna:<br /> ...yeah, I missed the &quot;horse&quot; bit. I just read &quot;busted leg&quot;. Which is weird, because I remember thinking &quot;maybe I should mention that if it was a horse with a broken leg, it would kinda make sense, but I don't want to make it complicated&quot;...<br /> ...damn that's embarrassing. And no Avoidance Kata after a full day!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T10:09:45-07:00","id":676533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=676330#post676330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's a lesbian, though, so that's okay.<br /> <br /> No, really.<br /> <br /> Note the talk about sexuality, even in this thread, and think of all the female characters in Exalted. There are those who have sex because they enjoy it, and those who use it as a weapon (Raksi as the former, Rafara as the latter, The Empress and The Lover being noted for both), and those who are in committed relationships with men they love... and there are absolutely no instances of a female character that sees men the way Siaka sees women. As you said, she 'is a sucker for a pretty face'. She is not having sex 'because she enjoys it', she finds girls attractive, woos them, and enjoys her time with them. For most other characters, though, that connection is absent; they seem to either value the male genitalia in abstract, their own pleasure, or be in a committed relationship built on entirely non-sexual impulses, but you don't see someone intent on 'that guy is a hunk, I want to have him and break the bed with him.' Not a single one.<br /> <br /> That kind of creeps me out, to be honest. And I'm someone who doesn't mind the Lady's outfit in the slightest.<br /> <br /> In fact, you also won't see this attitude in Exalted's men, either; they are oddly, eerily sexless, compared to the female characters.<br /> <br /> (The sad part? Exalted is just about the BEST RPG I've read on that topic. This complaint may well apply to most media, and certainly most RPGs.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So are you saying Iron Siaka's portrayal is particularly problematic, or that she's depicted well and more characters should approach sexuality like she does?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T11:05:25-07:00","id":676565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=676330#post676330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, you also won't see this attitude in Exalted's men, either; they are oddly, eerily sexless, compared to the female characters.<br /> <br /> (The sad part? Exalted is just about the BEST RPG I've read on that topic. This complaint may well apply to most media, and certainly most RPGs.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It was one of the big changes between 1st and 2nd edition where sex started to become something the gameline didn't want to discuss quite as much.<br /> <br /> If you get the chance you might want to read the old Aspect and Caste books. Back then the gameline absolutely wasn't afraid of exploring a character's (both male and female) sexuality and individual attitudes towards sex and romance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T11:54:01-07:00","id":676639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=676330#post676330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note the talk about sexuality, even in this thread, and think of all the female characters in Exalted. There are those who have sex because they enjoy it, and those who use it as a weapon (Raksi as the former, Rafara as the latter, The Empress and The Lover being noted for both), and those who are in committed relationships with men they love... and there are absolutely no instances of a female character that sees men the way Siaka sees women. As you said, she 'is a sucker for a pretty face'. She is not having sex 'because she enjoys it', she finds girls attractive, woos them, and enjoys her time with them. For most other characters, though, that connection is absent; they seem to either value the male genitalia in abstract, their own pleasure, or be in a committed relationship built on entirely non-sexual impulses, but you don't see someone intent on 'that guy is a hunk, I want to have him and break the bed with him.' Not a single one.<br /> <br /> That kind of creeps me out, to be honest. And I'm someone who doesn't mind the Lady's outfit in the slightest.<br /> <br /> In fact, you also won't see this attitude in Exalted's men, either; they are oddly, eerily sexless, compared to the female characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.... Not testing this idea by going through and reading the books, but thinking about who writes Exalted's characters, in about the only place where there is enough space for them to go into the character's romantic life, Aspect and Caste Books together look 1:2 female to male ratio in authors. For the particular authors, who crop up repeatedly, usually John Snead or Genevieve Cogman. <br /> <br /> I assume the authors for those are (were) just not very interested in their characters &quot;dating&quot;. (How interested am I in the dating life of Hercules? Really not very.) And maybe even dating generally. Not a view I'd see as creepy - a lot of the best people think of dating as horribly bloody hindering awkward unfortunate thing to get out of the way for the real &quot;meat&quot; they want of true intimacy, companionship and good sex. (If anything, the enthusiastic extroverted guys and girls who bank a third of their salary a month to dating, and spend their lives swiping right on Tinder, and like talking about dating as if it's *fun* are folks I'd be happier to describe as having a sort of &quot;creepy&quot; and strange view of life <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, maybe they did feel the need for their female characters to show they have sexual &quot;power&quot; or something? And that way some female sexuality crops up in a somewhat disembodied / disconnected context. I don't know though..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T14:19:23-07:00","id":676859,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=676533#post676533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are you saying Iron Siaka's portrayal is particularly problematic, or that she's depicted well and more characters should approach sexuality like she does?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Latter. Romance is a very natural human drive, and I like my Exalted human.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/665862-how-can-i-take-loyalist-abyssal-seriously-nsfw?p=676639#post676639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hmm.... Not testing this idea by going through and reading the books, but thinking about who writes Exalted's characters, in about the only place where there is enough space for them to go into the character's romantic life, Aspect and Caste Books together look 1:2 female to male ratio in authors. For the particular authors, who crop up repeatedly, usually John Snead or Genevieve Cogman.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I assume the authors for those are (were) just not very interested in their characters &quot;dating&quot;. (How interested am I in the dating life of Hercules? Really not very.) And maybe even dating generally. Not a view I'd see as creepy - a lot of the best people think of dating as horribly bloody hindering awkward unfortunate thing to get out of the way for the real &quot;meat&quot; they want of true intimacy, companionship and good sex. (If anything, the enthusiastic extroverted guys and girls who bank a third of their salary a month to dating, and spend their lives swiping right on Tinder, and like talking about dating as if it's *fun* are folks I'd be happier to describe as having a sort of &quot;creepy&quot; and strange view of life <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On the other hand, maybe they did feel the need for their female characters to show they have sexual &quot;power&quot; or something? And that way some female sexuality crops up in a somewhat disembodied / disconnected context. I don't know though..</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh, that wasn't a slam against the authors; and as I said, Exalted does the BEST with this topic. I mean, all the complaints about the Lady and the Maiden in this thread, it's worth remembering the Corebook had two women: a black woman with pants who's the best killer in the circle /and the character in the cover/, and also a flat-chested, not-particularly-attractive getting-to-middle-age woman. Oh, and the Roseblack and Lilith, who rock gender-neutral armor. I feel it is more of a blind spot than anything. I can see how a character that's interested in romance can be dismissed as shallow or problematic in hetero relationships [female characters coming across like 'they need a man', men coming across as mysoginistic if one of their first impulses seeing a pretty lady is 'I want to tap that'], but at the same time it feels like a natural possibility to me, and it's a bit disappointing that it ends up only being 'allowed' in a lesbian context.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T14:56:15-07:00","id":676875,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sure. With mentioning the authors, I wasn't so much thinking of what you said as a slam, so much as I just wanted to put the focus on the writers as the source of the characters. As we can get often more useful insights into why people write characters a certain way when looking at writers as people, rather than when we sometimes tend to see characterization as emanating from vague, impersonal sources like &quot;society&quot; or &quot;the Exalted gameline&quot; which are not people (as much as trends and contexts influence how people act and think and write).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:02:34-07:00","id":692531,"title":"","content":"I put the signature circle under Walker in Darkness as I\u2019d already fleshed out the Mask of Winters\u2019 Abyssals as a rogue\u2019s gallery of reoccurring antagonists for my PCs.<br /> <br /> My version of Mirth changed the most but hasn't had much screen time yet; she's loosely based on Jubal Early from Firefly in that she's got this air of professionalism hiding the fact that she's a sadist with a hair trigger-temper. The Lunar PC almost bit her in half which she survived but is only capable of walking thanks to an implant from the Physician.<br /> <br /> By extension Physician is someone you\u2019d actually trust to be your team\u2019s medic. He\u2019s still not a nice man but he\u2019d be quite horrified if people assumed he was no more than a talentless butcher with a knack for necromancy.<br /> <br /> Lady is still a seductress but dresses like she does on the MoEP cover and actually has dignity. There\u2019s more going on there but it\u2019s rather involved and incidental to her immediate presentation.<br /> <br /> Poet and Disciple haven\u2019t changed much. The most notable thing there was that Disciple surrendered to the PCs to prevent Mirth from getting bitten in two, was their prisoner for a time before they were ransomed back to the Walker in Darkness.<br /> <br /> Currently they\u2019re trying to stick together in the Walker\u2019s absence. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}